{"title":"SCC Generated CKLB at: 2026-09-05T13:07:40","id":"36881667-6BF8-1014-B373-B0104E0DF08C","stigs":[{"classification":"UNCLASSIFIED","rules":[{"stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","discussion":"Features such as Credential Guard use virtualization-based security to protect information that could be used in credential theft attacks if compromised. There are a number of system requirements that must be met in order for Credential Guard to be configured and enabled properly. Virtualization-based security and Credential Guard are only available with Windows 11 Enterprise 64-bit version.","mitigations":"","rule_title":"Domain-joined systems must use Windows 11 Enterprise Edition 64-bit version.","security_override_guidance":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253254"},"uuid":"366E6B72-6BF8-1014-879B-CB474629FCEA","status":"not_applicable","fix_text":"Use Windows 11 Enterprise 64-bit version for domain-joined systems.","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253254","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253254","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-253254"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253254r991589","check_content":"Verify domain-joined systems are using Windows 11 Enterprise Edition 64-bit version.\n\nFor standalone systems, this is NA.\n\nOpen \"Settings\".\n\nSelect \"System\", then \"About\".\n\nIf \"Edition\" is not \"Windows 11 Enterprise\", this is a finding.\n\nIf \"System type\" is not \"64-bit operating system...\", this is a finding.","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253254r991589_rule","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","severity":"medium","rule_version":"WN11-00-000005"},{"mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253255r1117271","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"check_content":"Verify domain-joined systems have a TPM enabled and ready for use.\n\nFor standalone systems, this is NA.\n\nVirtualization-based security, including Credential Guard, currently cannot be implemented in virtual desktop implementations (VDI) due to specific supporting requirements including a TPM, UEFI with Secure Boot, and the capability to run the Hyper-V feature within the virtual desktop.\n\nFor VDIs where the virtual desktop instance is deleted or refreshed upon logoff, this is NA.\n\nVerify the system has a TPM and is ready for use.\nRun \"tpm.msc\".\nReview the sections in the center pane.\n\"Status\" must indicate it has been configured with a message such as \"The TPM is ready for use\" or \"The TPM is on and ownership has been taken\".\nTPM Manufacturer Information - Specific Version = 2.0\n\nIf a TPM is not found or is not ready for use, this is a finding.","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253255r1117271_rule","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253255","title":"SRG-OS-000424-GPOS-00188"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","rule_version":"WN11-00-000010","ccis":["CCI-002421"],"group_title":"SRG-OS-000424-GPOS-00188","severity":"medium","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows 11 domain-joined systems must have a Trusted Platform Module (TPM) enabled.","discussion":"Credential Guard uses virtualization-based security to protect information that could be used in credential theft attacks if compromised. There are a number of system requirements that must be met in order for Credential Guard to be configured and enabled properly. Without a TPM enabled and ready for use, Credential Guard keys are stored in a less secure method using software.","mitigations":"","fix_text":"For standalone systems, this is NA.\n\nVirtualization-based security, including Credential Guard, currently cannot be implemented in virtual desktop implementations (VDI) due to specific supporting requirements including a TPM, UEFI with Secure Boot, and the capability to run the Hyper-V feature within the virtual desktop.\n\nFor VDIs where the virtual desktop instance is deleted or refreshed upon logoff, this is NA.\n\nEnsure domain-joined systems must have a TPM that is configured for use. (Versions 2.0 support Credential Guard.)\n\nThe TPM must be enabled in the firmware.\nRun \"tpm.msc\" for configuration options in Windows.","group_id":"V-253255","potential_impacts":"","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253255","uuid":"366E8C1F-6BF8-1014-82F3-B6DD86047788","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:253255","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml"},"status":"not_applicable"},{"rule_id_src":"SV-253256r1117271_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"For virtual desktop implementations (VDIs) where the virtual desktop instance is deleted or refreshed upon logoff, this is NA.\n\nVerify the system firmware is configured to run in UEFI mode, not Legacy BIOS.\n\nRun \"System Information\".\n\nUnder \"System Summary\", if \"BIOS Mode\" does not display \"UEFI\", this is a finding.","rule_id":"SV-253256r1117271","mitigation_control":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"id":"V-253256","title":"SRG-OS-000424-GPOS-00188"},"reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","rule_version":"WN11-00-000015","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000424-GPOS-00188","ccis":["CCI-002421"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Unified Extensible Firmware Interface (UEFI) firmware must exist and be configured to run in UEFI mode, not Legacy BIOS.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25325601 (cmdlet_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Unified Extensible Firmware Interface (UEFI) firmware must exist and be configured to run in UEFI mode, not Legacy BIOS.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : At least one collected item must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25325601 (cmdlet_object)\nObject Comment          : Secure Boot State Setting\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'module_name' must be equal to 'Microsoft.Powershell.Management'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'verb' must be equal to 'Get'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'noun' must be equal to 'ComputerInfo'\nObject Requirement      : for  'parameters' the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      : for  'select' the following must be true:\n                        : property must be equal to 'biosfirmwaretype'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25325601 (cmdlet_state)\nState Comment           : BIOS Firmware Type must be equal to UEFI\nState Requirement       : for all 'value' the following must be true:\n                        : all biosfirmwaretype must be equal (case insensitive) to 'UEFI'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : module_name equals 'Microsoft.PowerShell.Management'\n                        : module_id equals '{eefcb906-b326-4e99-9f54-8b4bb6ef3c6d}'\n                        : module_version equals '3.1.0.0'\n                        : verb equals 'Get'\n                        : noun equals 'ComputerInfo'\n                        : collected 'parameters' result: does not exist\n                        : collected 'select' result: \n                        : property = 'biosfirmwaretype'\n                        : collected 'value' result: \n                        : biosfirmwaretype = 'Uefi'\n","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows 11 systems must have Unified Extensible Firmware Interface (UEFI) firmware and be configured to run in UEFI mode, not Legacy BIOS.","mitigations":"","discussion":"UEFI provides additional security features in comparison to legacy BIOS firmware, including Secure Boot. UEFI is required to support additional security features in Windows 11, including virtualization-based Security and Credential Guard. Systems with UEFI that are operating in Legacy BIOS mode will not support these security features.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253256","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253256","fix_text":"Configure UEFI firmware to run in UEFI mode, not Legacy BIOS mode.","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"366E9FEC-6BF8-1014-83AF-C58CB4C38BF2","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:253256"}},{"status":"open","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:253257"},"uuid":"366EAE7A-6BF8-1014-A821-97F12F9FE743","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253257","group_id":"V-253257","potential_impacts":"","fix_text":"Enable Secure Boot in the system firmware.","mitigations":"","discussion":"Secure Boot is a standard that ensures systems boot only to a trusted operating system. Secure Boot is required to support additional security features in Windows 11, including virtualization-based Security and Credential Guard. If Secure Boot is turned off, these security features will not function.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Secure Boot must be enabled on Windows 11 systems.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Run a PowerShell command to determine if Secure Boot must be enabled.)\nResult Analysis         :        'False' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'True' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25325701 (shellcommand_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Run a PowerShell command to determine if Secure Boot must be enabled.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25325701 (shellcommand_object)\nObject Comment          : Run a PowerShell command to determine if secure boot is enabled\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'shell' must be equal to 'powershell'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'command' must be equal to 'Confirm-SecureBootUEFI'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25325701 (shellcommand_state)\nState Comment           : Verify True is returned to stdout\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'stdout_line' must be equal to 'True'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : shell equals 'powershell'\n                        : command equals 'Confirm-SecureBootUEFI'\n                        : pattern equals ''\n                        : exit_status equals ''\n                        : stdout_line equals 'False'\n\nResult Analysis         : 'False' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'True' \n","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000424-GPOS-00188","ccis":["CCI-002421"],"rule_version":"WN11-00-000020","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"id":"V-253257","title":"SRG-OS-000424-GPOS-00188"},"reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253257r1117271_rule","check_content":"Verify the system firmware is configured for Secure Boot.\n\nFor virtual desktop implementations (VDIs) where the virtual desktop instance is deleted or refreshed upon logoff, this is NA.\n\nRun \"System Information\".\n\nUnder \"System Summary\", if \"Secure Boot State\" does not display \"On\", this is a finding.","ia_controls":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id":"SV-253257r1117271","mitigation_control":""},{"fix_text":"Enable full disk encryption on all information systems (including SIPRNet) using BitLocker.\n\nBitLocker, included in Windows, can be enabled in the Control Panel under \"BitLocker Drive Encryption\" as well as other management tools.\n\nNote: An alternate encryption application may be used in lieu of BitLocker providing it is configured for full disk encryption and satisfies the pre-boot authentication requirements (WN11-00-000031 and WN11-00-000032).","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253259","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253259","uuid":"366EB84A-6BF8-1014-8A07-98C26D36A012","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253259","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"status":"open","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     false (BitLocker must be enabled on all fixed drives.)\nResult Analysis         :          protectionstatus = '0' failed test of 'equals' compared to '1' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25325900 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : BitLocker must be enabled on all fixed drives.\nCheck Existence         : All collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25325900 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : BitLocker status\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2\\security\\microsoftvolumeencryption'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT protectionstatus FROM win32_encryptablevolume'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25325900 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : BitLocker status is Protected\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all protectionstatus must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2\\security\\microsoftvolumeencryption'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT protectionstatus FROM win32_encryptablevolume'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : !![ protectionstatus = '0' ]!!\n\nResult Analysis         : protectionstatus = '0' failed test of 'equals' compared to '1' \n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows 11 information systems must use BitLocker to encrypt all disks to protect the confidentiality and integrity of all information at rest.","mitigations":"","discussion":"If data at rest is unencrypted, it is vulnerable to disclosure. Even if the operating system enforces permissions on data access, an adversary can remove non-volatile memory and read it directly, thereby circumventing operating system controls. Encrypting the data ensures that confidentiality is protected even when the operating system is not running.","rule_version":"WN11-00-000030","ccis":["CCI-002475"],"severity":"high","group_title":"SRG-OS-000404-GPOS-00183","rule_id":"SV-253259r958870","mitigation_control":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id_src":"SV-253259r958870_rule","check_content":"Verify all Windows 11 information systems (including SIPRNet) employ BitLocker for full disk encryption.\n\nFor virtual desktop implementations (VDIs) in which the virtual desktop instance is deleted or refreshed upon logoff, this is NA.\nFor AVD implementations with no data at rest, this is NA.\n\nIf full disk encryption using BitLocker is not implemented, this is a finding.\n\nVerify BitLocker is turned on for the operating system drive and any fixed data drives.\n\nOpen \"BitLocker Drive Encryption\" from the Control Panel.\n\nIf the operating system drive or any fixed data drives have \"Turn on BitLocker\", this is a finding.\n\nNote: An alternate encryption application may be used in lieu of BitLocker providing it is configured for full disk encryption and satisfies the pre-boot authentication requirements (WN11-00-000031 and WN11-00-000032).","ia_controls":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253259","title":"SRG-OS-000404-GPOS-00183"},"responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0"},{"rule_id_src":"SV-253260r1186370_rule","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nFor virtual desktop implementations (VDIs) in which the virtual desktop instance is deleted or refreshed upon logoff, this is NA.\n\nFor AVD implementations with no data at rest, this is NA.\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\FVE\\\n\nValue Name: UseAdvancedStartup\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)\n\nIf one of the following registry values does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding.\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\FVE\\\n\nValue Name: UseTPMPIN\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)\n\nValue Name: UseTPMKeyPIN\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)\n\nWhen BitLocker network unlock is used:\n\nValue Name: UseTPMPIN\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000002 (2)\n\nValue Name: UseTPMKeyPIN\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000002 (2)\n\nBitLocker network unlock may be used in conjunction with a BitLocker PIN. See the article below regarding information about network unlock.\n\nhttps://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/security/information-protection/bitlocker/bitlocker-how-to-enable-network-unlock","ia_controls":"","rule_id":"SV-253260r1186370","mitigation_control":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"id":"V-253260","title":"SRG-OS-000405-GPOS-00184"},"reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","rule_version":"WN11-00-000031","severity":"high","group_title":"SRG-OS-000405-GPOS-00184","ccis":["CCI-002476"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :     false (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nCriteria                :       false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :         false (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nTest                    :           false ('Configure TPM startup PIN' is set to 'Require startup PIN with TPM'.)\nResult Analysis         :                HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\FVE\\UseTPMPIN\\value = '2' failed test of 'equals' compared to '1' \nTest                    :           false ('Configure TPM startup key and PIN' is set to 'Require startup key and PIN with TPM'.)\nResult Analysis         :                HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\FVE\\UseTPMKeyPIN\\value = '2' failed test of 'equals' compared to '1' \nTest                    :         true ('Allow network unlock at startup' is Enabled.) (negated)\nCriteria                :       false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :         true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nTest                    :           true ('Configure TPM startup PIN' is set to 'Allow startup PIN with TPM'.)\nTest                    :           true ('Configure TPM startup key and PIN' is set to 'Allow startup key and PIN with TPM'.)\nTest                    :         false ('Allow network unlock at startup' is Enabled.)\nResult Analysis         :              Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\FVE\\OSManageNKP'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nTest                    :     true ('Require additional authentication at startup' is Enabled.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25326002 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : 'Configure TPM startup PIN' is set to 'Require startup PIN with TPM'.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25326002 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\FVE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'UseTPMPIN'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\FVE'\n                        : name equals 'UseTPMPIN'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '2'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\nResult Analysis         : HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\FVE\\UseTPMPIN\\value = '2' failed test of 'equals' compared to '1' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25326003 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : 'Configure TPM startup key and PIN' is set to 'Require startup key and PIN with TPM'.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25326003 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\FVE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'UseTPMKeyPIN'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\FVE'\n                        : name equals 'UseTPMKeyPIN'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '2'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\nResult Analysis         : HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\FVE\\UseTPMKeyPIN\\value = '2' failed test of 'equals' compared to '1' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25326000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : 'Allow network unlock at startup' is Enabled.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25326000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\FVE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'OSManageNKP'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\FVE\\OSManageNKP'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25326004 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Configure TPM startup PIN' is set to 'Allow startup PIN with TPM'.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25326002 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\FVE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'UseTPMPIN'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000002 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\FVE'\n                        : name equals 'UseTPMPIN'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '2'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25326005 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Configure TPM startup key and PIN' is set to 'Allow startup key and PIN with TPM'.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25326003 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\FVE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'UseTPMKeyPIN'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000002 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\FVE'\n                        : name equals 'UseTPMKeyPIN'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '2'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25326001 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Require additional authentication at startup' is Enabled.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25326001 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\FVE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'UseAdvancedStartup'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\FVE'\n                        : name equals 'UseAdvancedStartup'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows 11 systems must use a BitLocker PIN for pre-boot authentication.","mitigations":"","discussion":"If data at rest is unencrypted, it is vulnerable to disclosure. Even if the operating system enforces permissions on data access, an adversary can remove non-volatile memory and read it directly, thereby circumventing operating system controls. Encrypting the data ensures that confidentiality is protected even when the operating system is not running. Pre-boot authentication prevents unauthorized users from accessing encrypted drives.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","group_id":"V-253260","potential_impacts":"","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253260","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; BitLocker Drive Encryption &gt;&gt; Operating System Drives \"Require additional authentication at startup\" to \"Enabled\" with \"Configure TPM Startup PIN:\" set to \"Require startup PIN with TPM\" or with \"Configure TPM startup key and PIN:\" set to \"Require startup key and PIN with TPM\".\n\nIf Network Unlock is active, select \"Configure TPM startup PIN:\" and set to \"Require startup PIN with TPM\".\n\n If Network Unlock is not active, select \"Configure TPM startup key and PIN:\" and set to \"Require startup key and PIN with TPM\".","status":"open","uuid":"366EC4DE-6BF8-1014-AD13-B2A57F9E052F","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253260"}},{"fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; BitLocker Drive Encryption &gt;&gt; Operating System Drives \"Configure minimum PIN length for startup\" to \"Enabled\" with \"Minimum characters:\" set to \"6\" or greater.","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253261","group_id":"V-253261","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253261","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"uuid":"366ECDBE-6BF8-1014-8661-803C77E5F9DE","status":"not_a_finding","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (BitLocker must be 6 digits or more.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25326100 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : BitLocker must be 6 digits or more.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25326100 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Check for BitLocker MinimumPIN\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\FVE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'MinimumPIN'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25326100 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be greater than or equal to '6'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\FVE'\n                        : name equals 'MinimumPIN'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '6'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","mitigations":"","discussion":"If data at rest is unencrypted, it is vulnerable to disclosure. Even if the operating system enforces permissions on data access, an adversary can remove non-volatile memory and read it directly, thereby circumventing operating system controls. Encrypting the data ensures that confidentiality is protected even when the operating system is not running. Pre-boot authentication prevents unauthorized users from accessing encrypted drives. Increasing the pin length requires a greater number of guesses for an attacker.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows 11 systems must use a BitLocker PIN with a minimum length of six digits for pre-boot authentication.","rule_version":"WN11-00-000032","ccis":["CCI-000804"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000121-GPOS-00062","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id":"SV-253261r958504","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253261r958504_rule","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nFor virtual desktop implementations (VDIs) in which the virtual desktop instance is deleted or refreshed upon logoff, this is NA.\n\nFor AVD implementations with no data at rest, this is NA.\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\FVE\\\n\nValue Name: MinimumPIN\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000006 (6) or greater","ia_controls":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000121-GPOS-00062","id":"V-253261"},"reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0"},{"reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000370-GPOS-00155","id":"V-253262"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253262r958808","ia_controls":"","check_content":"Verify the operating system employs a deny-all, permit-by-exception policy to allow the execution of authorized software programs. This must include packaged apps such as the universal apps installed by default on systems.\n\nIf an application allowlisting program is not in use on the system, this is a finding.\n\nConfiguration of allowlisting applications will vary by the program.\n\nAppLocker is an allowlisting application built into Windows 11 Enterprise. A deny-by-default implementation is initiated by enabling any AppLocker rules within a category, only allowing what is specified by defined rules.\n\nIf AppLocker is used, perform the following to view the configuration of AppLocker:\nRun \"PowerShell\".\n\nExecute the following command, substituting [c:\\temp\\file.xml] with a location and file name appropriate for the system:\nGet-AppLockerPolicy -Effective -XML &gt; c:\\temp\\file.xml\n\nThis will produce an xml file with the effective settings that can be viewed in a browser or opened in a program such as Excel for review.\n\nImplementation guidance for AppLocker is available at the following link:\n\nhttps://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/security/threat-protection/windows-defender-application-control/applocker/applocker-policies-deployment-guide","rule_id_src":"SV-253262r958808_rule","ccis":["CCI-001774"],"group_title":"SRG-OS-000370-GPOS-00155","severity":"medium","rule_version":"WN11-00-000035","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","discussion":"Utilizing an allowlist provides a configuration management method for allowing the execution of only authorized software. Using only authorized software decreases risk by limiting the number of potential vulnerabilities.\n\nThe organization must identify authorized software programs and only permit execution of authorized software. The process used to identify software programs that are authorized to execute on organizational information systems is commonly referred to as allowlisting.","mitigations":"","rule_title":"The operating system must employ a deny-all, permit-by-exception policy to allow the execution of authorized software programs.","security_override_guidance":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-253262, SV-253262r958808, SRG-OS-000370-GPOS-00155)\n","check_content_ref":{"name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows11:questionnaire:1501","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-ocil.xml"},"uuid":"366EDA3F-6BF8-1014-9D13-F31941340CDB","status":"not_reviewed","fix_text":"Configure an application allowlisting program to employ a deny-all, permit-by-exception policy to allow the execution of authorized software programs.\n\nConfiguration of allowlisting applications will vary by the program. AppLocker is an allowlisting application built into Windows 11 Enterprise.\n\nIf AppLocker is used, it is configured through group policy in Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Application Control Policies &gt;&gt; AppLocker.\n\nImplementation guidance for AppLocker is available in the NSA paper \"Application allowlisting using Microsoft AppLocker\" at the following link:\n\nhttps://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/security/threat-protection/windows-defender-application-control/applocker/applocker-policies-deployment-guide","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253262","group_id":"V-253262","potential_impacts":""},{"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253263","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"check_content":"Run \"winver.exe\".\n\nIf the \"About Windows\" dialog box does not display \"Microsoft Windows 11 Version 22H2 (OS Build 22621.380)\" or greater, this is a finding.","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253263r1016364_rule","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253263r1016364","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","severity":"high","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"rule_version":"WN11-00-000040","discussion":"Windows 11 is maintained by Microsoft at servicing levels for specific periods of time to support Windows as a Service. Systems at unsupported servicing levels or releases will not receive security updates for new vulnerabilities which leaves them subject to exploitation.\n\nNew versions with feature updates are planned to be released on a semi-annual basis with an estimated support timeframe of 18 to 30 months depending on the release. Support for previously released versions has been extended for Enterprise editions.\n\nA separate servicing branch intended for special purpose systems is the Long-Term Servicing Channel (LTSC, formerly Branch - LTSB) which will receive security updates for 10 years but excludes feature updates.","mitigations":"","rule_title":"Windows 11 systems must be maintained at a supported servicing level.","security_override_guidance":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (The OS Version is equal to or greater than 6.3)\nTest                    :     true (The OS Build is equal to or greater than 22621)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25326300 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The OS Version is equal to or greater than 6.3\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25326300 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'CurrentVersion'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25326300 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_sz'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be greater than or equal to '6.3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion'\n                        : name equals 'CurrentVersion'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995370000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals '6.3'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25326301 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The OS Build is equal to or greater than 22621\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25326301 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'CurrentBuildNumber'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25326301 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_sz'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be greater than or equal to '22621'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion'\n                        : name equals 'CurrentBuildNumber'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995370000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals '26200'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253263","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"uuid":"366EE4E6-6BF8-1014-B35C-BDA4C293ADE7","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253263","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253263","fix_text":"Update systems on the Semi-Annual Channel to \"Microsoft Windows 11 Version 22H2 (OS Build 22621.380)\" or greater."},{"severity":"high","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"rule_version":"WN11-00-000045","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-253264"},"third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253264r1186372_rule","check_content":"Verify an organizationally approved antivirus solution (Microsoft Defender Antivirus, for example) is installed on the system and in use. \n\nVerify if Microsoft Defender Antivirus is in use or enabled:\n\nOpen PowerShell.\n\nEnter \"get-service | where {$_.DisplayName -Like \"*Defender*\"} | Select Status,DisplayName\"\n\nVerify third-party antivirus is in use or enabled:\n\nOpen PowerShell.\n\nEnter \"get-service | where {$_.DisplayName -Like \"*mcafee*\"} | Select Status,DisplayName\"\n\nEnter \"get-service | where {$_.DisplayName -Like \"*symantec*\"} | Select Status,DisplayName\"\n\nIf there is no antivirus solution installed on the system, this is a finding.","ia_controls":"","rule_id":"SV-253264r1186372","mitigation_control":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"366EEF82-6BF8-1014-9AD4-FBB5184A2DD8","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:253264"},"group_id":"V-253264","potential_impacts":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253264","false_positives":"","fix_text":"Install Microsoft Defender Antivirus or a third-party antivirus solution.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The Windows 11 system must use an antivirus program.","mitigations":"","discussion":"Malicious software can establish a base on individual desktops and servers. Employing an automated mechanism to detect this type of software will aid in elimination of the software from the operating system.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Windows must use an antivirus program)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25326401 (cmdlet_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Windows must use an antivirus program\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25326401 (cmdlet_object)\nObject Comment          : Gather AntivirusProduct from SecurityCenter2\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'module_name' must be equal to 'CimCmdlets'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'verb' must be equal to 'Get'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'noun' must be equal to 'CimInstance'\nObject Requirement      : for  'parameters' the following must be true:\n                        : classname must be equal to 'antivirusproduct'\n                        : namespace must be equal to 'root\\securitycenter2'\nObject Requirement      : for  'select' the following must be true:\n                        : property must be equal to 'displayname,productstate'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25326401 (cmdlet_state)\nState Comment           : An antivirus program must be installed and running\nState Requirement       : for at least one 'value' the following must be true:\n                        : all productstate must match a 'bitwise and' comparison to '4096'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : module_name equals 'CimCmdlets'\n                        : module_id equals '{fb6cc51d-c096-4b38-b78d-0fed6277096a}'\n                        : module_version equals '1.0.0.0'\n                        : verb equals 'Get'\n                        : noun equals 'CimInstance'\n                        : collected 'parameters' result: \n                        : classname = 'antivirusproduct'\n                        : namespace = 'root\\securitycenter2'\n                        : collected 'select' result: \n                        : property = 'displayname,productstate'\n                        : collected 'value' result: \n                        : displayname = 'Windows Defender'\n                        : productstate = '393472'\n                        : collected 'value' result: \n                        : displayname = 'Elastic Security'\n                        : productstate = '266240'\n"},{"status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253265","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"uuid":"366EFA65-6BF8-1014-B927-D85BCB46E158","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253265","group_id":"V-253265","potential_impacts":"","fix_text":"Format all local volumes to use NTFS.","discussion":"The ability to set access permissions and auditing is critical to maintaining the security and proper access controls of a system. To support this, volumes must be formatted using the NTFS file system.","mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Local volumes must be formatted using NTFS.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Local volumes use NTFS)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25326500 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Local volumes use NTFS\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25326500 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : All 'Local Disk' File systems not using NTFS\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT deviceid FROM win32_logicaldisk WHERE drivetype=3 AND filesystem!=\"NTFS\"'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : exists\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT deviceid FROM win32_logicaldisk WHERE drivetype=3 AND filesystem!=\"NTFS\"'\n","group_title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048","severity":"high","ccis":["CCI-000213"],"rule_version":"WN11-00-000050","weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253265","title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048"},"check_content":"Run \"Computer Management\".\nNavigate to Storage &gt;&gt; Disk Management.\n\nIf the \"File System\" column does not indicate \"NTFS\" for each volume assigned a drive letter, this is a finding.\n\nThis does not apply to system partitions such the Recovery and EFI System Partition.","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253265r1137691_rule","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253265r1137691"},{"reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-253266"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253266r991589","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"ia_controls":"","check_content":"Verify the system does not include other operating system installations.\n\nRun \"Advanced System Settings\".\nSelect the \"Advanced\" tab.\nClick the \"Settings\" button in the \"Startup and Recovery\" section.\n\nIf the drop-down list box \"Default operating system:\" shows any operating system other than Windows 11, this is a finding.","rule_id_src":"SV-253266r991589_rule","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","severity":"medium","rule_version":"WN11-00-000055","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Alternate operating systems must not be permitted on the same system.","discussion":"Allowing other operating systems to run on a secure system may allow security to be circumvented.","mitigations":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Review Installed OS via PowerShell)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25326601 (shellcommand_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Review Installed OS via PowerShell\nCheck Existence         : One and only one collected item may exist.\nCheck                   : One and only one item may match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25326601 (shellcommand_object)\nObject Comment          : Review Installed OS via PowerShell\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'shell' must be equal to 'powershell'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'command' must be equal to 'bcdedit /enum'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'pattern' must be equal to '^description'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25326601 (shellcommand_state)\nState Comment           : Boot Loader Description must be only Windows 11 (note Windows Boot Manager entry can be ignored)\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'command' must be equal to 'bcdedit /enum'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'pattern' must be equal to '^description'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'exit_status' must be equal to '0'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'stdout_line' must match the pattern '^description(\\s*)Windows (11|Boot Manager)$'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : shell equals 'powershell'\n                        : command equals 'bcdedit /enum'\n                        : pattern equals '^description'\n                        : exit_status equals '0'\n                        : stdout_line equals 'description             Windows Boot Manager'\n                        : stdout_line equals 'description             Windows 11'\n","uuid":"366F040A-6BF8-1014-A4EA-9A6CC3B99897","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:253266"},"status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Ensure Windows 11 is the only operating system on a device. Remove alternate operating systems.","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253266","group_id_src":"V-253266","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":""},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-253267, SV-253267r1137695, SRG-OS-000138-GPOS-00069)\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","mitigations":"","discussion":"Shares which provide network access, must not exist on a workstation except for system-created administrative shares, and could potentially expose sensitive information. If a share is necessary, share permissions, as well as NTFS permissions, must be reconfigured to give the minimum access to those accounts that require it.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Non-system-created file shares on a system must limit access to groups that require it.","fix_text":"If a non-system-created share is required on a system, configure the share and NTFS permissions to limit access to the specific groups or accounts that require it.\n\nRemove any unnecessary non-system-created shares.","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253267","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253267","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows11:questionnaire:2501"},"uuid":"366F1532-6BF8-1014-BEA1-B7FD70607413","status":"not_reviewed","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id":"SV-253267r1137695","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253267r1137695_rule","check_content":"Non-system-created shares must not exist on workstations.\n\nIf only system-created shares exist on the system, this is NA.\n\nRun \"Computer Management\".\nNavigate to System Tools &gt;&gt; Shared Folders &gt;&gt; Shares.\n\nIf the only shares listed are \"ADMIN$\", \"C$\" and \"IPC$\", this is NA.\n(Selecting Properties for system-created shares will display a message that it has been shared for administrative purposes.)\n\nRight-click any non-system-created shares.\nSelect \"Properties\".\nSelect the \"Share Permissions\" tab.\n\nVerify the necessity of any shares found.\nIf the file shares have not been reconfigured to restrict permissions to the specific groups or accounts that require access, this is a finding.\n\nSelect the \"Security\" tab.\n\nIf the NTFS permissions have not been reconfigured to restrict permissions to the specific groups or accounts that require access, this is a finding.","ia_controls":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253267","title":"SRG-OS-000138-GPOS-00069"},"reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN11-00-000060","ccis":["CCI-001090"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000138-GPOS-00069"},{"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000468-GPOS-00212","id":"V-253268"},"responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id":"SV-253268r1051039","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253268r1051039_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"Run \"PowerShell\".\nCopy the lines below to the PowerShell window and enter.\n\n\"([ADSI]('WinNT://{0}' -f $env:COMPUTERNAME)).Children | Where { $_.SchemaClassName -eq 'user' } | ForEach {\n  $user = ([ADSI]$_.Path)\n  $lastLogin = $user.Properties.LastLogin.Value\n  $enabled = ($user.Properties.UserFlags.Value -band 0x2) -ne 0x2\n  if ($lastLogin -eq $null) {\n   $lastLogin = 'Never'\n  }\n  Write-Host $user.Name $lastLogin $enabled \n}\"\n\nThis will return a list of local accounts with the account name, last logon, and if the account is enabled (True/False).\nFor example: User1 10/31/2015 5:49:56 AM True\n\nReview the list to determine the finding validity for each account reported.\n\nExclude the following accounts:\nBuilt-in administrator account (Disabled, SID ending in 500)\nBuilt-in guest account (Disabled, SID ending in 501)\nBuilt-in DefaultAccount (Disabled, SID ending in 503)\nLocal administrator account\n\nIf any enabled accounts have not been logged on to within the past 35 days, this is a finding.\n\nInactive accounts that have been reviewed and deemed to be required must be documented with the information system security officer (ISSO).","ccis":["CCI-000172","CCI-003627","CCI-000795"],"severity":"low","group_title":"SRG-OS-000468-GPOS-00212","rule_version":"WN11-00-000065","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","mitigations":"","discussion":"Outdated or unused accounts provide penetration points that may go undetected. Inactive accounts must be deleted if no longer necessary or, if still required, disable until needed.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000468-GPOS-00212, SRG-OS-000118-GPOS-00060","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Unused accounts must be disabled or removed from the system after 35 days of inactivity.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT III, V-253268, SV-253268r1051039, SRG-OS-000468-GPOS-00212)\n","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows11:questionnaire:2701"},"uuid":"366F21E4-6BF8-1014-86EB-B5A6ACD18A53","status":"not_reviewed","fix_text":"Review local accounts and verify their necessity. Disable or delete any active accounts that have not been used in the last 35 days.","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253268","group_id":"V-253268","potential_impacts":""},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT I, V-253269, SV-253269r958702, SRG-OS-000312-GPOS-00123)\n","rule_title":"Only accounts responsible for the administration of a system must have Administrator rights on the system.","security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"An account that does not have Administrator duties must not have Administrator rights. Such rights would allow the account to bypass or modify required security restrictions on that machine and make it vulnerable to attack.\n\nSystem administrators must log on to systems only using accounts with the minimum level of authority necessary.\n\nFor domain-joined workstations, the Domain Admins group must be replaced by a domain workstation administrator group (see V-36434 in the Active Directory Domain STIG). Restricting highly privileged accounts from the local Administrators group helps mitigate the risk of privilege escalation resulting from credential theft attacks.\n\nStandard user accounts must not be members of the local administrators group.","mitigations":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","group_id":"V-253269","potential_impacts":"","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253269","fix_text":"Configure the system to include only administrator groups or accounts that are responsible for the system in the local Administrators group.\n\nFor domain-joined workstations, the Domain Admins group must be replaced by a domain workstation administrator group.\n\nRemove any standard user accounts.","status":"not_reviewed","uuid":"366F2C5F-6BF8-1014-A86F-C3A4180684CD","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows11:questionnaire:2901"},"check_content":"Run \"Computer Management\".\nNavigate to System Tools &gt;&gt; Local Users and Groups &gt;&gt; Groups.\nReview the members of the Administrators group.\nOnly the appropriate administrator groups or accounts responsible for administration of the system may be members of the group.\n\nFor domain-joined workstations, the Domain Admins group must be replaced by a domain workstation administrator group.\n\nStandard user accounts must not be members of the local administrator group.\n\nIf prohibited accounts are members of the local administrators group, this is a finding.\n\nThe built-in Administrator account or other required administrative accounts would not be a finding.","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253269r958702_rule","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253269r958702","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000312-GPOS-00123","id":"V-253269"},"rule_version":"WN11-00-000070","group_title":"SRG-OS-000312-GPOS-00123","severity":"high","ccis":["CCI-002165"]},{"mitigations":"","discussion":"Backup Operators are able to read and write to any file in the system, regardless of the rights assigned to it. Backup and restore rights permit users to circumvent the file access restrictions present on NTFS disk drives for backup and restore purposes. Members of the Backup Operators group must have separate logon accounts for performing backup duties.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Only accounts responsible for the backup operations must be members of the Backup Operators group.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-253270, SV-253270r991589, SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227)\n","status":"not_reviewed","check_content_ref":{"name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows11:questionnaire:3101","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-ocil.xml"},"uuid":"366F390C-6BF8-1014-A4A9-F7CE197FB0F2","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253270","group_id":"V-253270","potential_impacts":"","fix_text":"Create separate accounts for backup operations for users with this privilege.","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-253270"},"responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253270r991589_rule","check_content":"Run \"Computer Management\".\nNavigate to System Tools &gt;&gt; Local Users and Groups &gt;&gt; Groups.\nReview the members of the Backup Operators group.\n\nIf the group contains no accounts, this is not a finding.\n\nIf the group contains any accounts, the accounts must be specifically for backup functions.\n\nIf the group contains any standard user accounts used for performing normal user tasks, this is a finding.","ia_controls":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id":"SV-253270r991589","mitigation_control":"","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"rule_version":"WN11-00-000075"},{"check_content":"If a hosted hypervisor (Hyper-V, VMware Workstation, etc.) is installed on the system, verify only authorized user accounts are allowed to run virtual machines.\n\nFor Hyper-V, run \"Computer Management\".\nNavigate to System Tools &gt;&gt; Local Users and Groups &gt;&gt; Groups.\nDouble click on \"Hyper-V Administrators\".\n\nIf any unauthorized groups or user accounts are listed in \"Members:\", this is a finding.\n\nFor hosted hypervisors other than Hyper-V, verify only authorized user accounts have access to run the virtual machines. Restrictions may be enforced by access to the physical system, software restriction policies, or access restrictions built into the application.\n\nIf any unauthorized groups or user accounts have access to create or run virtual machines, this is a finding.\n\nAll users authorized to create or run virtual machines must be documented with the ISSM/ISSO. Accounts nested within group accounts must be documented as individual accounts and not the group accounts.","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253271r958702_rule","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253271r958702","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253271","title":"SRG-OS-000312-GPOS-00124"},"rule_version":"WN11-00-000080","group_title":"SRG-OS-000312-GPOS-00124","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-002165"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-253271, SV-253271r958702, SRG-OS-000312-GPOS-00124)\n","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Only authorized user accounts must be allowed to create or run virtual machines on Windows 11 systems.","discussion":"Allowing other operating systems to run on a secure system may allow users to circumvent security. For Hyper-V, preventing unauthorized users from being assigned to the Hyper-V Administrators group will prevent them from accessing or creating virtual machines on the system. The Hyper-V Hypervisor is used by virtualization-based Security features such as Credential Guard on Windows 11; however, it is not the full Hyper-V installation.","mitigations":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253271","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253271","fix_text":"For Hyper-V, remove any unauthorized groups or user accounts from the \"Hyper-V Administrators\" group.\n\nFor hosted hypervisors other than Hyper-V, restrict access to create or run virtual machines to authorized user accounts only.","status":"not_reviewed","uuid":"366F4337-6BF8-1014-9DD8-EE0C940E4152","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows11:questionnaire:3301"}},{"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-253272"},"responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id":"SV-253272r991589","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253272r991589_rule","check_content":"Run \"Computer Management\".\nNavigate to System Tools &gt;&gt; Local Users and Groups &gt;&gt; Users.\n\nIf local users other than the accounts listed below exist on a workstation in a domain, this is a finding. \n\nFor standalone or nondomain-joined systems, this is Not Applicable.\n\nBuilt-in Administrator account (Disabled)\nBuilt-in Guest account (Disabled)\nBuilt-in DefaultAccount (Disabled)\nBuilt-in defaultuser0 (Disabled)\nBuilt-in WDAGUtilityAccount (Disabled)\nLocal administrator account(s)\n\nAll of the built-in accounts may not exist on a system, depending on the Windows 11 version.","ia_controls":"","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"severity":"low","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","rule_version":"WN11-00-000085","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","mitigations":"","discussion":"To minimize potential points of attack, local user accounts, other than built-in accounts and local administrator accounts, must not exist on a workstation in a domain. Users must log on to workstations in a domain with their domain accounts.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Standard local user accounts must not exist on a system in a domain.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT III, V-253272, SV-253272r991589, SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227)\n","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows11:questionnaire:3501"},"uuid":"366F4C43-6BF8-1014-B825-B725CF9A6517","status":"not_reviewed","fix_text":"Limit local user accounts on domain-joined systems. Remove any unauthorized local accounts.","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253272","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253272"},{"rule_id":"SV-253273r1051040","mitigation_control":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id_src":"SV-253273r1051040_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"Run \"Computer Management\".\nNavigate to System Tools &gt;&gt; Local Users and Groups &gt;&gt; Users.\nDouble-click each active account.\n\nIf \"Password never expires\" is selected for any account, this is a finding.","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000076-GPOS-00044","id":"V-253273"},"reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN11-00-000090","ccis":["CCI-004066","CCI-000199"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000076-GPOS-00044","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Accounts must be configured to require password expiration.)\nResult Analysis         :        Existence requirement is 'none_exists' and 1 collected item exists, so result is false\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25327301 (cmdlet_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Accounts must be configured to require password expiration.\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25327301 (cmdlet_object)\nObject Comment          : Enabled Local Accounts with PasswordExpires=False should not exist\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'module_name' must be equal to 'CimCmdlets'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'verb' must be equal to 'Get'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'noun' must be equal to 'CimInstance'\nObject Requirement      : for  'parameters' the following must be true:\n                        : class must be equal to 'Win32_Useraccount'\n                        : filter must be equal to 'PasswordExpires=False and LocalAccount=True and Disabled=false'\nObject Requirement      : for  'select' the following must be true:\n                        : unique must be equal to 'Name,PasswordExpires,Disabled,LocalAccount'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : exists\n                        : module_name equals 'CimCmdlets'\n                        : module_id equals '{fb6cc51d-c096-4b38-b78d-0fed6277096a}'\n                        : module_version equals '1.0.0.0'\n                        : verb equals 'Get'\n                        : noun equals 'CimInstance'\n                        : collected 'parameters' result: \n                        : collected 'select' result: \n                        : collected 'value' result: \n\nResult Analysis         : Existence requirement is 'none_exists' and 1 collected item exists, so result is false\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","rule_title":"Accounts must be configured to require password expiration.","security_override_guidance":"","mitigations":"","discussion":"Passwords that do not expire increase exposure with a greater probability of being discovered or cracked.","fix_text":"Configure all passwords to expire.\nRun \"Computer Management\".\nNavigate to System Tools &gt;&gt; Local Users and Groups &gt;&gt; Users.\nDouble-click each active account.\nEnsure \"Password never expires\" is not checked on all active accounts.","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253273","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253273","uuid":"366F53FE-6BF8-1014-A963-B61E23364DA5","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:253273"},"status":"open"},{"status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"366F5C1A-6BF8-1014-A028-A8ACCB05A6D9","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:253274"},"potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253274","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253274","fix_text":"Maintain the default file system permissions and configure the Security Option: \"Network access: Let everyone permissions apply to anonymous users\" to \"Disabled\" (WN11-SO-000160).","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Permissions for system files and directories must conform to minimum requirements.","mitigations":"","discussion":"Changing the system's file and directory permissions allows the possibility of unauthorized and anonymous modification to the operating system and installed applications.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Network access: Let Everyone permissions apply to anonymous users is set to 'Disabled')\nTest                    :   true (System drive root directory permissions must conform to minimum requirements.)\nTest                    :   true (Windows installation directory permissions must conform to minimum requirements.)\nTest                    :   true (Program Files directory permissions must conform to minimum requirements.)\nTest                    :   true (Program Files (x86) directory permissions must conform to minimum requirements.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25327401 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Network access: Let Everyone permissions apply to anonymous users is set to 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : One and only one item may match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25327401 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : everyoneincludesanonymous must be configured\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'everyoneincludesanonymous'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25327401 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Value must be equal to 0\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa'\n                        : name equals 'everyoneincludesanonymous'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995350000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25327402 (shellcommand_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : System drive root directory permissions must conform to minimum requirements.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25327402 (shellcommand_object)\nObject Comment          : Run Icacls command against system drive root directory\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'shell' must be equal to 'powershell'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'command' must be equal to 'icacls($env:SystemDrive + '\\')'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'pattern' must be equal to ':'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25327402 (shellcommand_state)\nState Comment           : Permissions must equal expected output\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'exit_status' must be equal to '0'\nState Requirement       : for allstdout_line, at least one of the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)S-1-15-3-65536-1888954469-739942743-1668119174-2468466756-4239452838-1296943325-355587736-700089176:\\(S,RD,X,RA\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)NT AUTHORITY\\\\SYSTEM:\\(OI\\)\\(CI\\)\\(F\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)BUILTIN\\\\Administrators:\\(OI\\)\\(CI\\)\\(F\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)BUILTIN\\\\Users:\\(OI\\)\\(CI\\)\\(RX\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)NT AUTHORITY\\\\Authenticated Users:\\(OI\\)\\(CI\\)\\(IO\\)\\(M\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)NT AUTHORITY\\\\Authenticated Users:\\(AD\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)Mandatory Label\\\\High Mandatory Level:\\(OI\\)\\(NP\\)\\(IO\\)\\(NW\\)'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : shell equals 'powershell'\n                        : command equals 'icacls($env:SystemDrive + '\\')'\n                        : pattern equals ':'\n                        : exit_status equals '0'\n                        : stdout_line equals 'C:\\ BUILTIN\\Administrators:(OI)(CI)(F)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '    NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM:(OI)(CI)(F)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '    BUILTIN\\Users:(OI)(CI)(RX)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '    NT AUTHORITY\\Authenticated Users:(OI)(CI)(IO)(M)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '    NT AUTHORITY\\Authenticated Users:(AD)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '    S-1-15-3-65536-1888954469-739942743-1668119174-2468466756-4239452838-1296943325-355587736-700089176:(S,RD,X,RA)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '    Mandatory Label\\High Mandatory Level:(OI)(NP)(IO)(NW)'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25327403 (shellcommand_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Windows installation directory permissions must conform to minimum requirements.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25327403 (shellcommand_object)\nObject Comment          : Run Icacls command against Windows install directory\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'shell' must be equal to 'powershell'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'command' must be equal to 'icacls($env:windir)'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'pattern' must be equal to ':'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25327403 (shellcommand_state)\nState Comment           : Permissions must equal expected output\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'exit_status' must be equal to '0'\nState Requirement       : for allstdout_line, at least one of the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)NT SERVICE\\\\TrustedInstaller:\\(F\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)NT SERVICE\\\\TrustedInstaller:\\(CI\\)\\(IO\\)\\(F\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)NT AUTHORITY\\\\SYSTEM:\\(M\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)NT AUTHORITY\\\\SYSTEM:\\(OI\\)\\(CI\\)\\(IO\\)\\(F\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)BUILTIN\\\\Administrators:\\(M\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)BUILTIN\\\\Administrators:\\(OI\\)\\(CI\\)\\(IO\\)\\(F\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)BUILTIN\\\\Users:\\(RX\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)BUILTIN\\\\Users:\\(OI\\)\\(CI\\)\\(IO\\)\\(GR,GE\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)CREATOR OWNER:\\(OI\\)\\(CI\\)\\(IO\\)\\(F\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\\\ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES:\\(RX\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\\\ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES:\\(OI\\)\\(CI\\)\\(IO\\)\\(GR,GE\\)'\nState Requirement       :     