ut_line must match the pattern '(?i)NT SERVICE\\\\TrustedInstaller:\\(F\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)NT SERVICE\\\\TrustedInstaller:\\(CI\\)\\(IO\\)\\(F\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)NT AUTHORITY\\\\SYSTEM:\\(M\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)NT AUTHORITY\\\\SYSTEM:\\(OI\\)\\(CI\\)\\(IO\\)\\(F\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)BUILTIN\\\\Administrators:\\(M\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)BUILTIN\\\\Administrators:\\(OI\\)\\(CI\\)\\(IO\\)\\(F\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)BUILTIN\\\\Users:\\(RX\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)BUILTIN\\\\Users:\\(OI\\)\\(CI\\)\\(IO\\)\\(GR,GE\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)CREATOR OWNER:\\(OI\\)\\(CI\\)\\(IO\\)\\(F\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\\\ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES:\\(RX\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\\\ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES:\\(OI\\)\\(CI\\)\\(IO\\)\\(GR,GE\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\\\ALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES:\\(RX\\)'\nState Requirement       :     stdout_line must match the pattern '(?i)APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\\\ALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES:\\(OI\\)\\(CI\\)\\(IO\\)\\(GR,GE\\)'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : shell equals 'powershell'\n                        : command equals 'icacls (Get-ItemProperty -Path \"HKLM:\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\" -Name 'ProgramFilesDir (x86)').'ProgramFilesDir (x86)''\n                        : pattern equals ':'\n                        : exit_status equals '0'\n                        : stdout_line equals 'C:\\Program Files (x86) NT SERVICE\\TrustedInstaller:(F)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '                       NT SERVICE\\TrustedInstaller:(CI)(IO)(F)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '                       NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM:(M)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '                       NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM:(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '                       BUILTIN\\Administrators:(M)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '                       BUILTIN\\Administrators:(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '                       BUILTIN\\Users:(RX)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '                       BUILTIN\\Users:(OI)(CI)(IO)(GR,GE)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '                       CREATOR OWNER:(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '                       APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES:(RX)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '                       APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES:(OI)(CI)(IO)(GR,GE)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '                       APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\ALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES:(RX)'\n                        : stdout_line equals '                       APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\ALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES:(OI)(CI)(IO)(GR,GE)'\n","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000312-GPOS-00122","ccis":["CCI-002165"],"rule_version":"WN11-00-000095","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000312-GPOS-00122","id":"V-253274"},"reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253274r1016661_rule","check_content":"The default file system permissions are adequate when the Security Option \"Network access: Let Everyone permissions apply to anonymous users\" is set to \"Disabled\" (WN11-SO-000160).\n\nIf the default file system permissions are maintained and the referenced option is set to \"Disabled\", this is not a finding.\n\nVerify the default permissions for the sample directories below. Non-privileged groups such as Users or Authenticated Users must not have greater than read &amp; execute permissions except where noted as defaults. (Individual accounts must not be used to assign permissions.)\n\nSelect the \"Security\" tab, and the \"Advanced\" button.\n\nC:\\\nType - \"Allow\" for all\nInherited from - \"None\" for all\nPrincipal - Access - Applies to\nAdministrators - Full control - This folder, subfolders, and files\nSYSTEM - Full control - This folder, subfolders, and files\nUsers - Read &amp; execute - This folder, subfolders, and files\nAuthenticated Users - Modify - Subfolders and files only\nAuthenticated Users - Create folders / append data - This folder only\n\n\\Program Files\nType - \"Allow\" for all\nInherited from - \"None\" for all\nPrincipal - Access - Applies to\nTrustedInstaller - Full control - This folder and subfolders\nSYSTEM - Modify - This folder only\nSYSTEM - Full control - Subfolders and files only\nAdministrators - Modify - This folder only\nAdministrators - Full control - Subfolders and files only\nUsers - Read &amp; execute - This folder, subfolders, and files\nCREATOR OWNER - Full control - Subfolders and files only\nALL APPLICATION PACKAGES - Read &amp; execute - This folder, subfolders, and files\nALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES - Read &amp; execute - This folder, subfolders, and files\n\n\\Windows\nType - \"Allow\" for all\nInherited from - \"None\" for all\nPrincipal - Access - Applies to\nTrustedInstaller - Full control - This folder and subfolders\nSYSTEM - Modify - This folder only\nSYSTEM - Full control - Subfolders and files only\nAdministrators - Modify - This folder only\nAdministrators - Full control - Subfolders and files only\nUsers - Read &amp; execute - This folder, subfolders, and files\nCREATOR OWNER - Full control - Subfolders and files only\nALL APPLICATION PACKAGES - Read &amp; execute - This folder, subfolders, and files\nALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES - Read &amp; execute - This folder, subfolders, and files\n\nAlternately use icacls.\n\nRun \"CMD\" as administrator.\nEnter \"icacls\" followed by the directory.\n\nicacls c:\\\nicacls \"c:\\program files\"\nicacls c:\\windows\n\nThe following results will be displayed as each is entered:\n\nc:\\\nS-1-15-3-65536-1888954469-739942743-1668119174-2468466756-4239452838-1296943325-355587736-700089176 (S,RD,X,RA)\nBUILTIN\\Administrators:(OI)(CI)(F)\nNT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM:(OI)(CI)(F)\nBUILTIN\\Users:(OI)(CI)(RX)\nNT AUTHORITY\\Authenticated Users:(OI)(CI)(IO)(M)\nNT AUTHORITY\\Authenticated Users:(AD)\nMandatory Label\\High Mandatory Level:(OI)(NP)(IO)(NW)\nSuccessfully processed 1 files; Failed processing 0 files\n\nc:\\program files \nNT SERVICE\\TrustedInstaller:(F)\nNT SERVICE\\TrustedInstaller:(CI)(IO)(F)\nNT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM:(M)\nNT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM:(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)\nBUILTIN\\Administrators:(M)\nBUILTIN\\Administrators:(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)\nBUILTIN\\Users:(RX)\nBUILTIN\\Users:(OI)(CI)(IO)(GR,GE)\nCREATOR OWNER:(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)\nAPPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES:(RX)\nAPPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES:(OI)(CI)(IO)(GR,GE)\nAPPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\ALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES:(RX)\nAPPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\ALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES:(OI)(CI)(IO)(GR,GE)\nSuccessfully processed 1 files; Failed processing 0 files\n\nc:\\windows\nNT SERVICE\\TrustedInstaller:(F)\nNT SERVICE\\TrustedInstaller:(CI)(IO)(F)\nNT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM:(M)\nNT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM:(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)\nBUILTIN\\Administrators:(M)\nBUILTIN\\Administrators:(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)\nBUILTIN\\Users:(RX)\nBUILTIN\\Users:(OI)(CI)(IO)(GR,GE)\nCREATOR OWNER:(OI)(CI)(IO)(F)\nAPPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES:(RX)\nAPPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES:(OI)(CI)(IO)(GR,GE)\nAPPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\ALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES:(RX)\nAPPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\ALL RESTRICTED APPLICATION PACKAGES:(OI)(CI)(IO)(GR,GE)\nSuccessfully processed 1 files; Failed processing 0 files","ia_controls":"","rule_id":"SV-253274r1016661","mitigation_control":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified"},{"severity":"high","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"rule_version":"WN11-00-000100","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"id":"V-253275","title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049"},"responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253275r958478_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"Verify it has not been installed on the system.\n\nRun \"Programs and Features\".\nSelect \"Turn Windows features on or off\".\n\nIf the entries for \"Internet Information Services\" or \"Internet Information Services Hostable Web Core\" are selected, this is a finding.\n\nIf an application requires IIS or a subset to be installed to function, this needs be documented with the ISSO. In addition, any applicable requirements from the IIS STIG must be addressed.","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id":"SV-253275r958478","mitigation_control":"","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253275","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"uuid":"366F6719-6BF8-1014-BB8E-F4FBC5AF2B37","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253275","group_id":"V-253275","potential_impacts":"","fix_text":"Uninstall \"Internet Information Services\" or \"Internet Information Services Hostable Web Core\" from the system.","mitigations":"","discussion":"IIS is not installed by default. Installation of Internet Information System (IIS) may allow unauthorized internet services to be hosted. Websites must only be hosted on servers that have been designed for that purpose and can be adequately secured.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Internet Information System (IIS) or its subcomponents must not be installed on a workstation.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Internet Information Services' feature is not installed)\nTest                    :     true ('Internet Information Services Hostable Web Core' feature is not installed)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25327500 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Internet Information Services' feature is not installed\nCheck Existence         : All collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25327500 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT installstate FROM win32_optionalfeature WHERE name = 'IIS-WebServerRole''\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25327500 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : InstallState is equal to 2\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : at least one installstate must be equal to '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT installstate FROM win32_optionalfeature WHERE name = 'IIS-WebServerRole''\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : installstate = '2'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25327501 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Internet Information Services Hostable Web Core' feature is not installed\nCheck Existence         : All collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25327501 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT installstate FROM win32_optionalfeature WHERE name = 'IIS-HostableWebCore''\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25327500 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : InstallState is equal to 2\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : at least one installstate must be equal to '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT installstate FROM win32_optionalfeature WHERE name = 'IIS-HostableWebCore''\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : installstate = '2'\n"},{"classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253276r958480","ia_controls":"","check_content":"Verify SNMP has not been installed.\n\nNavigate to the Windows\\System32 directory.\n\nIf the \"SNMP\" application exists, this is a finding.","rule_id_src":"SV-253276r958480_rule","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000096-GPOS-00050","id":"V-253276"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","rule_version":"WN11-00-000105","ccis":["CCI-000382"],"group_title":"SRG-OS-000096-GPOS-00050","severity":"medium","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (SNMP Shall Not Be Installed)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25327601 (service_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : SNMP Shall Not Be Installed\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25327601 (service_object)\nObject Comment          : SNMP Service\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'service_name' must be equal to 'SNMP'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : does not exist\n                        : service_name does not exist\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","discussion":"\"SNMP\" is not installed by default. Some protocols and services do not support required security features, such as encrypting passwords or traffic.","mitigations":"","rule_title":"Simple Network Management Protocol (SNMP) must not be installed on the system.","security_override_guidance":"","fix_text":"Uninstall \"Simple Network Management Protocol (SNMP)\" from the system.\n\nRun \"Programs and Features\".\nSelect \"Turn Windows Features on or off\".\nDe-select \"Simple Network Management Protocol (SNMP)\".","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253276","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253276","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:253276"},"uuid":"366F6F47-6BF8-1014-8CAB-B2968E7938C0","status":"not_a_finding"},{"fix_text":"Uninstall \"Simple TCPIP Services (i.e. echo, daytime etc.)\" from the system.\n\nRun \"Programs and Features\".\nSelect \"Turn Windows Features on or off\".\nDe-select \"Simple TCPIP Services (i.e. echo, daytime etc.)\".","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253277","group_id":"V-253277","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253277"},"uuid":"366F76DF-6BF8-1014-8818-AA88B05CB5AE","status":"not_a_finding","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Check to make sure the Simple TCP/IP Services server feature is not present.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25327700 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Check to make sure the Simple TCP/IP Services server feature is not present.\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25327700 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : Simple TCP/IP Services\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT startmode FROM Win32_Service WHERE name='simptcp''\n\nCollected Item/State Result : exists\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT startmode FROM Win32_Service WHERE name='simptcp''\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","mitigations":"","discussion":"\"Simple TCP/IP Services\" is not installed by default. Some protocols and services do not support required security features, such as encrypting passwords or traffic.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Simple TCP/IP Services must not be installed on the system.","rule_version":"WN11-00-000110","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id":"SV-253277r958478","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253277r958478_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"Verify Simple TCP/IP Services has not been installed.\n\nRun \"Services.msc\".\n\nIf \"Simple TCP/IP Services\" is listed, this is a finding.","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","id":"V-253277"},"reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0"},{"false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253278","group_id":"V-253278","potential_impacts":"","fix_text":"Uninstall \"Telnet Client\" from the system.\n\nRun \"Programs and Features\".\nSelect \"Turn Windows Features on or off\".\n\nDe-select \"Telnet Client\".","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253278"},"uuid":"366F7E02-6BF8-1014-BF72-AA61A821B75B","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (The Telnet Client is not installed on the system)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25327800 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The Telnet Client is not installed on the system\nCheck Existence         : All collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25327800 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT installstate FROM win32_optionalfeature WHERE name = 'TelnetClient''\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25327800 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : at least one installstate must be equal to '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT installstate FROM win32_optionalfeature WHERE name = 'TelnetClient''\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : installstate = '2'\n","discussion":"The \"Telnet Client\" is not installed by default. Some protocols and services do not support required security features, such as encrypting passwords or traffic.","mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The Telnet Client must not be installed on the system.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","rule_version":"WN11-00-000115","group_title":"SRG-OS-000096-GPOS-00050","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-000382"],"ia_controls":"","check_content":"Verify Telnet Client has not been installed.\n\nNavigate to the Windows\\System32 directory.\n\nIf the \"telnet\" application exists, this is a finding.","rule_id_src":"SV-253278r958480_rule","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253278r958480","weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000096-GPOS-00050","id":"V-253278"}},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (The TFTP Client is not installed on the system)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25327900 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The TFTP Client is not installed on the system\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25327900 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT installstate FROM win32_optionalfeature WHERE name = 'TFTP''\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25327900 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all installstate must be equal to '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT installstate FROM win32_optionalfeature WHERE name = 'TFTP''\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : installstate = '2'\n","rule_title":"The TFTP Client must not be installed on the system.","security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"The \"TFTP Client\" is not installed by default. Some protocols and services do not support required security features, such as encrypting passwords or traffic.","mitigations":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","group_id":"V-253279","potential_impacts":"","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253279","fix_text":"Uninstall \"TFTP Client\" from the system.\n\nRun \"Programs and Features\".\nSelect \"Turn Windows Features on or off\".\nDe-select \"TFTP Client\".","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"366F853E-6BF8-1014-BAB1-933F30358E20","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253279","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"check_content":"Verify TFTP Client has not been installed.\n\nNavigate to the Windows\\System32 directory.\n\nIf the \"TFTP\" application exists, this is a finding.","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253279r958480_rule","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253279r958480","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253279","title":"SRG-OS-000096-GPOS-00050"},"rule_version":"WN11-00-000120","group_title":"SRG-OS-000096-GPOS-00050","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-000382"]},{"security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Software certificate installation files must be removed from Windows 11.","discussion":"Use of software certificates and their accompanying installation files for end users to access resources is less secure than the use of hardware-based certificates.","mitigations":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Software certificate installation files must be removed. Remove .p12 files)\nTest                    :   true (Software certificate installation files must be removed. Remove .pfx files)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25328001 (file_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Software certificate installation files must be removed. Remove .p12 files\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25328001 (file_object)\nObject Comment          : Search for .p12 files\nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  recurse_direction = down\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'path' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'filename' must match the pattern '.[Pp]12$'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25328002 (file_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Software certificate installation files must be removed. Remove .pfx files\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25328002 (file_object)\nObject Comment          : Search for .pfx files\nObject Requirement      : behavior requirements:\n                        :  recurse_direction = down\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'path' must match the pattern '.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'filename' must match the pattern '.[Pp][Ff][Xx]$'\n","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"366F8CA3-6BF8-1014-8A84-A2B8626572ED","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:253280"},"group_id":"V-253280","potential_impacts":"","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253280","fix_text":"Remove any certificate installation files (*.p12 and *.pfx) found on a system.\n\nNote: This does not apply to server-based applications that have a requirement for .p12 certificate files (e.g., Oracle Wallet Manager) or Adobe PreFlight certificate files.","weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253280","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"check_content":"Search all drives for *.p12 and *.pfx files.\n\nIf any files with these extensions exist, this is a finding.\n\nThis does not apply to server-based applications that have a requirement for .p12 certificate files (e.g., Oracle Wallet Manager) or Adobe PreFlight certificate files. Some applications create files with extensions of .p12 that are not certificate installation files. Removal of non-certificate installation files from systems is not required. These must be documented with the ISSO.","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253280r991589_rule","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253280r991589","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"rule_version":"WN11-00-000130"},{"responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253281","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253281r991589","check_content":"Determine if a host-based firewall is installed and enabled on the system. If a host-based firewall is not installed and enabled on the system, this is a finding.\n\nThe configuration requirements will be determined by the applicable firewall STIG.","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253281r991589_rule","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","severity":"medium","rule_version":"WN11-00-000135","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","discussion":"A firewall provides a line of defense against attack, allowing or blocking inbound and outbound connections based on a set of rules.","mitigations":"","rule_title":"A host-based firewall must be installed and enabled on the system.","security_override_guidance":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nTest                    :   false (Verify a 3rd party firewall is installed and enabled via Security Center.)\nResult Analysis         :        .  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nTest                    :   false (Verify Windows defender firewall is enabled.)\nResult Analysis         :        enabled = 'False' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'True' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25328101 (cmdlet_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Verify a 3rd party firewall is installed and enabled via Security Center.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : At least one collected item must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25328101 (cmdlet_object)\nObject Comment          : Gather FirewallProduct from SecurityCenter2\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'module_name' must be equal to 'CimCmdlets'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'verb' must be equal to 'Get'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'noun' must be equal to 'CimInstance'\nObject Requirement      : for  'parameters' the following must be true:\n                        : classname must be equal to 'firewallproduct'\n                        : namespace must be equal to 'root\\securitycenter2'\nObject Requirement      : for  'select' the following must be true:\n                        : property must be equal to 'displayname,productstate'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25328101 (cmdlet_state)\nState Comment           : Product State must be 397568 (enabled)\nState Requirement       : for all 'value' the following must be true:\n                        : all productstate must be equal to '266240'\n\nResult Analysis         : .  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25328102 (cmdlet_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Verify Windows defender firewall is enabled.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : At least one collected item must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25328102 (cmdlet_object)\nObject Comment          : Gather FirewallProduct from NetSecurity\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'module_name' must be equal to 'NetSecurity'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'verb' must be equal to 'Get'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'noun' must be equal to 'NetFirewallProfile'\nObject Requirement      : for  'parameters' the following must be true:\n                        : policystore must be equal to 'ActiveStore'\nObject Requirement      : for  'select' the following must be true:\n                        : property must be equal to 'name,enabled,defaultinboundaction,defaultoutboundaction,logfilename'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25328102 (cmdlet_state)\nState Comment           : Enabled must be 'True')\nState Requirement       : for all 'value' the following must be true:\n                        : all enabled must be equal to 'True'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : module_name equals 'NetSecurity'\n                        : module_id equals '{4b26ff51-7aee-4731-9cf7-508b82532cbf}'\n                        : module_version equals '2.0.0.0'\n                        : verb equals 'Get'\n                        : noun equals 'NetFirewallProfile'\n                        : collected 'parameters' result: \n                        : collected 'select' result: \n                        : collected 'value' result: \n                        : !![ enabled = 'False' ]!!\n                        : defaultinboundaction = 'Allow'\n                        : defaultoutboundaction = 'Allow'\n                        : logfilename = '%systemroot%\\system32\\LogFiles\\Firewall\\pfirewall.log'\n                        : collected 'value' result: \n                        : !![ enabled = 'False' ]!!\n                        : defaultinboundaction = 'Allow'\n                        : defaultoutboundaction = 'Allow'\n                        : logfilename = '%systemroot%\\system32\\LogFiles\\Firewall\\pfirewall.log'\n                        : collected 'value' result: \n                        : !![ enabled = 'False' ]!!\n                        : defaultinboundaction = 'Allow'\n                        : defaultoutboundaction = 'Allow'\n                        : logfilename = '%systemroot%\\system32\\LogFiles\\Firewall\\pfirewall.log'\n\nResult Analysis         : enabled = 'False' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'True' \n","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:253281","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml"},"uuid":"366F950E-6BF8-1014-A609-EE79AFCB72C1","status":"open","fix_text":"Install and enable a host-based firewall on the system.","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253281","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253281"},{"stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","rule_title":"Inbound exceptions to the firewall on Windows 11 domain workstations must only allow authorized remote management hosts.","security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"Allowing inbound access to domain workstations from other systems may allow lateral movement across systems if credentials are compromised. Limiting inbound connections only from authorized remote management systems will help limit this exposure.","mitigations":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-253282, SV-253282r991593, SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00232)\n","uuid":"366F9DD7-6BF8-1014-836B-D776952CE2F9","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows11:questionnaire:5501"},"status":"not_reviewed","fix_text":"Configure firewall exceptions to inbound connections on domain workstations to include only authorized remote management hosts.\n\nConfigure only inbound connection exceptions for authorized remote management hosts.\nComputer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Windows Defender Firewall with Advanced Security &gt;&gt; Windows Defender Firewall with Advanced Security &gt;&gt; Inbound Rules (this link will be in the right pane)\n\nFor any inbound rules that allow connections, configure the Scope for Remote IP address to those of authorized remote management hosts. This may be defined as an IP address, subnet or range. Apply the rule to all firewall profiles.\n\nIf a third-party firewall is used, configure inbound exceptions to only include authorized remote management hosts.","group_id":"V-253282","potential_impacts":"","group_id_src":"V-253282","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00232","id":"V-253282"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253282r991593","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"ia_controls":"","check_content":"Verify firewall exceptions to inbound connections on domain workstations include only authorized remote management hosts.\n\nIf allowed inbound exceptions are not limited to authorized remote management hosts, this is a finding.\n\nReview inbound firewall exceptions.\nComputer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Windows Defender Firewall with Advanced Security &gt;&gt; Windows Defender Firewall with Advanced Security &gt;&gt; Inbound Rules (this link will be in the right pane)\n\nFor any inbound rules that allow connections view the Scope for Remote IP address. This may be defined as an IP address, subnet, or range. The rule must apply to all firewall profiles.\n\nIf a third-party firewall is used, ensure comparable settings are in place.","rule_id_src":"SV-253282r991593_rule","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00232","severity":"medium","rule_version":"WN11-00-000140"},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (SEHOP is turned on and properly configured)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25328400 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : SEHOP is turned on and properly configured\nCheck Existence         : All collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25328400 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Session Manager\\kernel'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisableExceptionChainValidation'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Session Manager\\kernel'\n                        : name equals 'DisableExceptionChainValidation'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134054533750000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","rule_title":"Structured Exception Handling Overwrite Protection (SEHOP) must be enabled.","security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"Attackers are constantly looking for vulnerabilities in systems and applications. Structured Exception Handling Overwrite Protection (SEHOP) blocks exploits that use the Structured Exception Handling overwrite technique, a common buffer overflow attack.","mitigations":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","group_id":"V-253284","potential_impacts":"","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253284","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; MS Security Guide &gt;&gt; \"Enable Structured Exception Handling Overwrite Protection (SEHOP)\" to \"Enabled\".\n\nThis policy setting requires the installation of the SecGuide custom templates included with the STIG package. \"SecGuide.admx\" and \"SecGuide.adml\" must be copied to the \\Windows\\PolicyDefinitions and \\Windows\\PolicyDefinitions\\en-US directories respectively.","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"366FA6C3-6BF8-1014-A8A2-BF5BFE070BEF","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253284","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"check_content":"Verify SEHOP is turned on.\n\nIf the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Session Manager\\kernel\\\n\nValue Name: DisableExceptionChainValidation\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000000 (0)","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253284r958928_rule","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253284r958928","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253284","title":"SRG-OS-000433-GPOS-00192"},"rule_version":"WN11-00-000150","group_title":"SRG-OS-000433-GPOS-00192","severity":"high","ccis":["CCI-002824"]},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The Windows PowerShell 2.0 feature must be disabled on the system.","discussion":"Windows PowerShell 5.0 added advanced logging features, which can provide additional detail when malware has been run on a system. Disabling the Windows PowerShell 2.0 mitigates against a downgrade attack that evades the Windows PowerShell 5.0 script block logging feature.","mitigations":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253285","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253285","fix_text":"Disable \"Windows PowerShell 2.0\" on the system.\n\nRun \"Windows PowerShell\" with elevated privileges (run as administrator).\nEnter the following:\nDisable-WindowsOptionalFeature -Online -FeatureName MicrosoftWindowsPowerShellV2Root\n\nThis command must disable both \"MicrosoftWindowsPowerShellV2Root\" and \"MicrosoftWindowsPowerShellV2\", which correspond to \"Windows PowerShell 2.0\" and \"Windows PowerShell 2.0 Engine\" respectively in \"Turn Windows features on or off\".\n\nAlternately:\nSearch for \"Features\".\nSelect \"Turn Windows features on or off\".\nDe-select \"Windows PowerShell 2.0\".","status":"not_applicable","uuid":"366FAF26-6BF8-1014-995B-D7C992A8D245","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253285"},"ia_controls":"","check_content":"For Windows 11 version 24H2 and newer, this requirement is Not Applicable.\n\nRun \"Windows PowerShell\" with elevated privileges (run as administrator).\n\nEnter the following:\nGet-WindowsOptionalFeature -Online | Where FeatureName -like *PowerShellv2*\n\nIf either of the following have a \"State\" of \"Enabled\", this is a finding.\n\nFeatureName : MicrosoftWindowsPowerShellV2\nState : Enabled\nFeatureName : MicrosoftWindowsPowerShellV2Root\nState : Enabled\n\nAlternately:\nSearch for \"Features\".\n\nSelect \"Turn Windows features on or off\".\n\nIf \"Windows PowerShell 2.0\" (whether the subcategory of \"Windows PowerShell 2.0 Engine\" is selected or not) is selected, this is a finding.","rule_id_src":"SV-253285r1153425_rule","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253285r1153425","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253285","title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049"},"rule_version":"WN11-00-000155","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-000381"]},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nCriteria                :     true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :       true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nTest                    :         false ('SMB 1.0/CIFS File Sharing Support' feature is not installed)\nTest                    :         true ('Configure SMBv1 Server' is set to 'Disabled')\nCriteria                :       true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nTest                    :         false ('SMB 1.0/CIFS File Sharing Support' feature is not installed)\nTest                    :         true ('Configure SMBv1 client driver' is set to 'Enabled' with 'Disable driver (recommended)' selected for 'Configure MrxSmb10 driver')\nTest                    :     false ('SMB 1.0/CIFS File Sharing Support' feature is not installed)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25328600 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : 'SMB 1.0/CIFS File Sharing Support' feature is not installed\nCheck Existence         : All collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25328600 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT installstate FROM win32_optionalfeature WHERE name = 'SMB1Protocol''\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25328600 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : Check SMB v1 Protocol Win32_OptionalFeature object InstallState is equal to 2\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : at least one installstate must be equal to '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT installstate FROM win32_optionalfeature WHERE name = 'SMB1Protocol''\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : installstate = '1'\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25328700 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Configure SMBv1 Server' is set to 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25328700 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\LanmanServer\\Parameters'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'SMB1'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\LanmanServer\\Parameters'\n                        : name equals 'SMB1'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995390000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25328800 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Configure SMBv1 client driver' is set to 'Enabled' with 'Disable driver (recommended)' selected for 'Configure MrxSmb10 driver'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25328800 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\mrxsmb10'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'Start'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000004 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Reg_Dword type and value equals 4\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '4'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\mrxsmb10'\n                        : name equals 'Start'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134054533750000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '4'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","discussion":"SMBv1 is a legacy protocol that uses the MD5 algorithm as part of SMB. MD5 is known to be vulnerable to a number of attacks such as collision and preimage attacks as well as not being FIPS compliant.\n\nDisabling SMBv1 support may prevent access to file or print sharing resources with systems or devices that only support SMBv1. File shares and print services hosted on Windows Server 2003 are an example, however Windows Server 2003 is no longer a supported operating system. Some older Network Attached Storage (NAS) devices may only support SMBv1.","mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The Server Message Block (SMB) v1 protocol must be disabled on the system.","fix_text":"Disable the SMBv1 protocol.\n\nRun \"Windows PowerShell\" with elevated privileges (run as administrator).\n\nEnter the following:\nDisable-WindowsOptionalFeature -Online -FeatureName SMB1Protocol\n\nAlternately:\nSearch for \"Features\".\n\nSelect \"Turn Windows features on or off\".\n\nDe-select \"SMB 1.0/CIFS File Sharing Support\".","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253286","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253286","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253286","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"uuid":"366FB6F9-6BF8-1014-9CC5-A50B184BD2D1","status":"not_a_finding","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253286r958478","check_content":"Different methods are available to disable SMBv1 on Windows 11. This is the preferred method, however if WN11-00-000165 and WN11-00-000170 are configured, this is NA.\n\nRun \"Windows PowerShell\" with elevated privileges (run as administrator).\n\nEnter the following:\nGet-WindowsOptionalFeature -Online | Where FeatureName -eq SMB1Protocol\n\nIf \"State : Enabled\" is returned, this is a finding.\n\nAlternately:\nSearch for \"Features\".\n\nSelect \"Turn Windows features on or off\".\n\nIf \"SMB 1.0/CIFS File Sharing Support\" is selected, this is a finding.","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253286r958478_rule","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","id":"V-253286"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","rule_version":"WN11-00-000160","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","severity":"medium"},{"security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The Server Message Block (SMB) v1 protocol must be disabled on the SMB server.","mitigations":"","discussion":"SMBv1 is a legacy protocol that uses the MD5 algorithm as part of SMB. MD5 is known to be vulnerable to a number of attacks such as collision and preimage attacks as well as not being FIPS compliant.\n\nDisabling SMBv1 support may prevent access to file or print sharing resources with systems or devices that only support SMBv1. File shares and print services hosted on Windows Server 2003 are an example, however Windows Server 2003 is no longer a supported operating system. Some older network attached devices may only support SMBv1.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nTest                    :     false ('SMB 1.0/CIFS File Sharing Support' feature is not installed)\nTest                    :     true ('Configure SMBv1 Server' is set to 'Disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25328600 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : 'SMB 1.0/CIFS File Sharing Support' feature is not installed\nCheck Existence         : All collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25328600 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT installstate FROM win32_optionalfeature WHERE name = 'SMB1Protocol''\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25328600 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : Check SMB v1 Protocol Win32_OptionalFeature object InstallState is equal to 2\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : at least one installstate must be equal to '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT installstate FROM win32_optionalfeature WHERE name = 'SMB1Protocol''\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : installstate = '1'\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25328700 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Configure SMBv1 Server' is set to 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25328700 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\LanmanServer\\Parameters'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'SMB1'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\LanmanServer\\Parameters'\n                        : name equals 'SMB1'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995390000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"366FBF98-6BF8-1014-ADB6-D8D452512FE5","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253287","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253287","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253287","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; MS Security Guide &gt;&gt; \"Configure SMBv1 Server\" to \"Disabled\".\n\nThis policy setting requires the installation of the SecGuide custom templates included with the STIG package. \"SecGuide.admx\" and \"SecGuide.adml\" must be copied to the \\Windows\\PolicyDefinitions and \\Windows\\PolicyDefinitions\\en-US directories, respectively.  \n\nThe system must be restarted for the change to take effect.","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"id":"V-253287","title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049"},"reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253287r958478_rule","check_content":"Different methods are available to disable SMBv1 on Windows 11, if WN11-00-000160 is configured, this is NA.\n\nIf the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\LanmanServer\\Parameters\\\n\nValue Name: SMB1\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000000 (0)","ia_controls":"","rule_id":"SV-253287r958478","mitigation_control":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"rule_version":"WN11-00-000165"},{"documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"id":"V-253288","title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049"},"reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253288r958478_rule","check_content":"Different methods are available to disable SMBv1 on Windows 11, if WN11-00-000160is configured, this is NA.\n\nIf the following registry value is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\mrxsmb10\\\n\nValue Name: Start\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000004 (4)","ia_controls":"","rule_id":"SV-253288r958478","mitigation_control":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"rule_version":"WN11-00-000170","rule_title":"The Server Message Block (SMB) v1 protocol must be disabled on the SMB client.","security_override_guidance":"","mitigations":"","discussion":"SMBv1 is a legacy protocol that uses the MD5 algorithm as part of SMB. MD5 is known to be vulnerable to a number of attacks such as collision and preimage attacks as well as not being FIPS compliant.\n\nDisabling SMBv1 support may prevent access to file or print sharing resources with systems or devices that only support SMBv1. File shares and print services hosted on Windows Server 2003 are an example, however Windows Server 2003 is no longer a supported operating system. Some older network attached devices may only support SMBv1.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nTest                    :     false ('SMB 1.0/CIFS File Sharing Support' feature is not installed)\nTest                    :     true ('Configure SMBv1 client driver' is set to 'Enabled' with 'Disable driver (recommended)' selected for 'Configure MrxSmb10 driver')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25328600 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : 'SMB 1.0/CIFS File Sharing Support' feature is not installed\nCheck Existence         : All collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25328600 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT installstate FROM win32_optionalfeature WHERE name = 'SMB1Protocol''\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25328600 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : Check SMB v1 Protocol Win32_OptionalFeature object InstallState is equal to 2\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : at least one installstate must be equal to '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT installstate FROM win32_optionalfeature WHERE name = 'SMB1Protocol''\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : installstate = '1'\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25328800 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Configure SMBv1 client driver' is set to 'Enabled' with 'Disable driver (recommended)' selected for 'Configure MrxSmb10 driver'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25328800 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\mrxsmb10'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'Start'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000004 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Reg_Dword type and value equals 4\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '4'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\mrxsmb10'\n                        : name equals 'Start'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134054533750000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '4'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"366FC772-6BF8-1014-958B-F38B4331EF9A","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253288"},"group_id":"V-253288","potential_impacts":"","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253288","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; MS Security Guide &gt;&gt; \"Configure SMBv1 client driver\" to \"Enabled\" with \"Disable driver (recommended)\" selected for \"Configure MrxSmb10 driver\".\n\nThis policy setting requires the installation of the SecGuide custom templates included with the STIG package. \"SecGuide.admx\" and \"SecGuide.adml\" must be copied to the \\Windows\\PolicyDefinitions and \\Windows\\PolicyDefinitions\\en-US directories, respectively.  \n\nThe system must be restarted for the changes to take effect."},{"rule_version":"WN11-00-000175","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"ia_controls":"","check_content":"Run \"Services.msc\".\n\nLocate the \"Secondary Logon\" service.\n\nIf the \"Startup Type\" is not \"Disabled\" or the \"Status\" is \"Running\", this is a finding.","rule_id_src":"SV-253289r958478_rule","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253289r958478","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","id":"V-253289"},"group_id":"V-253289","potential_impacts":"","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253289","fix_text":"Configure the \"Secondary Logon\" service \"Startup Type\" to \"Disabled\".","status":"open","uuid":"366FCFC6-6BF8-1014-8983-904081D6A90B","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253289","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     false (The Secondary Logon service Startup Type is Disabled or the service is uninstalled)\nResult Analysis         :          startmode = 'Manual' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'Disabled' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25328900 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : The Secondary Logon service Startup Type is Disabled or the service is uninstalled\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : At least one collected item must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25328900 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : Secondary Logon Service Startup Type\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT startmode FROM Win32_Service WHERE name='seclogon''\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25328900 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : Service Startup Type is Disabled\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all startmode must be equal to 'Disabled'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT startmode FROM Win32_Service WHERE name='seclogon''\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : !![ startmode = 'Manual' ]!!\n\nResult Analysis         : startmode = 'Manual' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'Disabled' \n","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The Secondary Logon service must be disabled on Windows 11.","discussion":"The Secondary Logon service provides a means for entering alternate credentials, typically used to run commands with elevated privileges. Using privileged credentials in a standard user session can expose those credentials to theft.","mitigations":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4"},{"group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"rule_version":"WN11-00-000190","weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253290","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"check_content":"Review the effective User Rights setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nReview each User Right listed for any unresolved SIDs to determine whether they are valid, such as due to being temporarily disconnected from the domain. (Unresolved SIDs have the format of \"*S-1-..\".)\n\nIf any unresolved SIDs exist and are not for currently valid accounts or groups, this is a finding.","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253290r991589_rule","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253290r991589","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"366FD7CB-6BF8-1014-B8E4-A86FA26C3386","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:253290"},"potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253290","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253290","fix_text":"Remove any unresolved SIDs found in User Rights assignments and determined to not be for currently valid accounts or groups by removing the accounts or groups from the appropriate group policy.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Orphaned security identifiers (SIDs) must be removed from user rights on Windows 11.","discussion":"Accounts or groups given rights on a system may show up as unresolved SIDs for various reasons including deletion of the accounts or groups. If the account or group objects are reanimated, there is a potential they may still have rights no longer intended. Valid domain accounts or groups may also show up as unresolved SIDs if a connection to the domain cannot be established for some reason.","mitigations":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Orphaned security identifiers (SIDs) must be removed from user rights.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25329001 (userright_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Orphaned security identifiers (SIDs) must be removed from user rights.\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25329001 (userright_object)\nObject Comment          : Gather all User Rights. Only include orphaned SIDs.\nObject Requirement      : for userright, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_ASSIGNPRIMARYTOKEN_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_AUDIT_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_BACKUP_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_CHANGE_NOTIFY_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_CREATE_GLOBAL_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_CREATE_PAGEFILE_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_CREATE_PERMANENT_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_CREATE_SYMBOLIC_LINK_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_CREATE_TOKEN_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_DEBUG_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_ENABLE_DELEGATION_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_IMPERSONATE_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_INC_BASE_PRIORITY_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_INCREASE_QUOTA_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_INC_WORKING_SET_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_LOAD_DRIVER_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_LOCK_MEMORY_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_MACHINE_ACCOUNT_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_MANAGE_VOLUME_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_PROF_SINGLE_PROCESS_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_RELABEL_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_REMOTE_SHUTDOWN_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_RESTORE_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_SECURITY_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_SHUTDOWN_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_SYNC_AGENT_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_SYSTEM_ENVIRONMENT_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_SYSTEM_PROFILE_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_SYSTEMTIME_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_TAKE_OWNERSHIP_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_TCB_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_TIME_ZONE_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_TRUSTED_CREDMAN_ACCESS_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_UNDOCK_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_UNSOLICITED_INPUT_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_BATCH_LOGON_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_DENY_BATCH_LOGON_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_DENY_INTERACTIVE_LOGON_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_DENY_NETWORK_LOGON_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_DENY_REMOTE_INTERACTIVE_LOGON_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_DENY_SERVICE_LOGON_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_INTERACTIVE_LOGON_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_NETWORK_LOGON_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_REMOTE_INTERACTIVE_LOGON_NAME'\nObject Requirement      :     userright must be equal to 'SE_SERVICE_LOGON_NAME'\nInclude Items If        : trustee_name matches the pattern '^$'\nInclude Items If        : trustee_sid matches the pattern '^S-'\n"},{"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"rule_version":"WN11-00-000210","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"id":"V-253291","title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049"},"third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253291r1153422_rule","check_content":"This is NA if the system does not have Bluetooth.\n\nVerify the Bluetooth radio is turned off unless approved by the organization. If it is not, this is a finding.\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\PolicyManager\\current\\device\\Connectivity\\\n\nValue Name: AllowBluetooth\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000000 (0)\n\nApproval must be documented with the ISSO.","ia_controls":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id":"SV-253291r1153422","mitigation_control":"","status":"not_applicable","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:253291","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml"},"uuid":"366FDFA5-6BF8-1014-9FD5-E16CC98EB37A","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253291","group_id":"V-253291","potential_impacts":"","fix_text":"Turn off Bluetooth radios not organizationally approved.\n\nFor systems managed by Intune, apply the DOD Windows 11 STIG Settings Catalog (or equivalent Intune policy) found in the Intune policy package available on cyber.mil.\nSteps to create an Intune policy:\n1. Sign in to the Intune admin center &gt;&gt; Devices &gt;&gt; Configuration &gt;&gt; Create &gt;&gt; New Policy.\n2. Platform: Windows 10 and later. Profile type: Settings Catalog, then click \"Create\".\n3. Basics: Provide a Name and Description of the profile, then click \"Next\".\n4. Configuration settings: Click \"+ Add settings\" and search for connectivity under the Settings picker. Under the Connectivity category, check the box next to Allow Bluetooth setting. Choose the first option, \"Disallow Bluetooth\", then click \"Next\".\n5. Scope tags: (optional), then click \"Next\".\n6. Assignments: Assign the policy to Entra security groups that contain the target users or devices, then click \"Next\".\n7. Review + create: Review the deployment summary, then click \"Create\".","mitigations":"","discussion":"If not configured properly, Bluetooth may allow rogue devices to communicate with a system. If a rogue device is paired with a system, there is potential for sensitive information to be compromised.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Bluetooth must be turned off unless approved by the organization.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n"},{"uuid":"366FE9AE-6BF8-1014-86F3-96DB230DF9C4","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:253293"},"status":"not_applicable","fix_text":"Configure Bluetooth to notify users if devices attempt to connect.\nView Bluetooth Settings.\nEnsure \"Alert me when a new Bluetooth device wants to connect\" is checked.","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253293","group_id_src":"V-253293","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The system must notify the user when a Bluetooth device attempts to connect.","discussion":"If not configured properly, Bluetooth may allow rogue devices to communicate with a system. If a rogue device is paired with a system, there is potential for sensitive information to be compromised.","mitigations":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","severity":"medium","rule_version":"WN11-00-000230","third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-253293"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253293r991589","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"check_content":"This is NA if the system does not have Bluetooth, or if Bluetooth is turned off per the organizations policy.\n\nSearch for \"Bluetooth\".\nView Bluetooth Settings.\nSelect \"More Bluetooth Options\"\nIf \"Alert me when a new Bluetooth device wants to connect\" is not checked, this is a finding.","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253293r991589_rule"},{"stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","mitigations":"","discussion":"Using applications that access the internet or have potential internet sources using administrative privileges exposes a system to compromise. If a flaw in an application is exploited while running as a privileged user, the entire system could be compromised. Web browsers and email are common attack vectors for introducing malicious code and must not be run with an administrative account.\n\nSince administrative accounts may generally change or work around technical restrictions for running a web browser or other applications, it is essential that policy requires administrative accounts to not access the internet or use applications, such as email.\n\nThe policy must define specific exceptions for local service administration. These exceptions may include HTTP(S)-based tools that are used for the administration of the local system, services, or attached devices.\n\nTechnical means such as application allowlisting can be used to enforce the policy to ensure compliance.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Administrative accounts must not be used with applications that access the internet, such as web browsers, or with potential internet sources, such as email.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT I, V-253294, SV-253294r991589, SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227)\n","check_content_ref":{"name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows11:questionnaire:7501","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-ocil.xml"},"uuid":"366FF0B6-6BF8-1014-8C38-F55C1A03DE6F","status":"not_reviewed","fix_text":"Establish and enforce a policy that prohibits administrative accounts from using applications that access the internet, such as web browsers, or with potential internet sources, such as email. Define specific exceptions for local service administration. These exceptions may include HTTP(S)-based tools that are used for the administration of the local system, services, or attached devices.\n\nImplement technical measures where feasible such as removal of applications or use of application allowlisting to restrict the use of applications that can access the internet.","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253294","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253294","group_tree":{"id":"V-253294","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id":"SV-253294r991589","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253294r991589_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"Determine whether administrative accounts are prevented from using applications that access the internet, such as web browsers, or with potential internet sources, such as email, except as necessary for local service administration.\n\nThe organization must have a policy that prohibits administrative accounts from using applications that access the internet, such as web browsers, or with potential internet sources, such as email, except as necessary for local service administration. The policy must define specific exceptions for local service administration. These exceptions may include HTTP(S)-based tools that are used for the administration of the local system, services, or attached devices.\n\nTechnical measures such as the removal of applications or application allowlisting must be used where feasible to prevent the use of applications that access the internet. \n\nIf accounts with administrative privileges are not prevented from using applications that access the internet or with potential internet sources, this is a finding.","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"severity":"high","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","rule_version":"WN11-00-000240"},{"discussion":"For virtual desktop implementations (VDIs) where the virtual desktop instance is deleted or refreshed upon logoff, the organization must enforce that sessions be terminated within 24 hours. This would ensure any data stored on the VM that is not encrypted or covered by Credential Guard is deleted.","mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows 11 nonpersistent VM sessions must not exceed 24 hours.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT II, V-253295, SV-253295r958552, SRG-OS-000185-GPOS-00079)\n","status":"not_reviewed","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows11:questionnaire:7701"},"uuid":"366FF77D-6BF8-1014-A13F-8FEBAA92DC30","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253295","group_id":"V-253295","potential_impacts":"","fix_text":"Set nonpersistent VM sessions to not exceed 24 hours.","weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000185-GPOS-00079","id":"V-253295"},"ia_controls":"","check_content":"Verify there is a documented policy or procedure in place that nonpersistent VM sessions do not exceed 24 hours.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  \n\nIf the system is NOT a nonpersistent VM, this is Not Applicable. \n\nFor Azure Virtual Desktop (AVD) implementations with no data at rest, this is Not Applicable.\n\nIf there is no such documented policy or procedure in place, this is a finding.","rule_id_src":"SV-253295r958552_rule","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253295r958552","group_title":"SRG-OS-000185-GPOS-00079","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-001199"],"rule_version":"WN11-00-000250"},{"documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"id":"V-253296","title":"SRG-OS-000355-GPOS-00143"},"responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253296r1051041_rule","check_content":"Review the Windows time service configuration.\n\nOpen an elevated \"Command Prompt\" (run as administrator).\n\nEnter \"W32tm /query /configuration\".\n\nDomain-joined systems (excluding the domain controller with the PDC emulator role):\n\nIf the value for \"Type\" under \"NTP Client\" is not \"NT5DS\", this is a finding.","ia_controls":"","rule_id":"SV-253296r1051041","mitigation_control":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"severity":"low","group_title":"SRG-OS-000355-GPOS-00143","ccis":["CCI-004923","CCI-001891"],"rule_version":"WN11-00-000260","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The Windows 11 time service must synchronize with an appropriate DOD time source.","mitigations":"","discussion":"The Windows Time Service controls time synchronization settings. Time synchronization is essential for authentication and auditing purposes. If the Windows Time Service is used, it must synchronize with a secure, authorized time source. Domain-joined systems are automatically configured to synchronize with domain controllers. If an NTP server is configured, it must synchronize with a secure, authorized time source.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Review the Windows time service configuration via PowerShell)\nResult Analysis         :        'Type: NTP (Local)' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'NT5DS' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25329601 (shellcommand_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Review the Windows time service configuration via PowerShell\nCheck Existence         : One and only one collected item may exist.\nCheck                   : One and only one item may match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25329601 (shellcommand_object)\nObject Comment          : Review the Windows time service configuration via PowerShell\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'shell' must be equal to 'powershell'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'command' must be equal to 'W32tm /query /configuration'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'pattern' must be equal to '^Type:'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25329601 (shellcommand_state)\nState Comment           : Confirm ExitStatus is 0 and stdout is NT5DS\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'command' must be equal to 'W32tm /query /configuration'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'pattern' must be equal to '^Type:'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'exit_status' must be equal to '0'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'stdout_line' must match the pattern 'NT5DS'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : shell equals 'powershell'\n                        : command equals 'W32tm /query /configuration'\n                        : pattern equals '^Type:'\n                        : exit_status equals '0'\n                        : stdout_line equals 'Type: NTP (Local)'\n\nResult Analysis         : 'Type: NTP (Local)' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to 'NT5DS' \n","status":"open","uuid":"366FFE49-6BF8-1014-B592-D8B808590CDF","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:253296"},"potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253296","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253296","fix_text":"Configure the system to synchronize time with an appropriate DOD time source.\n\nDomain-joined systems use NT5DS to synchronize time from other systems in the domain by default.\n\nIf the system needs to be configured to an NTP server, configure the system to point to an authorized time server by setting the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; System &gt;&gt; Windows Time Service &gt;&gt; Time Providers &gt;&gt; \"Configure Windows NTP Client\" to \"Enabled\", and configure the \"NtpServer\" field to point to an appropriate DOD time server.\n\nThe US Naval Observatory operates stratum 1 time servers, identified at https://www.cnmoc.usff.navy.mil/Our-Commands/United-States-Naval-Observatory/Precise-Time-Department/Network-Time-Protocol-NTP/. Time synchronization will occur through a hierarchy of time servers down to the local level. Clients and lower-level servers will synchronize with an authorized time server in the hierarchy."},{"stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","mitigations":"","discussion":"The account lockout feature, when enabled, prevents brute-force password attacks on the system. This parameter specifies the amount of time that an account will remain locked after the specified number of failed logon attempts.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows 11 account lockout duration must be configured to 15 minutes or greater.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :     true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nTest                    :       false ('Account lockout duration' is set to '0')\nTest                    :       true ('Account lockout duration' is set to '15 minutes' or greater)\nTest                    :     true ('Account lockout threshold' is not set to '0')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25329700 (lockoutpolicy_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : 'Account lockout duration' is set to '0'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\nState Operator          : One or more item-state comparisons may be true.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000001 (lockoutpolicy_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25329700 (lockoutpolicy_state)\nState Comment           : Lockout Duration equals -1\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'lockout_duration' must be less than or equal to '0'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25329701 (lockoutpolicy_state)\nState Comment           : Lockout Duration equals 4294967295\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'lockout_duration' must be equal to '4294967295'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : force_logoff equals '1'\n                        : lockout_duration equals '900'\n                        : lockout_observation_window equals '900'\n                        : lockout_threshold equals '3'\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25329701 (lockoutpolicy_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Account lockout duration' is set to '15 minutes' or greater\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000001 (lockoutpolicy_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25329702 (lockoutpolicy_state)\nState Comment           : Lockout Duration greater than or equals 900\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'lockout_duration' must be greater than or equal to '900'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : force_logoff equals '1'\n                        : lockout_duration equals '900'\n                        : lockout_observation_window equals '900'\n                        : lockout_threshold equals '3'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25329801 (lockoutpolicy_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Account lockout threshold' is not set to '0'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000001 (lockoutpolicy_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25329801 (lockoutpolicy_state)\nState Comment           : Lockout Threshold is greater than 0\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'lockout_threshold' must be greater than '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : force_logoff equals '1'\n                        : lockout_duration equals '900'\n                        : lockout_observation_window equals '900'\n                        : lockout_threshold equals '3'\n","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253297","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"uuid":"367004E3-6BF8-1014-B88F-9A199CCEC2B4","status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Account Lockout Policy &gt;&gt; \"Account lockout duration\" to \"15\" minutes or greater.\n\nA value of \"0\" is also acceptable, requiring an administrator to unlock the account.","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253297","group_id":"V-253297","potential_impacts":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000329-GPOS-00128","id":"V-253297"},"responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id":"SV-253297r958736","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253297r958736_rule","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Account Lockout Policy.\n\nIf the \"Account lockout duration\" is less than \"15\" minutes (excluding \"0\"), this is a finding.\n\nConfiguring this to \"0\", requiring an administrator to unlock the account, is more restrictive and is not a finding.","ia_controls":"","ccis":["CCI-002238"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000329-GPOS-00128","rule_version":"WN11-AC-000005"},{"fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Account Lockout Policy &gt;&gt; \"Account lockout threshold\" to \"3\" or less invalid logon attempts (excluding \"0\" which is unacceptable).","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253298","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253298","uuid":"36700B80-6BF8-1014-8128-DDE1EF03BD14","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253298"},"status":"not_a_finding","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Account lockout threshold' is set to '3' or less)\nTest                    :     true ('Account lockout threshold' is not set to '0')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25329800 (lockoutpolicy_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Account lockout threshold' is set to '3' or less\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000001 (lockoutpolicy_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25329800 (lockoutpolicy_state)\nState Comment           : Lockout Threshold is less than or equal to 3\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'lockout_threshold' must be less than or equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : force_logoff equals '1'\n                        : lockout_duration equals '900'\n                        : lockout_observation_window equals '900'\n                        : lockout_threshold equals '3'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25329801 (lockoutpolicy_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Account lockout threshold' is not set to '0'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000001 (lockoutpolicy_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25329801 (lockoutpolicy_state)\nState Comment           : Lockout Threshold is greater than 0\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'lockout_threshold' must be greater than '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : force_logoff equals '1'\n                        : lockout_duration equals '900'\n                        : lockout_observation_window equals '900'\n                        : lockout_threshold equals '3'\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The number of allowed bad logon attempts must be configured to three or less.","discussion":"The account lockout feature, when enabled, prevents brute-force password attacks on the system. The higher this value is, the less effective the account lockout feature will be in protecting the local system. The number of bad logon attempts must be reasonably small to minimize the possibility of a successful password attack, while allowing for honest errors made during a normal user logon.","mitigations":"","rule_version":"WN11-AC-000010","ccis":["CCI-000044"],"group_title":"SRG-OS-000021-GPOS-00005","severity":"medium","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253298r958388","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","ia_controls":"","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Account Lockout Policy.\n\nIf the \"Account lockout threshold\" is \"0\" or more than \"3\" attempts, this is a finding.","rule_id_src":"SV-253298r958388_rule","responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000021-GPOS-00005","id":"V-253298"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false"},{"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000021-GPOS-00005","id":"V-253299"},"reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","rule_id":"SV-253299r958388","mitigation_control":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id_src":"SV-253299r958388_rule","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Account Lockout Policy.\n\nIf the \"Reset account lockout counter after\" value is less than \"15\" minutes, this is a finding.","ia_controls":"","ccis":["CCI-000044"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000021-GPOS-00005","rule_version":"WN11-AC-000015","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The period of time before the bad logon counter is reset must be configured to 15 minutes.","mitigations":"","discussion":"The account lockout feature, when enabled, prevents brute-force password attacks on the system. This parameter specifies the period of time that must pass after failed logon attempts before the counter is reset to 0. The smaller this value is, the less effective the account lockout feature will be in protecting the local system.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Reset account lockout counter after' is set to at least the required value)\nTest                    :     true ('Account lockout threshold' is not set to '0')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25329900 (lockoutpolicy_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Reset account lockout counter after' is set to at least the required value\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000001 (lockoutpolicy_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25329900 (lockoutpolicy_state)\nState Comment           : Lockout Observation Window is greater than or equal to variable\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'lockout_observation_window' must be greater than or equal to '900'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : force_logoff equals '1'\n                        : lockout_duration equals '900'\n                        : lockout_observation_window equals '900'\n                        : lockout_threshold equals '3'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25329801 (lockoutpolicy_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Account lockout threshold' is not set to '0'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000001 (lockoutpolicy_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25329801 (lockoutpolicy_state)\nState Comment           : Lockout Threshold is greater than 0\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'lockout_threshold' must be greater than '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : force_logoff equals '1'\n                        : lockout_duration equals '900'\n                        : lockout_observation_window equals '900'\n                        : lockout_threshold equals '3'\n","uuid":"3670125C-6BF8-1014-BE61-A7033B3EBD57","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253299"},"status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Account Lockout Policy &gt;&gt; \"Reset account lockout counter after\" to \"15\" minutes.","group_id":"V-253299","potential_impacts":"","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253299"},{"group_id_src":"V-253300","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id":"V-253300","potential_impacts":"","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Password Policy &gt;&gt; \"Enforce password history\" to \"24\" passwords remembered.","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253300","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"uuid":"36701942-6BF8-1014-9E9E-BDCD6B0311BD","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Enforce password history' is set to '24' passwords or more)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25330000 (passwordpolicy_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Enforce password history' is set to '24' passwords or more\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000002 (passwordpolicy_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25330000 (passwordpolicy_state)\nState Comment           : Password History Length is greater than or equal to variable\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'password_hist_len' must be greater than or equal to '24'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : max_passwd_age equals '5184000'\n                        : min_passwd_age equals '86400'\n                        : min_passwd_len equals '14'\n                        : password_hist_len equals '24'\n                        : password_complexity equals '1'\n                        : reversible_encryption equals '0'\n                        : anonymous_name_lookup equals '0'\n","mitigations":"","discussion":"A system is more vulnerable to unauthorized access when system users recycle the same password several times without being required to change a password to a unique password on a regularly scheduled basis. This enables users to effectively negate the purpose of mandating periodic password changes. The default value is 24 for Windows domain systems. DOD has decided this is the appropriate value for all Windows systems.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The password history must be configured to 24 passwords remembered.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","rule_version":"WN11-AC-000020","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000077-GPOS-00045","ccis":["CCI-004061"],"rule_id_src":"SV-253300r1000103_rule","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Password Policy.\n\nIf the value for \"Enforce password history\" is less than \"24\" passwords remembered, this is a finding.","ia_controls":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id":"SV-253300r1000103","mitigation_control":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000077-GPOS-00045","id":"V-253300"},"reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":""},{"rule_version":"WN11-AC-000025","ccis":["CCI-004066","CCI-000199"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000076-GPOS-00044","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id":"SV-253301r1051042","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253301r1051042_rule","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Password Policy.\n\nIf the value for the \"Maximum password age\" is greater than \"60\" days, this is a finding. If the value is set to \"0\" (never expires), this is a finding.","ia_controls":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253301","title":"SRG-OS-000076-GPOS-00044"},"responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Password Policy &gt;&gt; \"Maximum Password Age\" to \"60\" days or less (excluding \"0\" which is unacceptable).","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253301","group_id":"V-253301","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253301"},"uuid":"36701FFE-6BF8-1014-9F5B-9422C995778D","status":"not_a_finding","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Maximum Password Age is set to 60 days or less, but greater than 0.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25330100 (passwordpolicy_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Maximum Password Age is set to 60 days or less, but greater than 0.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\nState Operator          : All item-state comparisons must be true.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000002 (passwordpolicy_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25330100 (passwordpolicy_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'max_passwd_age' must be less than or equal to '5184000'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25330101 (passwordpolicy_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'max_passwd_age' must be greater than '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : max_passwd_age equals '5184000'\n                        : min_passwd_age equals '86400'\n                        : min_passwd_len equals '14'\n                        : password_hist_len equals '24'\n                        : password_complexity equals '1'\n                        : reversible_encryption equals '0'\n                        : anonymous_name_lookup equals '0'\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","mitigations":"","discussion":"The longer a password is in use, the greater the opportunity for someone to gain unauthorized knowledge of the passwords. Scheduled changing of passwords hinders the ability of unauthorized system users to crack passwords and gain access to a system.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The maximum password age must be configured to 60 days or less."},{"rule_id":"SV-253302r1051043","mitigation_control":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id_src":"SV-253302r1051043_rule","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Password Policy.\n\nIf the value for the \"Minimum password age\" is less than \"1\" day, this is a finding.","ia_controls":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000075-GPOS-00043","id":"V-253302"},"responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN11-AC-000030","ccis":["CCI-004066","CCI-000198"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000075-GPOS-00043","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Minimum Password Age' is set to at least '1' day)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25330200 (passwordpolicy_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Minimum Password Age' is set to at least '1' day\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000002 (passwordpolicy_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25330200 (passwordpolicy_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'min_passwd_age' must be greater than or equal to '86400'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : max_passwd_age equals '5184000'\n                        : min_passwd_age equals '86400'\n                        : min_passwd_len equals '14'\n                        : password_hist_len equals '24'\n                        : password_complexity equals '1'\n                        : reversible_encryption equals '0'\n                        : anonymous_name_lookup equals '0'\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The minimum password age must be configured to at least 1 day.","mitigations":"","discussion":"Permitting passwords to be changed in immediate succession within the same day allows users to cycle passwords through their history database. This enables users to effectively negate the purpose of mandating periodic password changes.","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Password Policy &gt;&gt; \"Minimum Password Age\" to at least \"1\" day.","group_id":"V-253302","potential_impacts":"","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253302","uuid":"36702709-6BF8-1014-BD32-8FFA0965C23C","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253302"},"status":"not_a_finding"},{"third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253303","title":"SRG-OS-000078-GPOS-00046"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253303r1051044","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Password Policy.\n\nIf the value for the \"Minimum password length,\" is less than \"14\" characters, this is a finding.","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253303r1051044_rule","ccis":["CCI-004066","CCI-000205"],"group_title":"SRG-OS-000078-GPOS-00046","severity":"medium","rule_version":"WN11-AC-000035","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Passwords must, at a minimum, be 14 characters.","discussion":"Information systems not protected with strong password schemes (including passwords of minimum length) provide the opportunity for anyone to crack the password, thus gaining access to the system and compromising the device, information, or the local network.","mitigations":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Minimum password length' is set to at least '14' characters)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25330300 (passwordpolicy_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Minimum password length' is set to at least '14' characters\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000002 (passwordpolicy_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25330300 (passwordpolicy_state)\nState Comment           : Minimum Password Length is greater than or equal to 14\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'min_passwd_len' must be greater than or equal to '14'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : max_passwd_age equals '5184000'\n                        : min_passwd_age equals '86400'\n                        : min_passwd_len equals '14'\n                        : password_hist_len equals '24'\n                        : password_complexity equals '1'\n                        : reversible_encryption equals '0'\n                        : anonymous_name_lookup equals '0'\n","uuid":"36702DF9-6BF8-1014-B638-D2960A0FAB3D","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253303"},"status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Password Policy &gt;&gt; \"Minimum password length\" to \"14\" characters.","group_id":"V-253303","potential_impacts":"","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253303"},{"group_id":"V-253304","potential_impacts":"","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253304","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Password Policy &gt;&gt; \"Password must meet complexity requirements\" to \"Enabled\".","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"367039BE-6BF8-1014-BB79-B8E4073EC036","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253304","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Password must meet complexity requirements' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25330400 (passwordpolicy_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Password must meet complexity requirements' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000002 (passwordpolicy_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25330400 (passwordpolicy_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'password_complexity' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : max_passwd_age equals '5184000'\n                        : min_passwd_age equals '86400'\n                        : min_passwd_len equals '14'\n                        : password_hist_len equals '24'\n                        : password_complexity equals '1'\n                        : reversible_encryption equals '0'\n                        : anonymous_name_lookup equals '0'\n","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The built-in Microsoft password complexity filter must be enabled.","discussion":"The use of complex passwords increases their strength against guessing and brute-force attacks. This setting configures the system to verify that newly created passwords conform to the Windows password complexity policy.","mitigations":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","rule_version":"WN11-AC-000040","group_title":"SRG-OS-000069-GPOS-00037","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-004066","CCI-000192"],"ia_controls":"","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Password Policy.\n\nIf the value for \"Password must meet complexity requirements\" is not set to \"Enabled\", this is a finding.\n\nIf the site is using a password filter that requires this setting be set to \"Disabled\" for the filter to be used, this would not be considered a finding.","rule_id_src":"SV-253304r1051045_rule","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253304r1051045","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000069-GPOS-00037","id":"V-253304"}},{"ccis":["CCI-004062","CCI-000196"],"severity":"high","group_title":"SRG-OS-000073-GPOS-00041","rule_version":"WN11-AC-000045","group_tree":{"id":"V-253305","title":"SRG-OS-000073-GPOS-00041"},"third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id":"SV-253305r1051046","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253305r1051046_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Password Policy.\n\nIf the value for \"Store password using reversible encryption\" is not set to \"Disabled\", this is a finding.","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253305","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"uuid":"367044CC-6BF8-1014-A2EA-B93550130247","status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Account Policies &gt;&gt; Password Policy &gt;&gt; \"Store passwords using reversible encryption\" to \"Disabled\".","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253305","group_id":"V-253305","potential_impacts":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","mitigations":"","discussion":"Storing passwords using reversible encryption is essentially the same as storing clear-text versions of the passwords. For this reason, this policy must never be enabled.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Reversible password encryption must be disabled.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Store password using reversible encryption' is set to 'Disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25330500 (passwordpolicy_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Store password using reversible encryption' is set to 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000002 (passwordpolicy_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25330500 (passwordpolicy_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'reversible_encryption' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : max_passwd_age equals '5184000'\n                        : min_passwd_age equals '86400'\n                        : min_passwd_len equals '14'\n                        : password_hist_len equals '24'\n                        : password_complexity equals '1'\n                        : reversible_encryption equals '0'\n                        : anonymous_name_lookup equals '0'\n"},{"documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"id":"V-253306","title":"SRG-OS-000458-GPOS-00203"},"responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253306r991570_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"Security Option \"Audit: Force audit policy subcategory settings to override audit policy category settings\" must be set to \"Enabled\" (WN11-SO-000030) for the detailed auditing subcategories to be effective.\n\nUse the AuditPol tool to review the current Audit Policy configuration:\nOpen a Command Prompt with elevated privileges (\"Run as Administrator\").\nEnter \"AuditPol /get /category:*\".\n\nCompare the AuditPol settings with the following. If the system does not audit the following, this is a finding:\n\nAccount Logon &gt;&gt; Credential Validation - Failure","rule_id":"SV-253306r991570","mitigation_control":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000458-GPOS-00203","ccis":["CCI-000172"],"rule_version":"WN11-AU-000005","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The system must be configured to audit Account Logon - Credential Validation failures.","mitigations":"","discussion":"Maintaining an audit trail of system activity logs can help identify configuration errors, troubleshoot service disruptions, and analyze compromises that have occurred, as well as detect attacks. Audit logs are necessary to provide a trail of evidence in case the system or network is compromised. Collecting this data is essential for analyzing the security of information assets and detecting signs of suspicious and unexpected behavior.\n\nCredential validation records events related to validation tests on credentials for a user account logon.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResu