           : audit_policy_change equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : authentication_policy_change equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : authorization_policy_change equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : filtering_platform_policy_change equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : mpssvc_rule_level_policy_change equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n                        : other_policy_change_events equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n                        : non_sensitive_privilege_use equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : other_privilege_use_events equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : sensitive_privilege_use equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n                        : ipsec_driver equals 'AUDIT_FAILURE'\n                        : other_system_events equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n                        : security_state_change equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : security_system_extension equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : system_integrity equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n                        : group_membership equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : pnp_activity equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : user_device_claims equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : audit_detailedtracking_tokenrightadjusted equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","rule_title":"The system must be configured to audit Account Logon - Credential Validation successes.","security_override_guidance":"","mitigations":"","discussion":"Maintaining an audit trail of system activity logs can help identify configuration errors, troubleshoot service disruptions, and analyze compromises that have occurred, as well as detect attacks. Audit logs are necessary to provide a trail of evidence in case the system or network is compromised. Collecting this data is essential for analyzing the security of information assets and detecting signs of suspicious and unexpected behavior.\n\nCredential validation records events related to validation tests on credentials for a user account logon.","rule_version":"WN11-AU-000010","ccis":["CCI-000172"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000458-GPOS-00203","rule_id":"SV-253307r991570","mitigation_control":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id_src":"SV-253307r991570_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"Security Option \"Audit: Force audit policy subcategory settings to override audit policy category settings\" must be set to \"Enabled\" (WN11-SO-000030) for the detailed auditing subcategories to be effective.\n\nUse the AuditPol tool to review the current Audit Policy configuration:\nOpen a Command Prompt with elevated privileges (\"Run as Administrator\").\nEnter \"AuditPol /get /category:*\".\n\nCompare the AuditPol settings with the following. If the system does not audit the following, this is a finding:\n\nAccount Logon &gt;&gt; Credential Validation - Success","group_tree":{"id":"V-253307","title":"SRG-OS-000458-GPOS-00203"},"third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0"},{"status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253308"},"uuid":"367059C1-6BF8-1014-8191-C13EA47680C8","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253308","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253308","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Advanced Audit Policy Configuration &gt;&gt; System Audit Policies &gt;&gt; Account Management &gt;&gt; \"Audit Security Group Management\" with \"Success\" selected.","discussion":"Maintaining an audit trail of system activity logs can help identify configuration errors, troubleshoot service disruptions, and analyze compromises that have occurred, as well as detect attacks. Audit logs are necessary to provide a trail of evidence in case the system or network is compromised. Collecting this data is essential for analyzing the security of information assets and detecting signs of suspicious and unexpected behavior.\n\nSecurity Group Management records events such as creating, deleting or changing of security groups, including changes in group members.","mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The system must be configured to audit Account Management - Security Group Management successes.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Audit Security Group Management' is set to 'Success' or 'Success and Failure')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25330800 (auditeventpolicysubcategories_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Audit Security Group Management' is set to 'Success' or 'Success and Failure'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\nState Operator          : One or more item-state comparisons may be true.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000000 (auditeventpolicysubcategories_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25330800 (auditeventpolicysubcategories_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'security_group_management' must be equal to 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25330801 (auditeventpolicysubcategories_s