s 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : filtering_platform_connection equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : filtering_platform_packet_drop equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : handle_manipulation equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : kernel_object equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : other_object_access_events equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n                        : registry equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : sam equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : removable_storage equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n                        : central_access_policy_staging equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : audit_policy_change equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : authentication_policy_change equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : authorization_policy_change equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : filtering_platform_policy_change equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : mpssvc_rule_level_policy_change equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n                        : other_policy_change_events equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n                        : non_sensitive_privilege_use equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : other_privilege_use_events equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : sensitive_privilege_use equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n                        : ipsec_driver equals 'AUDIT_FAILURE'\n                        : other_system_events equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n                        : security_state_change equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : security_system_extension equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : system_integrity equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n                        : group_membership equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : pnp_activity equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : user_device_claims equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : audit_detailedtracking_tokenrightadjusted equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n","mitigations":"","discussion":"Maintaining an audit trail of system activity logs can help identify configuration errors, troubleshoot service disruptions, and analyze compromises that have occurred, as well as detect attacks. Audit logs are necessary to provide a trail of evidence in case the system or network is compromised. Collecting this data is essential for analyzing the security of information assets and detecting signs of suspicious and unexpected behavior.\n\nSystem Integrity records events related to violations of integrity to the security subsystem.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The system must be configured to audit System - System Integrity failures.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253335","false_positives":"","group_id":"V-253335","potential_impacts":"","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Advanced Audit Policy Configuration &gt;&gt; System Audit Policies &gt;&gt; System &gt;&gt; \"Audit System Integrity\" with \"Failure\" selected.","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253335","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"uuid":"3671330A-6BF8-1014-B6EC-EFAF4FB0BCE4","rule_id_src":"SV-253335r991573_rule","check_content":"Security Option \"Audit: Force audit policy subcategory settings to override audit policy category settings\" must be set to \"Enabled\" (WN11-SO-000030) for the detailed auditing subcategories to be effective.\n\nUse the AuditPol tool to review the current Audit Policy configuration:\nOpen a Command Prompt with elevated privileges (\"Run as Administrator\").\nEnter \"AuditPol /get /category:*\".\n\nCompare the AuditPol settings with the following. If the system does not audit the following, this is a finding:\n\nSystem &gt;&gt; System Integrity - Failure","ia_controls":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id":"SV-253335r991573","mitigation_control":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000463-GPOS-00207","id":"V-253335"},"third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","rule_version":"WN11-AU-000155","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000463-GPOS-00207","ccis":["CCI-000172"]},{"stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The system must be configured to audit System - System Integrity successes.","mitigations":"","discussion":"Maintaining an audit trail of system activity logs can help identify configuration errors, troubleshoot service disruptions, and analyze compromises that have occurred, as well as detect attacks. Audit logs are necessary to provide a trail of evidence in case the system or network is compromised. Collecting this data is essential for analyzing the security of information assets and detecting signs of suspicious and unexpected behavior.\n\nSystem Integrity records events related to violations of integrity to the security subsystem.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Audit - System Integrity - Success only)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25333600 (auditeventpolicysubcategories_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Audit - System Integrity - Success only\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\nState Operator          : One or more item-state comparisons may be true.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000000 (auditeventpolicysubcategories_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25333600 (auditeventpolicysubcategories_state)\nState Comment           : Audit - System Integrity - Success only\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'system_integrity' must be equal to 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25333601 (auditeventpolicysubcategories_state)\nState Comment           : Audit - System Integrity - Success and Failure\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'system_integrity' must be equal to 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : credential_validation equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n                        : kerberos_authentication_service equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : kerberos_service_ticket_operations equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : kerberos_ticket_events equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : other_account_logon_events equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : application_group_management equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : computer_account_management equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : distribution_group_management equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : other_account_management_events equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : security_group_management equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : user_account_management equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n                        : dpapi_activity equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : process_creation equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : process_termination equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : rpc_events equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : directory_service_access equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : directory_service_changes equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : directory_service_replication equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : detailed_directory_service_replication equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : account_lockout equals 'AUDIT_FAILURE'\n                        : ipsec_extended_mode equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : ipsec_main_mode equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : ipsec_quick_mode equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : logoff equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : logon equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n                        : network_policy_server equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : other_logon_logoff_events equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n                        : special_logon equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : logon_claims equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : application_generated equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : certification_services equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : detailed_file_share equals 'AUDIT_FAILURE'\n                        : file_share equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n                        : file_system equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : filtering_platform_connection equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : filtering_platform_packet_drop equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : handle_manipulation equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : kernel_object equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : other_object_access_events equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n                        : registry equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : sam equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : removable_storage equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n                        : central_access_policy_staging equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : audit_policy_change equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : authentication_policy_change equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : authorization_policy_change equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : filtering_platform_policy_change equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : mpssvc_rule_level_policy_change equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n                        : other_policy_change_events equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n                        : non_sensitive_privilege_use equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : other_privilege_use_events equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : sensitive_privilege_use equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n                        : ipsec_driver equals 'AUDIT_FAILURE'\n                        : other_system_events equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n                        : security_state_change equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : security_system_extension equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : system_integrity equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n                        : group_membership equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : pnp_activity equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : user_device_claims equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : audit_detailedtracking_tokenrightadjusted equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n","uuid":"3671411B-6BF8-1014-99C7-F91BEE5F818D","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253336"},"status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Advanced Audit Policy Configuration &gt;&gt; System Audit Policies &gt;&gt; System &gt;&gt; \"Audit System Integrity\" with \"Success\" selected.","group_id":"V-253336","potential_impacts":"","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253336","group_tree":{"id":"V-253336","title":"SRG-OS-000463-GPOS-00207"},"third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","rule_id":"SV-253336r991573","mitigation_control":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id_src":"SV-253336r991573_rule","check_content":"Security Option \"Audit: Force audit policy subcategory settings to override audit policy category settings\" must be set to \"Enabled\" (WN11-SO-000030) for the detailed auditing subcategories to be effective.\n\nUse the AuditPol tool to review the current Audit Policy configuration:\nOpen a Command Prompt with elevated privileges (\"Run as Administrator\").\nEnter \"AuditPol /get /category:*\".\n\nCompare the AuditPol settings with the following. If the system does not audit the following, this is a finding:\n\nSystem &gt;&gt; System Integrity - Success","ia_controls":"","ccis":["CCI-000172"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000463-GPOS-00207","rule_version":"WN11-AU-000160"},{"rule_id":"SV-253337r958752","mitigation_control":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id_src":"SV-253337r958752_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"If the system is configured to send audit records directly to an audit server, this is NA. This must be documented with the ISSO.\n\nIf the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\EventLog\\Application\\\n\nValue Name: MaxSize\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00008000 (32768) (or greater)","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000341-GPOS-00132","id":"V-253337"},"third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN11-AU-000500","ccis":["CCI-001849"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000341-GPOS-00132","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (The Application event log size is configured to 32768 KB or greater)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25333700 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The Application event log size is configured to 32768 KB or greater\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25333700 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\EventLog\\Application'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'MaxSize'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25333700 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be greater than or equal to '32768'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\EventLog\\Application'\n                        : name equals 'MaxSize'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '32768'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The Application event log size must be configured to 32768 KB or greater.","mitigations":"","discussion":"Inadequate log size will cause the log to fill up quickly. This may prevent audit events from being recorded properly and require frequent attention by administrative personnel.","fix_text":"If the system is configured to send audit records directly to an audit server, this is NA. This must be documented with the ISSO.\n\nConfigure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Event Log Service &gt;&gt; Application &gt;&gt; \"Specify the maximum log file size (KB)\" to \"Enabled\" with a \"Maximum Log Size (KB)\" of \"32768\" or greater.","group_id":"V-253337","potential_impacts":"","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253337","uuid":"367148E7-6BF8-1014-B0C0-9A5CED1D12E4","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253337"},"status":"not_a_finding"},{"rule_id":"SV-253338r1186375","mitigation_control":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id_src":"SV-253338r1186375_rule","check_content":"If the system is configured to send audit records directly to an audit server, this requirement is not applicable. This must be documented with the information system security officer (ISSO).\n\nThe registry configuration setting below must be set (at least) to a value equal to the size needed to contain one week's worth of audit records in the security event log. The value used below is an example that assumes a typical weekâs log size of 5GB.\n\nIf the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nNote: The following registry entry is an example; the value must equal at least one week's worth of records.\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\EventLog\\Security\\\n\nValue Name: MaxSize\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue:0x49960800 (5120000) (or greater)","ia_controls":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253338","title":"SRG-OS-000341-GPOS-00132"},"reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN11-AU-000505","ccis":["CCI-001849"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000341-GPOS-00132","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     false (The Security event log size is configured to 5120000 KB or greater)\nResult Analysis         :          HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\EventLog\\Security\\MaxSize\\value = '1024000' failed test of 'greater than or equal' compared to '5120000' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25333800 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : The Security event log size is configured to 5120000 KB or greater\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25333800 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\EventLog\\Security'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'MaxSize'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25333800 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be greater than or equal to '5120000'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\EventLog\\Security'\n                        : name equals 'MaxSize'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1024000'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\nResult Analysis         : HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\EventLog\\Security\\MaxSize\\value = '1024000' failed test of 'greater than or equal' compared to '5120000' \n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The security event log size must be configured to a value that holds at least one week's worth of audit records.","mitigations":"","discussion":"Inadequate log size will cause the log to fill up quickly. This may prevent audit events from being recorded properly and require frequent attention by administrative personnel. System administrators (SAs) must monitor the volume of security event audit records and increase the registry value for the log size as needed.","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Event Log Service &gt;&gt; Security &gt;&gt; \"Specify the maximum log file size (KB)\" to \"Enabled\" with a \"Maximum Log Size (KB)\" of a value that will contain one week of audit records or greater.\n\nIf the system is configured to send audit records directly to an audit server, this must be documented with the ISSO.","group_id":"V-253338","potential_impacts":"","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253338","uuid":"36715057-6BF8-1014-ACAA-9F49EBA50AB9","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253338","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"status":"open"},{"fix_text":"If the system is configured to send audit records directly to an audit server, this is NA. This must be documented with the ISSO.\n\nConfigure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Event Log Service &gt;&gt; System &gt;&gt; \"Specify the maximum log file size (KB)\" to \"Enabled\" with a \"Maximum Log Size (KB)\" of \"32768\" or greater.","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253339","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253339","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253339"},"uuid":"36715793-6BF8-1014-B81E-9D484B1B7195","status":"not_a_finding","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (The System event log size is configured to 32768 KB or greater)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25333900 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The System event log size is configured to 32768 KB or greater\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25333900 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\EventLog\\System'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'MaxSize'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25333700 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be greater than or equal to '32768'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\EventLog\\System'\n                        : name equals 'MaxSize'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '32768'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","mitigations":"","discussion":"Inadequate log size will cause the log to fill up quickly. This may prevent audit events from being recorded properly and require frequent attention by administrative personnel.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The System event log size must be configured to 32768 KB or greater.","rule_version":"WN11-AU-000510","ccis":["CCI-001849"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000341-GPOS-00132","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id":"SV-253339r958752","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253339r958752_rule","check_content":"If the system is configured to send audit records directly to an audit server, this is NA. This must be documented with the ISSO.\n\nIf the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\EventLog\\System\\\n\nValue Name: MaxSize\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00008000 (32768) (or greater)","ia_controls":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253339","title":"SRG-OS-000341-GPOS-00132"},"reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0"},{"stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows 11 permissions for the Application event log must prevent access by non-privileged accounts.","mitigations":"","discussion":"Maintaining an audit trail of system activity logs can help identify configuration errors, troubleshoot service disruptions, and analyze compromises that have occurred, as well as detect attacks. Audit logs are necessary to provide a trail of evidence in case the system or network is compromised. The Application event log may be susceptible to tampering if proper permissions are not applied.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nCriteria                :     false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :       true (The Application event log must have at least default permissions. Strict Path)\nTest                    :       false (The Application event log registry specified location must have the %SystemRoot% environment variable.) (negated)\nCriteria                :     true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :       true (The Application event log must have at least default permissions. Built Path)\nTest                    :       true (The Application event log registry specified location must have the %SystemRoot% environment variable.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25334001 (fileeffectiverights53_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The Application event log must have at least default permissions. Strict Path\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25334003 (fileeffectiverights53_object)\nObject Comment          : Permissions of Application event log, minus those allowed. Strict filepath, as listed.\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-80-880578595-1860270145-482643319-2788375705-1540778122'\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-18'\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-32-544'\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-19'\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-15-2-1'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25334002 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The Application event log registry specified location must have the %SystemRoot% environment variable.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25334002 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : path Application.evtx\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\EventLog\\Application'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'file'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000016 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : %SystemRoot% environment variable.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must match the pattern '^(?i)%SystemRoot%.*$'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\EventLog\\Application'\n                        : name equals 'file'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134197086260000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_expand_sz'\n                        : value equals '%SystemRoot%\\system32\\winevt\\Logs\\Application.evtx'\n                        : expanded_value equals 'C:\\WINDOWS\\system32\\winevt\\Logs\\Application.evtx'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25334000 (fileeffectiverights53_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The Application event log must have at least default permissions. Built Path\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25334000 (fileeffectiverights53_object)\nObject Comment          : Permissions of Application event log, minus those allowed. Built filepath.\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-80-880578595-1860270145-482643319-2788375705-1540778122'\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-18'\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-32-544'\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-19'\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-15-2-1'\n","uuid":"36715EBF-6BF8-1014-931B-CE7D445EB197","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253340"},"status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Ensure the permissions on the Application event log (Application.evtx) are configured to prevent standard user accounts or groups from having access. The default permissions listed below satisfy this requirement.\n\nEventlog - Full Control\nSYSTEM - Full Control\nAdministrators - Full Control\n\nThe default location is the \"%SystemRoot%\\SYSTEM32\\WINEVT\\LOGS\" directory.\n\nIf the location of the logs has been changed, when adding Eventlog to the permissions, it must be entered as \"NT Service\\Eventlog\".","group_id":"V-253340","potential_impacts":"","group_id_src":"V-253340","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000057-GPOS-00027","id":"V-253340"},"reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","rule_id":"SV-253340r958434","mitigation_control":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id_src":"SV-253340r958434_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"Verify the permissions on the Application event log (Application.evtx). Standard user accounts or groups must not have access. The default permissions listed below satisfy this requirement.\n\nEventlog - Full Control\nSYSTEM - Full Control\nAdministrators - Full Control\n\nThe default location is the \"%SystemRoot%\\SYSTEM32\\WINEVT\\LOGS\" directory. They may have been moved to another folder.\n\nIf the permissions for these files are not as restrictive as the ACLs listed, this is a finding.\n\nNote: If \"APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES\" has Special Permissions, this would not be a finding.","ccis":["CCI-000162"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000057-GPOS-00027","rule_version":"WN11-AU-000515"},{"fix_text":"Ensure the permissions on the Security event log (Security.evtx) are configured to prevent standard user accounts or groups from having access. The default permissions listed below satisfy this requirement.\n\nEventlog - Full Control\nSYSTEM - Full Control\nAdministrators - Full Control\n\nThe default location is the \"%SystemRoot%\\SYSTEM32\\WINEVT\\LOGS\" directory.\n\nIf the location of the logs has been changed, when adding Eventlog to the permissions, it must be entered as \"NT Service\\Eventlog\".","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253341","false_positives":"","group_id":"V-253341","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253341"},"uuid":"367165FA-6BF8-1014-9948-CD37D1239551","status":"not_a_findi