est)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The Security event log registry specified location must have the %SystemRoot% environment variable.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25334102 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : path Security.evtx\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\EventLog\\Security'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'file'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000016 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : %SystemRoot% environment variable.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must match the pattern '^(?i)%SystemRoot%.*$'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\EventLog\\Security'\n                        : name equals 'file'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134054566400000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_expand_sz'\n                        : value equals '%SystemRoot%\\System32\\winevt\\Logs\\Security.evtx'\n                        : expanded_value equals 'C:\\WINDOWS\\System32\\winevt\\Logs\\Security.evtx'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25334100 (fileeffectiverights53_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The Security event log must have at least default permissions. Built Path\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25334100 (fileeffectiverights53_object)\nObject Comment          : Permissions of Security event log, minus those allowed. Built filepath.\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-80-880578595-1860270145-482643319-2788375705-1540778122'\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-18'\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-32-544'\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-19'\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-15-2-1'\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","discussion":"Maintaining an audit trail of system activity logs can help identify configuration errors, troubleshoot service disruptions, and analyze compromises that have occurred, as well as detect attacks. Audit logs are necessary to provide a trail of evidence in case the system or network is compromised. The Security event log may disclose sensitive information or be susceptible to tampering if proper permissions are not applied.","mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows 11 permissions for the Security event log must prevent access by non-privileged accounts.","rule_version":"WN11-AU-000520","ccis":["CCI-000162"],"group_title":"SRG-OS-000057-GPOS-00027","severity":"medium","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253341r958434","check_content":"Verify the permissions on the Security event log (Security.evtx). Standard user accounts or groups must not have access. The default permissions listed below satisfy this requirement.\n\nEventlog - Full Control\nSYSTEM - Full Control\nAdministrators - Full Control\n\nThe default location is the \"%SystemRoot%\\SYSTEM32\\WINEVT\\LOGS\" directory. They may have been moved to another folder.\n\nIf the permissions for these files are not as restrictive as the ACLs listed, this is a finding.\n\nNote: If \"APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES\" has Special Permissions, this would not be a finding.","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253341r958434_rule","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253341","title":"SRG-OS-000057-GPOS-00027"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false"},{"ccis":["CCI-000162"],"group_title":"SRG-OS-000057-GPOS-00027","severity":"medium","rule_version":"WN11-AU-000525","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000057-GPOS-00027","id":"V-253342"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253342r958434","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","check_content":"Verify the permissions on the System event log (System.evtx). Standard user accounts or groups must not have access. The default permissions listed below satisfy this requirement.\n\nEventlog - Full Control\nSYSTEM - Full Control\nAdministrators - Full Control\n\nThe default location is the \"%SystemRoot%\\SYSTEM32\\WINEVT\\LOGS\" directory. They may have been moved to another folder.\n\nIf the permissions for these files are not as restrictive as the ACLs listed, this is a finding.\n\nNote: If \"APPLICATION PACKAGE AUTHORITY\\ALL APPLICATION PACKAGES\" has Special Permissions, this would not be a finding.","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253342r958434_rule","uuid":"36717115-6BF8-1014-93CB-FB544831AA0E","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253342","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Ensure the permissions on the System event log (System.evtx) are configured to prevent standard user accounts or groups from having access. The default permissions listed below satisfy this requirement.\n\nEventlog - Full Control\nSYSTEM - Full Control\nAdministrators - Full Control\n\nThe default location is the \"%SystemRoot%\\SYSTEM32\\WINEVT\\LOGS\" directory.\n\nIf the location of the logs has been changed, when adding Eventlog to the permissions, it must be entered as \"NT Service\\Eventlog\".","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253342","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253342","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","rule_title":"Windows 11 permissions for the System event log must prevent access by non-privileged accounts.","security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"Maintaining an audit trail of system activity logs can help identify configuration errors, troubleshoot service disruptions, and analyze compromises that have occurred, as well as detect attacks. Audit logs are necessary to provide a trail of evidence in case the system or network is compromised. The System event log may be susceptible to tampering if proper permissions are not applied.","mitigations":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nCriteria                :     false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :       true (The System event log must have at least default permissions. Strict Path)\nTest                    :       false (The System event log registry specified location must have the %SystemRoot% environment variable.) (negated)\nCriteria                :     true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :       true (The System event log must have at least default permissions. Built Path)\nTest                    :       true (The System event log registry specified location must have the %SystemRoot% environment variable.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25334201 (fileeffectiverights53_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The System event log must have at least default permissions. Strict Path\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25334203 (fileeffectiverights53_object)\nObject Comment          : Permissions of System event log, minus those allowed. Strict filepath, as listed.\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-80-880578595-1860270145-482643319-2788375705-1540778122'\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-18'\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-32-544'\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-19'\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-15-2-1'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25334202 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The System event log registry specified location must have the %SystemRoot% environment variable.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25334202 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : path System.evtx\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\EventLog\\System'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'file'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000016 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : %SystemRoot% environment variable.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must match the pattern '^(?i)%SystemRoot%.*$'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\EventLog\\System'\n                        : name equals 'file'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134317254390000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_expand_sz'\n                        : value equals '%SystemRoot%\\system32\\winevt\\Logs\\System.evtx'\n                        : expanded_value equals 'C:\\WINDOWS\\system32\\winevt\\Logs\\System.evtx'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25334200 (fileeffectiverights53_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The System event log must have at least default permissions. Built Path\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25334200 (fileeffectiverights53_object)\nObject Comment          : Permissions of System event log, minus those allowed. Built filepath.\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-80-880578595-1860270145-482643319-2788375705-1540778122'\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-18'\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-32-544'\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-19'\nExclude Items If        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-15-2-1'\n"},{"stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","rule_title":"Windows 11 must be configured to audit Other Policy Change Events Failures.","security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"Maintaining an audit trail of system activity logs can help identify configuration errors, troubleshoot service disruptions, and analyze compromises that have occurred, as well as detect attacks. Audit logs are necessary to provide a trail of evidence in case the system or network is compromised. Collecting this data is essential for analyzing the security of information assets and detecting signs of suspicious and unexpected behavior.\n\nAudit Other Policy Change Events contains events about EFS Data Recovery Agent policy changes, changes in Windows Filtering Platform filter, status on Security policy settings updates for local Group Policy settings, Central Access Policy changes, and detailed troubleshooting events for Cryptographic Next Generation (CNG) operations.","mitigations":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Other Policy Change Events' is set to 'Failure' or 'Success and Failure')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25334400 (auditeventpolicysubcategories_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Other Policy Change Events' is set to 'Failure' or 'Success and Failure'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\nState Operator          : One or more item-state comparisons may be true.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000000 (auditeventpolicysubcategories_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25334400 (auditeventpolicysubcategories_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'other_policy_change_events' must be equal to 'AUDIT_FAILURE'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25334401 (auditeventpolicysubcategories_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'other_policy_change_events' must be equal to 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n             