,"classification":"Unclassified","comments":null},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Camera access from the lock screen must be disabled.","discussion":"Enabling camera access from the lock screen could allow for unauthorized use. Requiring logon will ensure the device is only used by authorized personnel.","mitigations":"","fix_text":"If the device does not have a camera, this is NA.\n\nConfigure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Control Panel &gt;&gt; Personalization &gt;&gt; \"Prevent enabling lock screen camera\" to \"Enabled\".","group_id":"V-253350","potential_impacts":"","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253350","uuid":"3671A5BD-6BF8-1014-9E0E-9FC73CF30487","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:253350","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml"},"status":"not_applicable","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253350r958478","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","ia_controls":"","check_content":"If the device does not have a camera, this is NA.\n\nIf the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Personalization\\\n\nValue Name: NoLockScreenCamera\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1","rule_id_src":"SV-253350r958478_rule","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","id":"V-253350"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","rule_version":"WN11-CC-000005","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","severity":"medium"},{"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"rule_version":"WN11-CC-000007","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"id":"V-253351","title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049"},"third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253351r1106508_rule","check_content":"If the device or operating system does not have a camera installed, this requirement is not applicable.\n\nThis requirement is not applicable to mobile devices (smartphones and tablets), where the use of the camera is a local authorizing official (AO) decision.\n\nThis requirement is not applicable to dedicated VTC suites located in approved VTC locations that are centrally managed.\n\nFor an external camera, if there is not a method for the operator to manually disconnect camera at the end of collaborative computing sessions, this is a finding.\n\nFor a built-in camera, the camera must be protected by a camera cover (e.g. laptop camera cover slide) when not in use. If the built-in camera is not protected with a camera cover, or if the built-in\ncamera is not disabled in the bios, this is a finding.\n\nIf the camera is not disconnected or covered, the following registry entry is required:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistryPath\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\CapabilityAccessManager\\ConsentStore\\webcam\n\nValue Name: Value                                                                             Value Data: Deny\n\nIf \"Value Name\" is set to a value other than \"Deny\" and the collaborative computing device has not been authorized for use, this is a finding.","ia_controls":"","rule_id":"SV-253351r1106508","mitigation_control":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"status":"not_applicable","uuid":"3671ACA1-6BF8-1014-AE83-B9D22C2136F1","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows11:questionnaire:18701"},"potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253351","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253351","fix_text":"If the camera is not disconnected or covered, the following registry entry is required.\n \nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistryPath\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\CapabilityAccessManager\\ConsentStore\\webcam\n\nValue Name: Value                                                                            Value Data: Deny","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows 11 must cover or disable the built-in or attached camera when not in use.","mitigations":"","discussion":"It is detrimental for operating systems to provide, or install by default, functionality exceeding requirements or mission objectives. These unnecessary capabilities or services are often overlooked and therefore may remain unsecured. They increase the risk to the platform by providing additional attack vectors.\n\nFailing to disconnect from collaborative computing devices (i.e. cameras) can result in subsequent compromises of organizational information. Providing easy methods to physically disconnect from such devices after a collaborative computing session helps to ensure that participants actually carry out the disconnect activity without having to go through complex and tedious procedures.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049, SRG-OS-000370-GPOS-00155","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n"},{"uuid":"3671B3FB-6BF8-1014-B107-C3A9CEAF1D7C","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253352","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Control Panel &gt;&gt; Personalization &gt;&gt; \"Prevent enabling lock screen slide show\" to \"Enabled\".","group_id":"V-253352","potential_impacts":"","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253352","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The display of slide shows on the lock screen must be disabled.","mitigations":"","discussion":"Slide shows that are displayed on the lock screen could display sensitive information to unauthorized personnel. Turning off this feature will limit access to the information to a logged on user.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Verifies 'Prevent enabling lock screen slide show' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25335200 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Verifies 'Prevent enabling lock screen slide show' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25335200 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Registry object for HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Personalization\\NoLockScreenSlideshow\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Personalization'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'NoLockScreenSlideshow'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Personalization'\n                        : name equals 'NoLockScreenSlideshow'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","rule_version":"WN11-CC-000010","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","id":"V-253352"},"reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","rule_id":"SV-253352r958478","mitigation_control":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id_src":"SV-253352r958478_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Personalization\\\n\nValue Name: NoLockScreenSlideshow\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1"},{"legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253353","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253353","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; MSS (Legacy) &gt;&gt; \"MSS: (DisableIPSourceRouting IPv6) IP source routing protection level (protects against packet spoofing)\" to \"Highest protection, source routing is completely disabled\".\n\nThis policy setting requires the installation of the MSS-Legacy custom templates included with the STIG package. \"MSS-Legacy.admx\" and \"MSS-Legacy.adml\" must be copied to the \\Windows\\PolicyDefinitions and \\Windows\\PolicyDefinitions\\en-US directories respectively.","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253353","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"uuid":"3671BE5C-6BF8-1014-99C4-E6BC4866EF88","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('MSS: (DisableIPSourceRouting IPv6) IP source routing protection level (protects against packet spoofing)' is set to 'Highest protection, source routing is completely disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25335300 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'MSS: (DisableIPSourceRouting IPv6) IP source routing protection level (protects against packet spoofing)' is set to 'Highest protection, source routing is completely disabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25335300 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Tcpip6\\Parameters'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisableIPSourceRouting'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000002 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Tcpip6\\Parameters'\n                        : name equals 'DisableIPSourceRouting'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134055257810000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '2'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","mitigations":"","discussion":"Configuring the system to disable IPv6 source routing protects against spoofing.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"IPv6 source routing must be configured to highest protection.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","rule_version":"WN11-CC-000020","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"rule_id_src":"SV-253353r991589_rule","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Tcpip6\\Parameters\\\n\nValue Name: DisableIpSourceRouting\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 2","ia_controls":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id":"SV-253353r991589","mitigation_control":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"id":"V-253353","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":""},{"check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Tcpip\\Parameters\\\n\nValue Name: DisableIPSourceRouting\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 2","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253354r991589_rule","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253354r991589","weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253354","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"rule_version":"WN11-CC-000025","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('MSS: (DisableIPSourceRouting) IP source routing protection level (protects against packet spoofing)' is set to 'Highest protection, source routing is completely disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25335400 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'MSS: (DisableIPSourceRouting) IP source routing protection level (protects against packet spoofing)' is set to 'Highest protection, source routing is completely disabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25335400 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Tcpip\\Parameters'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisableIPSourceRouting'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000002 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Tcpip\\Parameters'\n                        : name equals 'DisableIPSourceRouting'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134317244800000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '2'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","discussion":"Configuring the system to disable IP source routing protects against spoofing.","mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The system must be configured to prevent IP source routing.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253354","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253354","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; MSS (Legacy) &gt;&gt; \"MSS: (DisableIPSourceRouting) IP source routing protection level (protects against packet spoofing)\" to \"Highest protection, source routing is completely disabled\".\n\nThis policy setting requires the installation of the MSS-Legacy custom templates included with the STIG package. \"MSS-Legacy.admx\" and \"MSS-Legacy.adml\" must be copied to the \\Windows\\PolicyDefinitions and \\Windows\\PolicyDefinitions\\en-US directories respectively.","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253354"},"uuid":"3671C760-6BF8-1014-AAE1-9A110CA995E0"},{"ccis":["CCI-000366"],"severity":"low","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","rule_version":"WN11-CC-000030","group_tree":{"id":"V-253355","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id":"SV-253355r991589","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253355r991589_rule","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Tcpip\\Parameters\\\n\nValue Name: EnableICMPRedirect\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0","ia_controls":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253355","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"uuid":"3671CE3C-6BF8-1014-80FF-D281F5A69283","status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; MSS (Legacy) &gt;&gt; \"MSS: (EnableICMPRedirect) Allow ICMP redirects to override OSPF generated routes\" to \"Disabled\".\n\nThis policy setting requires the installation of the MSS-Legacy custom templates included with the STIG package. \"MSS-Legacy.admx\" and \"MSS-Legacy.adml\" must be copied to the \\Windows\\PolicyDefinitions and \\Windows\\PolicyDefinitions\\en-US directories respectively.","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253355","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253355","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","mitigations":"","discussion":"Allowing ICMP redirect of routes can lead to traffic not being routed properly.  When disabled, this forces ICMP to be routed via shortest path first.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The system must be configured to prevent Internet Control Message Protocol (ICMP) redirects from overriding Open Shortest Path First (OSPF) generated routes.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('MSS: (EnableICMPRedirect) Allow ICMP redirects to override OSPF generated routes' is set to 'Disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25335500 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'MSS: (EnableICMPRedirect) Allow ICMP redirects to override OSPF generated routes' is set to 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25335500 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Tcpip\\Parameters'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'EnableICMPRedirect'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Tcpip\\Parameters'\n                        : name equals 'EnableICMPRedirect'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134317244800000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n"},{"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253356","title":"SRG-OS-000420-GPOS-00186"},"check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Netbt\\Parameters\\\n\nValue Name: NoNameReleaseOnDemand\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253356r958902_rule","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253356r958902","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"group_title":"SRG-OS-000420-GPOS-00186","severity":"low","ccis":["CCI-002385"],"rule_version":"WN11-CC-000035","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The system must be configured to ignore NetBIOS name release requests except from WINS servers.","discussion":"Configuring the system to ignore name release requests, except from WINS servers, prevents a denial of service (DoS) attack. The DoS consists of sending a NetBIOS name release request to the server for each entry in the server's cache, causing a response delay in the normal operation of the servers WINS resolution capability.","mitigations":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('MSS: (NoNameReleaseOnDemand) Allow computer to ignore NetBIOS name release requests except from WINS servers' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25335600 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'MSS: (NoNameReleaseOnDemand) Allow computer to ignore NetBIOS name release requests except from WINS servers' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25335600 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Netbt\\Parameters'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'NoNameReleaseOnDemand'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Netbt\\Parameters'\n                        : name equals 'NoNameReleaseOnDemand'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134054567550000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"3671D531-6BF8-1014-9FFA-E1C5AEB1916D","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253356","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253356","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253356","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; MSS (Legacy) &gt;&gt; \"MSS: (NoNameReleaseOnDemand) Allow the computer to ignore NetBIOS name release requests except from WINS servers\" to \"Enabled\".\n\nThis policy setting requires the installation of the MSS-Legacy custom templates included with the STIG package. \"MSS-Legacy.admx\" and \"MSS-Legacy.adml\" must be copied to the \\Windows\\PolicyDefinitions and \\Windows\\PolicyDefinitions\\en-US directories respectively."},{"rule_version":"WN11-CC-000037","ccis":["CCI-001084"],"group_title":"SRG-OS-000134-GPOS-00068","severity":"medium","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253357r958518","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","check_content":"If the system is not a member of a domain, this is NA.\n\nIf the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System\\\n\nValue Name: LocalAccountTokenFilterPolicy\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000000 (0)","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253357r958518_rule","third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253357","title":"SRG-OS-000134-GPOS-00068"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; MS Security Guide &gt;&gt; \"Apply UAC restrictions to local accounts on network logons\" to \"Enabled\".\n\nThis policy setting requires the installation of the SecGuide custom templates included with the STIG package. \"SecGuide.admx\" and \"SecGuide.adml\" must be copied to the \\Windows\\PolicyDefinitions and \\Windows\\PolicyDefinitions\\en-US directories respectively.","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253357","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253357","uuid":"3671DC22-6BF8-1014-A5FA-95FA92F83E90","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253357"},"status":"not_applicable","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Local administrator accounts must have their privileged token filtered to prevent elevated privileges from being used over the network on domain systems.","discussion":"A compromised local administrator account can provide means for an attacker to move laterally between domain systems.\n\nWith User Account Control enabled, filtering the privileged token for built-in administrator accounts will prevent the elevated privileges of these accounts from being used over the network.","mitigations":""},{"rule_version":"WN11-CC-000038","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\Wdigest\\\n\nValue Name: UseLogonCredential\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000000 (0)","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253358r958478_rule","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253358r958478","weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253358","title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049"},"legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253358","group_id":"V-253358","potential_impacts":"","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; MS Security Guide &gt;&gt; \"WDigest Authentication (disabling may require KB2871997)\" to \"Disabled\".\n\nThe patch referenced in the policy title is not required for Windows 11.\n\nThis policy setting requires the installation of the SecGuide custom templates included with the STIG package. \"SecGuide.admx\" and \"SecGuide.adml\" must be copied to the \\Windows\\PolicyDefinitions and \\Windows\\PolicyDefinitions\\en-US directories respectively.","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253358"},"uuid":"3671E2E9-6BF8-1014-9657-A0FE4B78FAC8","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (WDigest Authentication is disabled)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25335800 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : WDigest Authentication is disabled\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25335800 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\Wdigest'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'UseLogonCredential'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\SecurityProviders\\Wdigest'\n                        : name equals 'UseLogonCredential'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134054567970000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","discussion":"When the WDigest Authentication protocol is enabled, plain text passwords are stored in the Local Security Authority Subsystem Service (LSASS) exposing them to theft. WDigest is disabled by default in Windows 11. This setting ensures this is enforced.","mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"WDigest Authentication must be disabled.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4"},{"rule_id":"SV-253359r958478","mitigation_control":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id_src":"SV-253359r958478_rule","check_content":"If the following registry values do not exist or are not configured as specified, this is a finding.\nThe policy configures the same Value Name, Type and Value under four different registry paths.\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Paths: \n\\SOFTWARE\\Classes\\batfile\\shell\\runasuser\\\n\\SOFTWARE\\Classes\\cmdfile\\shell\\runasuser\\\n\\SOFTWARE\\Classes\\exefile\\shell\\runasuser\\\n\\SOFTWARE\\Classes\\mscfile\\shell\\runasuser\\\n\nValue Name: SuppressionPolicy\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00001000 (4096)","ia_controls":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","id":"V-253359"},"reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN11-CC-000039","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Remove 'Run as Different User' from context menus' is set to 'Enabled' (batfile))\nTest                    :     true ('Remove 'Run as Different User' from context menus' is set to 'Enabled' (cmdfile))\nTest                    :     true ('Remove 'Run as Different User' from context menus' is set to 'Enabled' (exefile))\nTest                    :     true ('Remove 'Run as Different User' from context menus' is set to 'Enabled' (mscfile))\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25335900