ype and value equals 4096\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '4096'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Classes\\exefile\\shell\\runasuser'\n                        : name equals 'SuppressionPolicy'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134054533750000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '4096'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25335903 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Remove 'Run as Different User' from context menus' is set to 'Enabled' (mscfile)\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25335903 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Classes\\mscfile\\shell\\runasuser'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'SuppressionPolicy'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25335900 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Reg_Dword type and value equals 4096\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '4096'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Classes\\mscfile\\shell\\runasuser'\n                        : name equals 'SuppressionPolicy'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134054533750000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '4096'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Run as different user must be removed from context menus.","mitigations":"","discussion":"The \"Run as different user\" selection from context menus allows the use of credentials other than the currently logged on user. Using privileged credentials in a standard user session can expose those credentials to theft. Removing this option from context menus helps prevent this from occurring.","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; MS Security Guide &gt;&gt; \"Remove \"Run as Different User\" from context menus\" to \"Enabled\".\n\nThis policy setting requires the installation of the SecGuide custom templates included with the STIG package. \"SecGuide.admx\" and \"SecGuide.adml\" must be copied to the \\Windows\\PolicyDefinitions and \\Windows\\PolicyDefinitions\\en-US directories respectively.","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253359","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253359","uuid":"3671E9DB-6BF8-1014-BC98-E6118B269DCF","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253359"},"status":"not_a_finding"},{"rule_version":"WN11-CC-000040","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"ia_controls":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\LanmanWorkstation\\\n\nValue Name: AllowInsecureGuestAuth\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000000 (0)","rule_id_src":"SV-253360r991589_rule","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253360r991589","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-253360"},"group_id":"V-253360","potential_impacts":"","group_id_src":"V-253360","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Network &gt;&gt; Lanman Workstation &gt;&gt; \"Enable insecure guest logons\" to \"Disabled\".","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"367201FD-6BF8-1014-A878-B86D400D9593","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253360"},"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Enable insecure guest logons' is set to 'Disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25336000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Enable insecure guest logons' is set to 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25336000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\LanmanWorkstation'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'AllowInsecureGuestAuth'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\LanmanWorkstation'\n                        : name equals 'AllowInsecureGuestAuth'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Insecure logons to an SMB server must be disabled.","discussion":"Insecure guest logons allow unauthenticated access to shared folders. Shared resources on a system must require authentication to establish proper access.","mitigations":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4"},{"documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"id":"V-253361","title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049"},"third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253361r958478_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Network Connections\\\n\nValue Name: NC_ShowSharedAccessUI\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000000 (0)","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id":"SV-253361r958478","mitigation_control":"","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"rule_version":"WN11-CC-000044","mitigations":"","discussion":"Internet connection sharing makes it possible for an existing internet connection, such as through wireless, to be shared and used by other systems essentially creating a mobile hotspot. This exposes the system sharing the connection to others with potentially malicious purpose.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Internet connection sharing must be disabled.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Prohibit use of Internet Connection Sharing on your DNS domain network' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25336100 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Prohibit use of Internet Connection Sharing on your DNS domain network' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25336100 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Network Connections'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'NC_ShowSharedAccessUI'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Network Connections'\n                        : name equals 'NC_ShowSharedAccessUI'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253361","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"uuid":"367209CB-6BF8-1014-BADF-DE2D99058B81","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253361","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253361","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Network &gt;&gt; Network Connections &gt;&gt; \"Prohibit use of Internet Connection Sharing on your DNS domain network\" to \"Enabled\"."},{"check_content":"This requirement is applicable to domain-joined systems, for standalone systems this is NA.\n\nIf the following registry values do not exist or are not configured as specified, this is a finding.\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\NetworkProvider\\HardenedPaths\\\n\nValue Name: \\\\*\\NETLOGON\nValue Type: REG_SZ\nValue: RequireMutualAuthentication=1, RequireIntegrity=1\n\nValue Name: \\\\*\\SYSVOL\nValue Type: REG_SZ\nValue: RequireMutualAuthentication=1, RequireIntegrity=1\n\nAdditional entries would not be a finding.","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253362r991589_rule","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253362r991589","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253362","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"rule_version":"WN11-CC-000050","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Hardened UNC Paths must be defined to require mutual authentication and integrity for at least the \\\\*\\SYSVOL and \\\\*\\NETLOGON shares.","discussion":"Additional security requirements are applied to Universal Naming Convention (UNC) paths specified in Hardened UNC paths before allowing access them. This aids in preventing tampering with or spoofing of connections to these paths.","mitigations":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","group_id":"V-253362","potential_impacts":"","group_id_src":"V-253362","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Network &gt;&gt; Network Provider &gt;&gt; \"Hardened UNC Paths\" to \"Enabled\" with at least the following configured in \"Hardened UNC Paths:\" (click the \"Show\" button to display).\n\nValue Name: \\\\*\\SYSVOL\nValue: RequireMutualAuthentication=1, RequireIntegrity=1\n\nValue Name: \\\\*\\NETLOGON\nValue: RequireMutualAuthentication=1, RequireIntegrity=1","status":"not_applicable","uuid":"367213F1-6BF8-1014-ABCB-B1DE7EBA82F0","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253362"}},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Prioritize ECC Curves with longer key lengths first. NistP384 Requirement)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25336301 (variable_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Prioritize ECC Curves with longer key lengths first. NistP384 Requirement\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : One and only one item may match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25336301 (variable_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'var_ref' must be equal to 'oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:var:25336301'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25336301 (variable_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must match the pattern '^NistP384\\s*NistP256$'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : var_ref equals 'oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:var:25336301'\n                        : value equals 'NistP384NistP256'\n","mitigations":"","discussion":"Use of weak or untested encryption algorithms undermines the purposes of utilizing encryption to protect data. By default Windows uses ECC curves with shorter key lengths first. Requiring ECC curves with longer key lengths to be prioritized first helps ensure more secure algorithms are used.","rule_title":"Windows 11 must be configured to prioritize ECC Curves with longer key lengths first.","security_override_guidance":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253363","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253363","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Network &gt;&gt; SSL Configuration Settings &gt;&gt; \"ECC Curve Order\" to \"Enabled\" with \"ECC Curve Order:\" including the following in the order listed:\n\nNistP384\nNistP256","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:253363"},"uuid":"36721B16-6BF8-1014-A211-F3BAA922BA2E","rule_id_src":"SV-253363r971535_rule","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Cryptography\\Configuration\\SSL\\00010002\\\n\nValue Name: EccCurves\n\nValue Type: REG_MULTI_SZ\nValue: NistP384 NistP256","ia_controls":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id":"SV-253363r971535","mitigation_control":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000120-GPOS-00061","id":"V-253363"},"reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","rule_version":"WN11-CC-000052","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000120-GPOS-00061","ccis":["CCI-000803"]},{"mitigations":"","discussion":"Multiple network connections can provide additional attack vectors to a system and must be limited. The \"Minimize the number of simultaneous connections to the Internet or a Windows Domain\" setting prevents systems from automatically establishing multiple connections. When both wired and wireless connections are available, for example, the less preferred connection (typically wireless) will be disconnected.","rule_title":"Simultaneous connections to the internet or a Windows domain must be limited.","security_override_guidance":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Simultaneous connections to the internet or a Windows domain are limited)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25336400 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Simultaneous connections to the internet or a Windows domain are limited\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25336400 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\WcmSvc\\GroupPolicy'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'fMinimizeConnections'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000003 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '3'\n","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253364"},"uuid":"3672220D-6BF8-1014-9FCF-FA92D49DDBF0","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253364","group_id":"V-253364","potential_impacts":"","fix_text":"The default behavior for \"Minimize the number of simultaneous connections to the Internet or a Windows Domain\" is \"Enabled\".\n\nIf this needs to be corrected, configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Network &gt;&gt; Windows Connection Manager &gt;&gt; \"Minimize the number of simultaneous connections to the Internet or a Windows Domain\" to \"Enabled\".  Under \"Options\", set \"Minimize Policy Options\" to \"3 = Prevent Wi-Fi When on Ethernet\".","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000481-GPOS-00481","id":"V-253364"},"third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253364r958358_rule","check_content":"The default behavior for \"Minimize the number of simultaneous connections to the Internet or a Windows Domain\" is \"Enabled\".\n\nIf it exists and is configured with a value of \"0\", this is a finding.\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\WcmSvc\\GroupPolicy\\\n\nValue Name: fMinimizeConnections\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 3 (or if the Value Name does not exist)","ia_controls":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id":"SV-253364r958358","mitigation_control":"","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000481-GPOS-00481","ccis":["CCI-002418"],"rule_version":"WN11-CC-000055"},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Prohibit connection to non-domain networks when connected to domain authenticated network' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25336500 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Prohibit connection to non-domain networks when connected to domain authenticated network' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25336500 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\WcmSvc\\GroupPolicy\\'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'fBlockNonDomain'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\WcmSvc\\GroupPolicy\\'\n                        : name equals 'fBlockNonDomain'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","mitigations":"","discussion":"Multiple network connections can provide additional attack vectors to a system and must be limited. When connected to a domain, communication must go through the domain connection.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Connections to non-domain networks when connected to a domain authenticated network must be blocked.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253365","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253365","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Network &gt;&gt; Windows Connection Manager &gt;&gt; \"Prohibit connection to non-domain networks when connected to domain authenticated network\" to \"Enabled\".","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253365"},"uuid":"367228F2-6BF8-1014-91D9-FEBE136F7396","rule_id_src":"SV-253365r991589_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\WcmSvc\\GroupPolicy\\\n\nValue Name: fBlockNonDomain\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id":"SV-253365r991589","mitigation_control":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-253365"},"responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","rule_version":"WN11-CC-000060","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","ccis":["CCI-000366"]},{"third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-253366"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253366r991589","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"ia_controls":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\WcmSvc\\wifinetworkmanager\\config\\\n\nValue Name: AutoConnectAllowedOEM\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000000 (0)","rule_id_src":"SV-253366r991589_rule","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","severity":"medium","rule_version":"WN11-CC-000065","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Wi-Fi Sense must be disabled.","discussion":"Wi-Fi Sense automatically connects the system to known hotspots and networks that contacts have shared. It also allows the sharing of the system's known networks to contacts. Automatically connecting to hotspots and shared networks can expose a system to unsecured or potentially malicious systems.","mitigations":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Verifies 'Allow Windows to automatically connect to suggested open hotspots, to networks shared by contacts, and to hotspots offering paid service' is set to 'Disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25336600 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Verifies 'Allow Windows to automatically connect to suggested open hotspots, to networks shared by contacts, and to hotspots offering paid service' is set to 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25336600 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : AutoConnectAllowedOEM\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\WcmSvc\\wifinetworkmanager\\config'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'AutoConnectAllowedOEM'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\WcmSvc\\wifinetworkmanager\\config'\n                        : name equals 'AutoConnectAllowedOEM'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134054567770000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","uuid":"36722F9D-6BF8-1014-931C-FF1F77B0F9E8","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253366"},"status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Network &gt;&gt; WLAN Service &gt;&gt; WLAN Settings&gt;&gt; \"Allow Windows to automatically connect to suggested open hotspots, to networks shared by contacts, and to hotspots offering paid services\" to \"Disabled\".","group_id":"V-253366","potential_impacts":"","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253366"},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Include command line in process creation events' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25336700 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Include command line in process creation events' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25336700 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System\\Audit'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'ProcessCreationIncludeCmdLine_Enabled'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System\\Audit'\n                        : name equals 'ProcessCreationIncludeCmdLine_Enabled'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","rule_title":"Command line data must be included in process creation events.","security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"Maintaining an audit trail of system activity logs can help identify configuration errors, troubleshoot service disruptions, and analyze compromises that have occurred, as well as detect attacks. Audit logs are necessary to provide a trail of evidence in case the system or network is compromised. Collecting this data is essential for analyzing the security of information assets and detecting signs of suspicious and unexpected behavior.\n\nEnabling \"Include command line data for process creation events\" will record the command line information with the process creation events in the log. This can provide additional detail when malware has run on a system.","mitigations":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","group_id":"V-253367","potential_impacts":"","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253367","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; System &gt;&gt; Audit Process Creation &gt;&gt; \"Include command line in process creation events\" to \"Enabled\".","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"367236B1-6BF8-1014-BD9B-F8F7FD25814F","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253367","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"ia_controls":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE \nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System\\Audit\\\n\nValue Name: ProcessCreationIncludeCmdLine_Enabled\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1","rule_id_src":"SV-253367r958422_rule","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253367r958422","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000042-GPOS-00020","id":"V-253367"},"rule_version":"WN11-CC-000066","group_title":"SRG-OS-000042-GPOS-00020","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-000135"]},{"group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"rule_version":"WN11-CC-000068","weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-253368"},"check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CredentialsDelegation\\\n\nValue Name: AllowProtectedCreds\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253368r991589_rule","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253368r991589","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253368"},"uuid":"36723D9E-6BF8-1014-95F3-A81C1CD32BE6","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253368","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253368","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; System &gt;&gt; Credentials Delegation &gt;&gt; \"Remote host allows delegation of non-exportable credentials\" to \"Enabled\".","discussion":"An exportable version of credentials is provided to remote hosts when using credential delegation which exposes them to theft on the remote host. Restricted Admin mode or Remote Credential Guard allow delegation of non-exportable credentials providing additional protection of the credentials. Enabling this configures the host to support Restricted Admin mode or Remote Credential Guard.","mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows 11 must be configured to enable Remote host allows delegation of non-exportable credentials.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Remote host allows delegation of non-exportable credentials' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25336800 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Remote host allows delegation of non-exportable credentials' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25336800 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CredentialsDelegation'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'AllowProtectedCreds'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CredentialsDelegation'\n                        : name equals 'AllowProtectedCreds'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n"},{"mitigations":"","discussion":"Virtualization-based Security (VBS) provides the platform for the additional security features, Credential Guard and virtualization-based protection of code integrity. Secure Boot is the minimum security level with DMA protection providing additional memory protection. DMA Protection requires a CPU that supports input/output memory management unit (IOMMU).","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Virtualization-based Security must be enabled on Windows 11 with the platform security level configured to Secure Boot or Secure Boot with DMA Protection.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (RequiredSecurityProperties should return a value of 2)\nTest                    :   false (VirtualizationBasedSecurityStatus should return a value of 2)\nResult Analysis         :        virtualizationbasedsecuritystatus = '1' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to '2' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25336901 (cmdlet_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : RequiredSecurityProperties should return a value of 2\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25336901 (cmdlet_object)\nObject Comment          : DeviceGuard requiredsecurityproperties\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'module_name' must be equal to 'CimCmdlets'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'verb' must be equal to 'Get'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'noun' must be equal to 'CimInstance'\nObject Requirement      : for  'parameters' the following must be true:\n                        : classname must be equal to 'Win32_DeviceGuard'\n                        : namespace must be equal to 'root\\Microsoft\\Windows\\DeviceGuard'\nObject Requirement      : for  'select' the following must be true:\n                        : property must be equal to 'requiredsecurityproperties'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25336901 (cmdlet_state)\nState Comment           : requiredsecurityproperties must match a pattern of 2\nState Requirement       : for all 'value' the following must be true:\n                        : all requiredsecurityproperties must match the pattern '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : module_name equals 'CimCmdlets'\n                        : module_id equals '{fb6cc51d-c096-4b38-b78d-0fed6277096a}'\n                        : module_version equals '1.0.0.0'\n                        : verb equals 'Get'\n                        : noun equals 'CimInstance'\n                        : collected 'parameters' result: \n                        : classname = 'Win32_DeviceGuard'\n                        : namespace = 'root\\Microsoft\\Windows\\DeviceGuard'\n                        : collected 'select' result: \n                        : property = 'requiredsecurityproperties'\n                        : collected 'value' result: \n                        : requiredsecurityproperties = '{1,2}'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25336902 (cmdlet_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : VirtualizationBasedSecurityStatus should return a value of 2\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25336902 (cmdlet_object)\nObject Comment          : DeviceGuard virtualizationbasedsecuritystatus\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'module_name' must be equal to 'CimCmdlets'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'verb' must be equal to 'Get'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'noun' must be equal to 'CimInstance'\nObject Requirement      : for  'parameters' the following must be true:\n                        : classname must be equal to 'Win32_DeviceGuard'\n                        : namespace must be equal to 'root\\Microsoft\\Windows\\DeviceGuard'\nObject Requirement      : for  'select' the following must be true:\n                        : property must be equal to 'virtualizationbasedsecuritystatus'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25336902 (cmdlet_state)\nState Comment           : requiredsecurityproperties must match a pattern of 2\nState Requirement       : for all 'value' the following must be true:\n                        : all virtualizationbasedsecuritystatus must match the pattern '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : module_name equals 'CimCmdlets'\n                        : module_id equals '{fb6cc51d-c096-4b38-b78d-0fed6277096a}'\n                        : module_version equals '1.0.0.0'\n                        : verb equals 'Get'\n                        : noun equals 'CimInstance'\n                        : collected 'parameters' result: \n                        : collected 'select' result: \n                        : collected 'value' result: \n                        : !![ virtualizationbasedsecuritystatus = '1' ]!!\n\nResult Analysis         : virtualizationbasedsecuritystatus = '1' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to '2' \n","status":"open","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:253369"},"uuid":"367244A8-6BF8-1014-9D5C-E2ADA525D2B0","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253369","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253369","fix_text":"Virtualization-based security, including Credential Guard, currently cannot be implemented in virtual desktop implementations (VDI) due to specific supporting requirements including a TPM, UEFI with Secure Boot, and the capability to run the Hyper-V feature within the virtual desktop.\n\nFor VDIs where the virtual desktop instance is deleted or refreshed upon logoff, this is NA.\n\nConfigure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; System &gt;&gt; Device Guard &gt;&gt; \"Turn On virtualization-based Security\" to \"Enabled\" with \"Secure Boot\" or \"Secure Boot and DMA Protection\" selected for \"Select Platform Security Level:\".\n\nA Microsoft article on Credential Guard system requirement can be found at the following link.\nhttps://technet.microsoft.com/en-us/itpro/windows/keep-secure/credential-guard-requirements","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"id":"V-253369","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253369r991589_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"Confirm virtualization-based Security is enabled and running with Secure Boot or Secure Boot and DMA Protection.\n\nFor those devices that support virtualization-based security (VBS) features, including Credential Guard or protection of code integrity, this must be enabled. If the system meets the hardware and firmware dependencies for enabling VBS but it is not enabled, this is a CAT III finding.\n\nVirtualization-based security, including Credential Guard, currently cannot be implemented in virtual desktop implementations (VDI) due to specific supporting requirements including a TPM, UEFI with Secure Boot, and the capability to run the Hyper-V feature within the virtual desktop.\n\nFor VDIs where the virtual desktop instance is deleted or refreshed upon logoff, this is NA.\n\nRun \"PowerShell\" with elevated privileges (run as administrator).\n\nEnter the following:\n\n\"Get-CimInstance -ClassName Win32_DeviceGuard -Namespace root\\Microsoft\\Windows\\DeviceGuard\"\n\nIf \"RequiredSecurityProperties\" does not include a value of \"2\" indicating \"Secure Boot\" (e.g., \"{1, 2}\"), this is a finding.\n\nIf \"Secure Boot and DMA Protection\" is configured, \"3\" will also be displayed in the results (e.g., \"{1, 2, 3}\").\n\nIf \"VirtualizationBasedSecurityStatus\" is not a value of \"2\" indicating \"Running\", this is a finding.\n\nAlternately:\n\nRun \"System Information\".\n\nUnder \"System Summary\", verify the following:\n\nIf \"Device Guard virtualization-based security\" does not display \"Running\", this is finding.\n\nIf \"Device Guard Required Security Properties\" does not display \"Base Virtualization Support, Secure Boot\", this is finding.\n\nIf \"Secure Boot and DMA Protection\" is configured, \"DMA Protection\" will also be displayed (e.g., \"Base Virtualization Support, Secure Boot, DMA Protection\").\n\nThe policy settings referenced in the Fix section will configure the following registry values. However due to hardware requirements, the registry values alone do not ensure proper function.\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\DeviceGuard\\\n\nValue Name: EnableVirtualizationBasedSecurity\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1\n\nValue Name: RequirePlatformSecurityFeatures\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1 (Secure Boot only) or 3 (Secure Boot and DMA Protection)\n\nA Microsoft article on Credential Guard system requirement can be found at the following link:\n\nhttps://technet.microsoft.com/en-us/itpro/windows/keep-secure/credential-guard-requirements","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id":"SV-253369r991589","mitigation_control":"","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"rule_version":"WN11-CC-000070"},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Credential Guard must be running on Windows 11 domain-joined systems.)\nResult Analysis         :        securityservicesrunning = '{0}' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to '1' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25337001 (cmdlet_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Credential Guard must be running on Windows 11 domain-joined systems.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : One and only one item may match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25337001 (cmdlet_object)\nObject Comment          : DeviceGuard securityservicesrunning\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'module_name' must be equal to 'CimCmdlets'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'verb' must be equal to 'Get'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'noun' must be equal to 'CimInstance'\nObject Requirement      : for  'parameters' the following must be true:\n                        : classname must be equal to 'Win32_DeviceGuard'\n                        : namespace must be equal to 'root\\Microsoft\\Windows\\DeviceGuard'\nObject Requirement      : for  'select' the following must be true:\n                        : property must be equal to 'securityservicesrunning'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25337001 (cmdlet_state)\nState Comment           : securityservicesrunning contains 1 in array element\nState Requirement       : for all 'value' the following must be true:\n                        : all securityservicesrunning must match the pattern '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : module_name equals 'CimCmdlets'\n                        : module_id equals '{fb6cc51d-c096-4b38-b78d-0fed6277096a}'\n                        : module_version equals '1.0.0.0'\n                        : verb equals 'Get'\n                        : noun equals 'CimInstance'\n                        : collected 'parameters' result: \n                        : collected 'select' result: \n                        : collected 'value' result: \n                        : !![ securityservicesrunning = '{0}' ]!!\n\nResult Analysis         : securityservicesrunning = '{0}' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to '1' \n","mitigations":"","discussion":"Credential Guard uses virtualization-based security to protect information that could be used in credential theft attacks if compromised. This authentication information, which was stored in the Local Security Authority (LSA) in previous versions of Windows, is isolated from the rest of operating system and can only be accessed by privileged system software.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Credential Guard must be running on Windows 11 domain-joined systems.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253370","group_id":"V-253370","potential_impacts":"","fix_text":"Virtualization-based security, including Credential Guard, currently cannot be implemented in virtual desktop implementations (VDI) due to specific supporting requirements including a TPM, UEFI with Secure Boot, and the capability to run the Hyper-V feature within the virtual desktop.\n\nFor VDIs where the virtual desktop instance is deleted or refreshed upon logoff, this is NA.\n\nFor VDIs with persistent desktops, this may be downgraded to a CAT II only where administrators have specific tokens for the VDI. Administrator accounts on virtual desktops must only be used on systems in the VDI; they may not have administrative privileges on any other systems such as servers and physical workstations.\n\nConfigure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; System &gt;&gt; Device Guard &gt;&gt; \"Turn On virtualization-based Security\" to \"Enabled\" with \"Enabled with UEFI lock\" selected for \"Credential Guard Configuration:\".\n\n\nA Microsoft TechNet article on Credential Guard, including system requirement details, can be found at the following link:\n\nhttps://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/access-protection/credential-guard/credential-guard","status":"open","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:253370"},"uuid":"36724BCA-6BF8-1014-8E01-A0F512491408","rule_id_src":"SV-253370r991589_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"Confirm Credential Guard is running on domain-joined systems.\n\nFor those devices that support Credential Guard, this feature must be enabled. Organizations need to take the appropriate action to acquire and implement compatible hardware with Credential Guard enabled.\n\nVirtualization-based security, including Credential Guard, currently cannot be implemented in virtual desktop implementations (VDI) due to specific supporting requirements including a TPM, UEFI with Secure Boot, and the capability to run the Hyper-V feature within the virtual desktop.\n\nFor VDIs where the virtual desktop instance is deleted or refreshed upon logoff, this is NA.\n\nRun \"PowerShell\" with elevated privileges (run as administrator).\nEnter the following:\n\"Get-CimInstance -ClassName Win32_DeviceGuard -Namespace root\\Microsoft\\Windows\\DeviceGuard\"\n\nIf \"SecurityServicesRunning\" does not include a value of \"1\" (e.g., \"{1, 2}\"), this is a finding.\n\nAlternately:\n\nRun \"System Information\".\nUnder \"System Summary\", verify the following:\nIf \"virtualization-based Services Running\" does not list \"Credential Guard\", this is finding.\n\nThe policy settings referenced in the Fix section will configure the following registry value. However, due to hardware requirements, the registry value alone does not ensure proper function.\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\DeviceGuard\\\n\nValue Name: LsaCfgFlags\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1) (Enabled with UEFI lock)","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id":"SV-253370r991589","mitigation_control":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"id":"V-253370","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","rule_version":"WN11-CC-000075","severity":"high","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","ccis":["CCI-000366"]},{"comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253371r991589","check_content":"Confirm virtualization-based protection of code integrity.\n\nFor those devices that support the virtualization-based security (VBS) feature for protection of code integrity, this must be enabled. If the system meets the hardware, firmware and compatible device driver dependencies for enabling virtualization-based protection of code integrity but it is not enabled, this is a CAT II finding.\n\nVirtualization-based security currently cannot be implemented in virtual desktop implementations (VDI) due to specific supporting requirements including a TPM, UEFI with Secure Boot, and the capability to run the Hyper-V feature within the virtual desktop.\n\nFor VDIs where the virtual desktop instance is deleted or refreshed upon logoff, this is NA.\n\nRun \"PowerShell\" with elevated privileges (run as administrator).\nEnter the following:\n\"Get-CimInstance -ClassName Win32_DeviceGuard -Namespace root\\Microsoft\\Windows\\DeviceGuard\"\n\nIf \"SecurityServicesRunning\" does not include a value of \"2\" (e.g., \"{1, 2}\"), this is a finding.\n\nAlternately:\n\nRun \"System Information\".\nUnder \"System Summary\", verify the following:\nIf \"Virtualization-based Security Services Running\" does not list \"Hypervisor enforced Code Integrity\", this is finding.\n\nThe policy settings referenced in the Fix section will configure the following registry value. However due to hardware requirements, the registry value alone does not ensure proper function.\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\DeviceGuard\\\n\nValue Name: HypervisorEnforcedCodeIntegrity\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1) (Enabled with UEFI lock), or 0x00000002 (2) (Enabled without lock)","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253371r991589_rule","responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253371","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","rule_version":"WN11-CC-000080","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","severity":"medium","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Verify SecurityServicesRunning includes a value of 2)\nResult Analysis         :        securityservicesrunning = '{0}' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to '2' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25337101 (cmdlet_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Verify SecurityServicesRunning includes a value of 2\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25337101 (cmdlet_object)\nObject Comment          : DeviceGuard SecurityServicesRunning\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'module_name' must be equal to 'CimCmdlets'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'verb' must be equal to 'Get'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'noun' must be equal to 'CimInstance'\nObject Requirement      : for  'parameters' the following must be true:\n                        : classname must be equal to 'Win32_DeviceGuard'\n                        : namespace must be equal to 'root\\Microsoft\\Windows\\DeviceGuard'\nObject Requirement      : for  'select' the following must be true:\n                        : property must be equal to 'securityservicesrunning'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25337101 (cmdlet_state)\nState Comment           : SecurityServicesRunning equal to 2 as formatted array element\nState Requirement       : for all 'value' the following must be true:\n                        : all securityservicesrunning must match the pattern '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : module_name equals 'CimCmdlets'\n                        : module_id equals '{fb6cc51d-c096-4b38-b78d-0fed6277096a}'\n                        : module_version equals '1.0.0.0'\n                        : verb equals 'Get'\n                        : noun equals 'CimInstance'\n                        : collected 'parameters' result: \n                        : collected 'select' result: \n                        : collected 'value' result: \n                        : !![ securityservicesrunning = '{0}' ]!!\n\nResult Analysis         : securityservicesrunning = '{0}' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to '2' \n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","discussion":"Virtualization-based protection of code integrity enforces kernel mode memory protections as well as protecting Code Integrity validation paths. This isolates the processes from the rest of the operating system and can only be accessed by privileged system software.","mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Virtualization-based protection of code integrity must be enabled.","fix_text":"Virtualization-based security currently cannot be implemented in virtual desktop implementations (VDI) due to specific supporting requirements including a TPM, UEFI with Secure Boot, and the capability to run the Hyper-V feature within the virtual desktop.\n\nFor VDIs where the virtual desktop instance is deleted or refreshed upon logoff, this is NA.\n\nConfigure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; System &gt;&gt; Device Guard &gt;&gt; \"Turn On virtualization-based Security\" to \"Enabled\" with \"Enabled with UEFI lock\" or \"Enabled without lock\" selected for \"virtualization-based Protection of Code Integrity:\".\n\n\"Enabled with UEFI lock\" is preferred as more secure, however it cannot be turned off remotely through a group policy change if there is an issue.\n\n\"Enabled without lock\" will allow this to be turned off remotely while testing for issues.","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253371","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253371","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:253371"},"uuid":"3672543E-6BF8-1014-BEE4-D2E697F17622","status":"open"},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Boot-Start Driver Initialization Policy' is not set to 'Enabled' with 'All' selected)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25337200 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Boot-Start Driver Initialization Policy' is not set to 'Enabled' with 'All' selected\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\nState Operator          : One or more item-state comparisons may be true.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25337200 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'System\\CurrentControlSet\\Policies\\EarlyLaunch'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DriverLoadPolicy'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000003 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '3'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25337200 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Reg_Dword type and value equals 8\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '8'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'System\\CurrentControlSet\\Policies\\EarlyLaunch'\n                        : name equals 'DriverLoadPolicy'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '3'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","mitigations":"","discussion":"The default behavior is for Early Launch Antimalware - Boot-Start Driver Initialization policy is to enforce \"Good, unknown and bad but critical\" (preventing \"bad\"). By being launched first by the kernel, ELAM ( Early Launch Antimalware) is ensured to be launched before any third-party software, and is therefore able to detect malware in the boot process and prevent it from initializing.","rule_title":"Early Launch Antimalware, Boot-Start Driver Initialization Policy must prevent boot drivers.","security_override_guidance":"","fix_text":"Ensure that Early Launch Antimalware - Boot-Start Driver Initialization policy is set to enforce \"Good, unknown and bad but critical\" (preventing \"bad\").\n\nTo correct this, configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; System &gt;&gt; Early Launch Antimalware &gt;&gt; \"Boot-Start Driver Initialization Policy\" to \"Enabled with \"Good, unknown and bad but critical\" selected.","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253372","group_id":"V-253372","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253372","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"uuid":"36726047-6BF8-1014-9D74-8A3434793A66","status":"not_a_finding","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id":"SV-253372r991589","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253372r991589_rule","check_content":"The default behavior is for Early Launch Antimalware - Boot-Start Driver Initialization policy is to enforce \"Good, unknown and bad but critical\" (preventing \"bad\").\n\nIf the registry value name below does not exist, this is a finding.\n\nIf it exists and is configured with a value of \"7\", this is a finding.\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Policies\\EarlyLaunch\\\n\nValue Name: DriverLoadPolicy\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1, 3, or 8 \n\nPossible values for this setting are:\n8 - Good only\n1 - Good and unknown\n3 - Good, unknown and bad but critical\n7 - All (which includes \"Bad\" and would be a finding)","ia_controls":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-253372"},"reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN11-CC-000085","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},{"ccis":["CCI-000366"],"group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","severity":"medium","rule_version":"WN11-CC-000090","responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253373","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253373r991589","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Group Policy\\{35378EAC-683F-11D2-A89A-00C04FBBCFA2}\n\nValue Name: NoGPOListChanges\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253373r991589_rule","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253373"},"uuid":"36726904-6BF8-1014-810B-B7E77BE4FE1F","status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; System &gt;&gt; Group Policy &gt;&gt; \"Configure registry policy processing\" to \"Enabled\" and select the option \"Process even if the Group Policy objects have not changed\".","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253373","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253373","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","discussion":"Enabling this setting and then selecting the \"Process even if the Group Policy objects have not changed\" option ensures that the policies will be reprocessed even if none have been changed. This way, any unauthorized changes are forced to match the domain-based group policy settings again.","mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Group Policy objects must be reprocessed even if they have not changed.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (NoGPOistChanges is set to 0.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25337300 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : NoGPOistChanges is set to 0.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25337300 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Group Policy\\{35378EAC-683F-11D2-A89A-00C04FBBCFA2}'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'NoGPOListChanges'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Group Policy\\{35378EAC-683F-11D2-A89A-00C04FBBCFA2}'\n                        : name equals 'NoGPOListChanges'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n"},{"ccis":["CCI-000381"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","rule_version":"WN11-CC-000100","group_tree":{"id":"V-253374","title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049"},"responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","rule_id":"SV-253374r958478","mitigation_control":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id_src":"SV-253374r958478_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\Printers\\\n\nValue Name: DisableWebPnPDownload\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1","uuid":"367270E7-6BF8-1014-9F9D-E35D01C617A0","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253374"},"status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; System &gt;&gt; Internet Communication Management &gt;&gt; Internet Communication settings &gt;&gt; \"Turn off downloading of print drivers over HTTP\" to \"Enabled\".","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253374","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253374","false_positives":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Downloading print driver packages over HTTP must be prevented.","mitigations":"","discussion":"Some features may communicate with the vendor, sending system information or downloading data or components for the feature. Turning off this capability will prevent potentially sensitive information from being sent outside the enterprise and uncontrolled updates to the system. This setting prevents the computer from downloading print driver packages over HTTP.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Turn off downloading of print drivers over HTTP' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25337400 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Turn off downloading of print drivers over HTTP' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25337400 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\Printers'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisableWebPnPDownload'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\Printers'\n                        : name equals 'DisableWebPnPDownload'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n"},{"false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253375","group_id":"V-253375","potential_impacts":"","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; System &gt;&gt; Internet Communication Management &gt;&gt; Internet Communication settings &gt;&gt; \"Turn off Internet download for Web publishing and online ordering wizards\" to \"Enabled\".","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253375","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"uuid":"367278B4-6BF8-1014-9250-8F23233B01CA","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Turn off Internet download for Web publishing and online ordering wizards' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25337500 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Turn off Internet download for Web publishing and online ordering wizards' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25337500 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\Explorer'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'NoWebServices'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\Explorer'\n                        : name equals 'NoWebServices'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","mitigations":"","discussion":"Some features may communicate with the vendor, sending system information or downloading data or components for the feature. Turning off this capability will prevent potentially sensitive information from being sent outside the enterprise and uncontrolled updates to the system. This setting prevents Windows from downloading a list of providers for the Web publishing and online ordering wizards.","rule_title":"Web publishing and online ordering wizards must be prevented from downloading a list of providers.","security_override_guidance":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","rule_version":"WN11-CC-000105","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"rule_id_src":"SV-253375r958478_rule","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\Explorer\\\n\nValue Name: NoWebServices\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1","ia_controls":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id":"SV-253375r958478","mitigation_control":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","id":"V-253375"},"reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":""},{"rule_title":"Printing over HTTP must be prevented.","security_override_guidance":"","mitigations":"","discussion":"Some features may communicate with the vendor, sending system information or downloading data or components for the feature. Turning off this capability will prevent potentially sensitive information from being sent outside the enterprise and uncontrolled updates to the system. This setting prevents the client computer from printing over HTTP, which allows the computer to print to printers on the intranet as well as the internet.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Turn off printing over HTTP' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25337600 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Turn off printing over HTTP' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25337600 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\Printers'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisableHTTPPrinting'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\Printers'\n                        : name equals 'DisableHTTPPrinting'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"36728097-6BF8-1014-8FAE-8E8F188BAB1A","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253376","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"group_id":"V-253376","potential_impacts":"","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253376","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; System &gt;&gt; Internet Communication Management &gt;&gt; Internet Communication settings &gt;&gt; \"Turn off printing over HTTP\" to \"Enabled\".","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"id":"V-253376","title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049"},"third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253376r958478_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\Printers\\\n\nValue Name: DisableHTTPPrinting\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1","rule_id":"SV-253376r958478","mitigation_control":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"rule_version":"WN11-CC-000110"},{"legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253377","group_id":"V-253377","potential_impacts":"","fix_text":"This requirement is applicable to domain-joined systems, for standalone systems this is NA.\n\nThe default behavior for \"Support device authentication using certificate\" is \"Automatic\".\n\nTo correct this, configured the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; System &gt;&gt; Kerberos &gt;&gt; \"Support device authentication using certificate\" to \"Not Configured or \"Enabled\" with either option selected in \"Device authentication behavior using certificate:\".","status":"not_applicable","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253377"},"uuid":"36728888-6BF8-1014-9521-EDC74D4CC0D2","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","mitigations":"","discussion":"Using certificates to authenticate devices to the domain provides increased security over passwords. By default systems will attempt to authenticate using certificates and fall back to passwords if the domain controller does not support certificates for devices. This may also be configured to always use certificates for device authentication.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Systems must at least attempt device authentication using certificates.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","rule_version":"WN11-CC-000115","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"rule_id_src":"SV-253377r991589_rule","check_content":"This requirement is applicable to domain-joined systems, for standalone systems this is NA.\n\nThe default behavior for \"Support device authentication using certificate\" is \"Automatic\".\n\nIf it exists and is configured with a value of \"0\", this is a finding.\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System\\Kerberos\\Parameters\\\n\nValue Name: DevicePKInitEnabled\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1 (or if the Value Name does not exist)","ia_controls":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id":"SV-253377r991589","mitigation_control":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-253377"},"reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":""},{"rule_title":"The network selection user interface (UI) must not be displayed on the logon screen.","security_override_guidance":"","mitigations":"","discussion":"Enabling interaction with the network selection UI allows users to change connections to available networks without signing into Windows.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Verifies 'Do not display network selection UI' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25337800 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Verifies 'Do not display network selection UI' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25337800 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\System\\DontDisplayNetworkSelectionUI\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\System'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DontDisplayNetworkSelectionUI'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\System'\n                        : name equals 'DontDisplayNetworkSelectionUI'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"367290A6-6BF8-1014-9254-929A22873F74","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253378"},"group_id":"V-253378","potential_impacts":"","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253378","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; System &gt;&gt; Logon &gt;&gt; \"Do not display network selection UI\" to \"Enabled\".","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","id":"V-253378"},"reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253378r958478_rule","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\System\\\n\nValue Name: DontDisplayNetworkSelectionUI\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1","ia_controls":"","rule_id":"SV-253378r958478","mitigation_control":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"rule_version":"WN11-CC-000120"},{"group_tree":{"id":"V-253379","title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049"},"reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","rule_id":"SV-253379r958478","mitigation_control":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id_src":"SV-253379r958478_rule","check_content":"This requirement is applicable to domain-joined systems, for standalone systems this is NA.\n\nIf the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\System\\\n\nValue Name: EnumerateLocalUsers\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0","ia_controls":"","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","rule_version":"WN11-CC-000130","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","rule_title":"Local users on domain-joined computers must not be enumerated.","security_override_guidance":"","mitigations":"","discussion":"The username is one part of logon credentials that could be used to gain access to a system. Preventing the enumeration of users limits this information to authorized personnel.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","uuid":"3672985A-6BF8-1014-9F86-E60781C727D3","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253379"},"status":"not_applicable","fix_text":"This requirement is applicable to domain-joined systems, for standalone systems this is NA.\n\nConfigure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; System &gt;&gt; Logon &gt;&gt; \"Enumerate local users on domain-joined computers\" to \"Disabled\".","group_id":"V-253379","potential_impacts":"","group_id_src":"V-253379","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":""},{"rule_version":"WN11-CC-000145","group_title":"SRG-OS-000373-GPOS-00156","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-002038"],"ia_controls":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Power\\PowerSettings\\0e796bdb-100d-47d6-a2d5-f7d2daa51f51\\\n\nValue Name: DCSettingIndex\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1","rule_id_src":"SV-253380r1051049_rule","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253380r1051049","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253380","title":"SRG-OS-000373-GPOS-00156"},"group_id":"V-253380","potential_impacts":"","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253380","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; System &gt;&gt; Power Management &gt;&gt; Sleep Settings &gt;&gt; \"Require a password when a computer wakes (on battery)\" to \"Enabled\".","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"36729F9