 windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","rule_title":"Autoplay must be disabled for all drives.","security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"Allowing autoplay to execute may introduce malicious code to a system. Autoplay begins reading from a drive as soon as media is inserted in the drive. As a result, the setup file of programs or music on audio media may start. By default, autoplay is disabled on removable drives, such as the floppy disk drive (but not the CD-ROM drive) and on network drives. If this policy is enabled, autoplay can be disabled on all drives.","mitigations":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4"},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Configure enhanced anti-spoofing' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25338900 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Configure enhanced anti-spoofing' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25338900 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Biometrics\\FacialFeatures'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'EnhancedAntiSpoofing'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Biometrics\\FacialFeatures'\n                        : name equals 'EnhancedAntiSpoofing'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","rule_title":"Enhanced anti-spoofing for facial recognition must be enabled on Windows 11.","security_override_guidance":"","mitigations":"","discussion":"Enhanced anti-spoofing provides additional protections when using facial recognition with devices that support it.","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Biometrics &gt;&gt; Facial Features &gt;&gt; \"Configure enhanced anti-spoofing\" to \"Enabled\".","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253389","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253389","uuid":"3672E314-6BF8-1014-8CF9-BE57CEDC3701","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253389"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id":"SV-253389r991589","mitigation_control":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id_src":"SV-253389r991589_rule","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Biometrics\\FacialFeatures\\\n\nValue Name: EnhancedAntiSpoofing\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)","ia_controls":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253389","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN11-CC-000195","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},{"fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Cloud Content &gt;&gt; \"Turn off Microsoft consumer experiences\" to \"Enabled\".","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253390","false_positives":"","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253390","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253390"},"uuid":"3672EAA0-6BF8-1014-9F20-C7A529A3CF36","status":"not_a_finding","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Turn off Microsoft consumer experiences' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25339000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Turn off Microsoft consumer experiences' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25339000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CloudContent'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisableWindowsConsumerFeatures'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CloudContent'\n                        : name equals 'DisableWindowsConsumerFeatures'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","mitigations":"","discussion":"Microsoft consumer experiences provides suggestions and notifications to users, which may include the installation of Windows Store apps. Organizations may control the execution of applications through other means such as allowlisting. Turning off Microsoft consumer experiences will help prevent the unwanted installation of suggested applications.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Microsoft consumer experiences must be turned off.","rule_version":"WN11-CC-000197","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"severity":"low","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id":"SV-253390r958478","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253390r958478_rule","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CloudContent\\\n\nValue Name: DisableWindowsConsumerFeatures\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)","ia_controls":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253390","title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049"},"third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0"},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Enumerate administrator accounts on elevation' is set to 'Disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25339100 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Enumerate administrator accounts on elevation' is set to 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25339100 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\CredUI'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'EnumerateAdministrators'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\CredUI'\n                        : name equals 'EnumerateAdministrators'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","mitigations":"","discussion":"Enumeration of administrator accounts when elevating can provide part of the logon information to an unauthorized user. This setting configures the system to always require users to type in a username and password to elevate a running application.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Administrator accounts must not be enumerated during elevation.","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Credential User Interface &gt;&gt; \"Enumerate administrator accounts on elevation\" to \"Disabled\".","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253391","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253391","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253391","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"uuid":"3672F23D-6BF8-1014-AAE4-BB488687B434","status":"not_a_finding","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id":"SV-253391r958518","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253391r958518_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\CredUI\\\n\nValue Name: EnumerateAdministrators\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000134-GPOS-00068","id":"V-253391"},"responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN11-CC-000200","ccis":["CCI-001084"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000134-GPOS-00068"},{"stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Enhanced diagnostic data must be limited to the minimum required to support Windows Analytics.","mitigations":"","discussion":"Some features may communicate with the vendor, sending system information or downloading data or components for the feature. Limiting this capability will prevent potentially sensitive information from being sent outside the enterprise. The \"Enhanced\" level for telemetry includes additional information beyond \"Security\" and \"Basic\" on how Windows and apps are used and advanced reliability data. Windows Analytics can use a \"limited enhanced\" level to provide information such as health data for devices.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nTest                    :   true (Enhanced diagnostic data must be limited to the minimum required to support Windows Analytics.)\nTest                    :   false (Enhanced diagnostic data must be limited to the minimum required to support Windows Analytics.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25339201 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Enhanced diagnostic data must be limited to the minimum required to support Windows Analytics.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : At least one collected item must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25339201 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : DataCollection LimitEnhancedDiagnosticDataWindowsAnalytics Setting\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\DataCollection'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'LimitEnhancedDiagnosticDataWindowsAnalytics'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25339201 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Value Equal To 1\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\DataCollection'\n                        : name equals 'LimitEnhancedDiagnosticDataWindowsAnalytics'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25339202 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Enhanced diagnostic data must be limited to the minimum required to support Windows Analytics.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : At least one collected item must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25339202 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : DataCollection AllowTelemetry Setting\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\DataCollection'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'AllowTelemetry'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25339202 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Value Equal To 1\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be less than or equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\DataCollection'\n                        : name equals 'AllowTelemetry'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '2'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\n","uuid":"3672FC35-6BF8-1014-BDA1-A0F065A9540A","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:253392"},"status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Data Collection and Preview Builds &gt;&gt; \"Limit optional diagnostic data for Windows Analytics\" to \"Enabled\" with \"Enable Desktop Analytics collection\" selected in \"Options:\".","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253392","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253392","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-253392"},"reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","rule_id":"SV-253392r991589","mitigation_control":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id_src":"SV-253392r991589_rule","check_content":"If \"Enhanced\" level is enabled for telemetry, this must be configured. If \"Security\" or \"Basic\" are configured, this is NA. (See WN11-CC-000205).\n\nIf the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\DataCollection\\\n\nValue Name: LimitEnhancedDiagnosticDataWindowsAnalytics\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)","ia_controls":"","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","rule_version":"WN11-CC-000204"},{"security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Telemetry must not be configured to Full.","mitigations":"","discussion":"Some features may communicate with the vendor, sending system information or downloading data or components for the feature. Limiting this capability will prevent potentially sensitive information from being sent outside the enterprise. The \"Security\" option for Telemetry configures the lowest amount of data, effectively none outside of the Malicious Software Removal Tool (MSRT), Defender and telemetry client settings. \"Basic\" sends basic diagnostic and usage data and may be required to support some Microsoft services. \"Enhanced\" includes additional information on how Windows and apps are used and advanced reliability data. Windows Analytics can use a \"limited enhanced\" level to provide information such as health data for devices.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     false ('Allow Diagnostic Data' is set to 'Enabled' with 'Diagnostic Data Off (Not recommended)' or 'Send Required Diagnostic Data' selected in 'Options:')\nResult Analysis         :          HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\DataCollection\\AllowTelemetry\\value = '2' failed test of 'equals' compared to '1' \n                        : HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\DataCollection\\AllowTelemetry\\value = '2' failed test of 'equals' compared to '0' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25339300 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : 'Allow Diagnostic Data' is set to 'Enabled' with 'Diagnostic Data Off (Not recommended)' or 'Send Required Diagnostic Data' selected in 'Options:'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\nState Operator          : One or more item-state comparisons may be true.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25339300 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\DataCollection'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'AllowTelemetry'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\DataCollection'\n                        : name equals 'AllowTelemetry'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '2'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\nResult Analysis         : HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\DataCollection\\AllowTelemetry\\value = '2' failed test of 'equals' compared to '1' \n                        : HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\DataCollection\\AllowTelemetry\\value = '2' failed test of 'equals' compared to '0' \n","status":"open","uuid":"3673047D-6BF8-1014-AD3C-B8C4B9B262A4","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253393"},"potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253393","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253393","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Data Collection and Preview Builds &gt;&gt; \"Allow Diagnostic Data\" to \"Enabled\" with \"Send required diagnostic data\" selected in \"Options:\".","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"id":"V-253393","title":"SRG-OS-000205-GPOS-00083"},"third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253393r958564_rule","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\DataCollection\\\n\nValue Name: AllowTelemetry\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000000 (0) (Security)\n0x00000001 (1) (Basic)","ia_controls":"","rule_id":"SV-253393r958564","mitigation_control":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000205-GPOS-00083","ccis":["CCI-001312"],"rule_version":"WN11-CC-000205"},{"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-253394"},"ia_controls":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\DeliveryOptimization\\\n\nValue Name: DODownloadMode\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000000 (0) - No peering (HTTP Only)\n0x00000001 (1) - Peers on same NAT only (LAN)\n0x00000002 (2) - Local Network / Private group peering (Group)\n0x00000063 (99) - Simple download mode, no peering (Simple)\n0x00000064 (100) - Bypass mode, Delivery Optimization not used (Bypass)\n\nA value of 0x00000003 (3), Internet, is a finding.\n\nStandalone systems (configured in Settings):\nIf the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\DeliveryOptimization\\Config\\\n\nValue Name: DODownloadMode\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000000 (0) - Off\n0x00000001 (1) - LAN","rule_id_src":"SV-253394r991589_rule","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253394r991589","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","severity":"low","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"rule_version":"WN11-CC-000206","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows Update must not obtain updates from other PCs on the internet.","discussion":"Windows 11 allows Windows Update to obtain updates from additional sources instead of Microsoft. In addition to Microsoft, updates can be obtained from and sent to PCs on the local network as well as on the Internet. This is part of the Windows Update trusted process, however to minimize outside exposure, obtaining updates from or sending to systems on the internet must be prevented.","mitigations":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nCriteria                :     false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :       true (The system is a Windows Standalone Workstation or Server)\nTest                    :       false ('DownloadMode' is set to 'Enabled' with 'HTTP only or LAN' selected.)\nCriteria                :     true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :       true ('DownloadMode' is set to 'Enabled' with 'HTTP only, LAN, Group, Simple or Bypass' selected.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25339402 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The system is a Windows Standalone Workstation or Server\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\nState Operator          : One or more item-state comparisons may be true.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:10000100 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT DomainRole FROM win32_computersystem'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:10000100 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : Standalone Workstation\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all domainrole must be equal to '0'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:10000300 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : Standalone Server\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all domainrole must be equal to '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT DomainRole FROM win32_computersystem'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : domainrole = '0'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25339403 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : 'DownloadMode' is set to 'Enabled' with 'HTTP only or LAN' selected.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\nState Operator          : One or more item-state comparisons may be true.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25339401 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : DownloadMode set through the Settings App\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\DeliveryOptimization\\Config'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DODownloadMode'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25339401 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'DownloadMode' is set to 'Enabled' with 'HTTP only, LAN, Group, Simple or Bypass' selected.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\nState Operator          : One or more item-state comparisons may be true.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25339400 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\DeliveryOptimization'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DODownloadMode'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000002 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '2'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25339400 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Reg_Dword type and value equals 99\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '99'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25339401 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Reg_Dword type and value equals 100\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '100'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\DeliveryOptimization'\n                        : name equals 'DODownloadMode'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '100'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"36730BB3-6BF8-1014-8924-BED504A905A4","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253394","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"group_id":"V-253394","potential_impacts":"","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253394","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Delivery Optimization &gt;&gt; \"Download Mode\" to \"Enabled\" with any option except \"Internet\" selected.\n\nAcceptable selections include:\nBypass (100)\nGroup (2)\nHTTP only (0)\nLAN (1)\nSimple (99)\n\n."},{"third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","id":"V-253395"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253395r958478","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"check_content":"This is applicable to unclassified systems, for other systems this is NA.\n\nIf the following registry values do not exist or are not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\System\\\n\nValue Name: EnableSmartScreen\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)\n\nAnd\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\System\\\n\nValue Name: ShellSmartScreenLevel\n\nValue Type: REG_SZ\nValue: Block","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253395r958478_rule","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","severity":"medium","rule_version":"WN11-CC-000210","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","rule_title":"The Microsoft Defender SmartScreen for Explorer must be enabled.","security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"Microsoft Defender SmartScreen helps protect systems from programs downloaded from the internet that may be malicious. Enabling Microsoft Defender SmartScreen will warn or prevent users from running potentially malicious programs.","mitigations":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Configure Windows SmartScreen' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25339500 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Configure Windows SmartScreen' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25339500 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\System'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'EnableSmartScreen'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\System'\n                        : name equals 'EnableSmartScreen'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","uuid":"36732F49-6BF8-1014-8EB6-E253D823E772","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253395","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; File Explorer &gt;&gt; \"Configure Windows Defender SmartScreen\" to \"Enabled\" with \"Warn and prevent bypass\" selected. \n\nWindows 11 includes duplicate policies for this setting. It can also be configured under Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Windows Defender SmartScreen &gt;&gt; Explorer.","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253395","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253395"},{"mitigations":"","discussion":"Data Execution Prevention (DEP) provides additional protection by performing checks on memory to help prevent malicious code from running. This setting will prevent Data Execution Prevention from being turned off for File Explorer.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Explorer Data Execution Prevention must be enabled.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Turn off Data Execution Prevention for Explorer' is set to 'Disabled' or 'Not Configured')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25339600 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Turn off Data Execution Prevention for Explorer' is set to 'Disabled' or 'Not Configured'\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25339600 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Explorer'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'NoDataExecutionPrevention'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Explorer'\n                        : name equals 'NoDataExecutionPrevention'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253396","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"uuid":"36733B53-6BF8-1014-A5D3-BADA8DF49F15","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253396","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253396","fix_text":"The default behavior is for data execution prevention to be turned on for file explorer.\n\nTo correct this, configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; File Explorer &gt;&gt; \"Turn off Data Execution Prevention for Explorer\" to \"Not Configured\" or \"Disabled\".","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"id":"V-253396","title":"SRG-OS-000433-GPOS-00192"},"third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253396r958928_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"The default behavior is for data execution prevention to be turned on for file explorer.\n\nIf it exists and is configured with a value of \"1\", this is a finding.\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Explorer\\\n\nValue Name: NoDataExecutionPrevention\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0 (or if the Value Name does not exist)","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id":"SV-253396r958928","mitigation_control":"","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000433-GPOS-00192","ccis":["CCI-002824"],"rule_version":"WN11-CC-000215"},{"comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253397r958902","ia_controls":"","check_content":"The default behavior is for File Explorer heap termination on corruption to be enabled.\n\nIf it exists and is configured with a value of \"1\", this is a finding.\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Explorer\\\n\nValue Name: NoHeapTerminationOnCorruption\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000000 (0) (or if the Value Name does not exist)","rule_id_src":"SV-253397r958902_rule","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253397","title":"SRG-OS-000420-GPOS-00186"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","rule_version":"WN11-CC-000220","ccis":["CCI-002385"],"group_title":"SRG-OS-000420-GPOS-00186","severity":"low","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Turn off heap termination on corruption' is set to 'Not Configured' or 'Disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25339700 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Turn off heap termination on corruption' is set to 'Not Configured' or 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25339700 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Explorer'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'NoHeapTerminationOnCorruption'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","discussion":"Legacy plug-in applications may continue to function when a File Explorer session has become corrupt. Disabling this feature will prevent this.","mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"File Explorer heap termination on corruption must be disabled.","fix_text":"The default behavior is for File Explorer heap termination on corruption to be enabled.\n\nTo correct this, configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; File Explorer &gt;&gt; \"Turn off heap termination on corruption\" to \"Not Configured\" or \"Disabled\".","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253397","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253397","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253397"},"uuid":"3673431B-6BF8-1014-8DEF-DC906687CE85","status":"not_a_finding"},{"ccis":["CCI-000366"],"group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","severity":"medium","rule_version":"WN11-CC-000225","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253398","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253398r991589","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"ia_controls":"","check_content":"The default behavior is for shell protected mode to be turned on for file explorer.\n\nIf it exists and is configured with a value of \"1\", this is a finding.\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\Explorer\\\n\nValue Name: PreXPSP2ShellProtocolBehavior\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0 (or if the Value Name does not exist)","rule_id_src":"SV-253398r991589_rule","uuid":"36734BFC-6BF8-1014-9E73-9BF2774A30D8","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253398"},"status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"The default behavior is for shell protected mode to be turned on for file explorer.\n\nTo correct this, configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; File Explorer &gt;&gt; \"Turn off shell protocol protected mode\" to \"Not Configured\" or \"Disabled\".","group_id":"V-253398","potential_impacts":"","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253398","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","rule_title":"File Explorer shell protocol must run in protected mode.","security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"The shell protocol will limit the set of folders applications can open when run in protected mode. Restricting files an application can open, to a limited set of folders, increases the security of Windows.","mitigations":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Turn off shell protocol protected mode' is set to 'Disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25339800 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Turn off shell protocol protected mode' is set to 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25339800 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\Explorer'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'PreXPSP2ShellProtocolBehavior'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n"},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Enables or disables Windows Game Recording and Broadcasting' is set to 'Disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25339900 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Enables or disables Windows Game Recording and Broadcasting' is set to 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25339900 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\GameDVR'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'AllowGameDVR'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\GameDVR'\n                        : name equals 'AllowGameDVR'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows 11 must be configured to disable Windows Game Recording and Broadcasting.","discussion":"Windows Game Recording and Broadcasting is intended for use with games; however, it could potentially record screen shots of other applications and expose sensitive data. Disabling the feature will prevent this from occurring.","mitigations":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253399","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253399","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Windows Game Recording and Broadcasting &gt;&gt; \"Enables or disables Windows Game Recording and Broadcasting\" to \"Disabled\".","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"367353FC-6BF8-1014-9ECF-A4AB7583485B","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253399"},"check_content":"This is NA for Windows 11 LTSC. \n                \nIf the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\GameDVR\\\n\nValue Name: AllowGameDVR\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000000 (0)","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253399r958478_rule","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253399r958478","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","id":"V-253399"},"rule_version":"WN11-CC-000252","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-000381"]},{"ccis":["CCI-000366"],"group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","severity":"medium","rule_version":"WN11-CC-000255","third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253400","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253400r991589","ia_controls":"","check_content":"Virtual desktop implementations currently may not support the use of TPMs. For virtual desktop implementations where the virtual desktop instance is deleted or refreshed upon logoff, this is NA.\n\nIf the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\PassportForWork\\\n\nValue Name: RequireSecurityDevice\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1","rule_id_src":"SV-253400r991589_rule","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253400"},"uuid":"36735B7D-6BF8-1014-A2B6-F9B7374BF410","status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Windows Hello for Business &gt;&gt; \"Use a hardware security device\" to \"Enabled\".","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253400","group_id":"V-253400","potential_impacts":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","discussion":"The use of a Trusted Platform Module (TPM) to store keys for Windows Hello for Business provides additional security. Keys stored in the TPM may only be used on that system while keys stored using software are more susceptible to compromise and could be used on other systems.","mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The use of a hardware security device with Windows Hello for Business must be enabled.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Us