"discussion":"Standard user accounts must not be granted elevated privileges. Enabling Windows Installer to elevate privileges when installing applications can allow malicious persons and applications to gain full control of a system.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The Windows Installer feature \"Always install with elevated privileges\" must be disabled.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4"},{"ccis":["CCI-000366"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","rule_version":"WN11-CC-000320","group_tree":{"id":"V-253412","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","rule_id":"SV-253412r991589","mitigation_control":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id_src":"SV-253412r991589_rule","check_content":"The default behavior is for Internet Explorer to warn users and select whether to allow or refuse installation when a web-based program attempts to install software on the system.\n\nIf it exists and is configured with a value of \"1\", this is a finding.\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Installer\\\n\nValue Name: SafeForScripting\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0 (or if the Value Name does not exist)","ia_controls":"","uuid":"3673B5AA-6BF8-1014-B806-853F66BC38E2","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253412","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"The default behavior is for Internet Explorer to warn users and select whether to allow or refuse installation when a web-based program attempts to install software on the system.\n\nTo correct this, configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Windows Installer &gt;&gt; \"Prevent Internet Explorer security prompt for Windows Installer scripts\" to \"Not Configured\" or \"Disabled\".","group_id":"V-253412","potential_impacts":"","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253412","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Users must be notified if a web-based program attempts to install software.","mitigations":"","discussion":"Web-based programs may attempt to install malicious software on a system. Ensuring users are notified if a web-based program attempts to install software allows them to refuse the installation.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Prevent Internet Explorer security prompt for Windows Installer scripts' is set to 'Not Configured' or 'Disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25341200 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Prevent Internet Explorer security prompt for Windows Installer scripts' is set to 'Not Configured' or 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25341200 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Installer'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'SafeForScripting'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n"},{"stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Automatically signing in the last interactive user after a system-initiated restart must be disabled.","mitigations":"","discussion":"Windows can be configured to automatically sign the user back in after a Windows Update restart. Some protections are in place to help ensure this is done in a secure fashion; however, disabling this will prevent the caching of credentials for this purpose and also ensure the user is aware of the restart.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Verifies 'Sign-in last interactive user automatically after a system-initiated restart' is set to 'Disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25341300 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Verifies 'Sign-in last interactive user automatically after a system-initiated restart' is set to 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25341300 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisableAutomaticRestartSignOn'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\n                        : name equals 'DisableAutomaticRestartSignOn'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","uuid":"3673BCAD-6BF8-1014-A500-D232C1AEEBDA","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253413"},"status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Windows Logon Options &gt;&gt; \"Sign-in last interactive user automatically after a system-initiated restart\" to \"Disabled\".","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253413","group_id_src":"V-253413","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00229","id":"V-253413"},"reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","rule_id":"SV-253413r991591","mitigation_control":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id_src":"SV-253413r991591_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System\\\n\nValue Name: DisableAutomaticRestartSignOn\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00229","rule_version":"WN11-CC-000325"},{"uuid":"3673C3F7-6BF8-1014-A545-E0FE3CA02116","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253414"},"status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Windows PowerShell &gt;&gt; \"Turn on PowerShell Script Block Logging\" to \"Enabled\".","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253414","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253414","false_positives":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"PowerShell script block logging must be enabled on Windows 11.","discussion":"Maintaining an audit trail of system activity logs can help identify configuration errors, troubleshoot service disruptions, and analyze compromises that have occurred, as well as detect attacks. Audit logs are necessary to provide a trail of evidence in case the system or network is compromised. Collecting this data is essential for analyzing the security of information assets and detecting signs of suspicious and unexpected behavior.\n\nEnabling PowerShell script block logging will record detailed information from the processing of PowerShell commands and scripts. This can provide additional detail when malware has run on a system.","mitigations":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Turn on PowerShell Script Block Logging' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25341400 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Turn on PowerShell Script Block Logging' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25341400 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\PowerShell\\ScriptBlockLogging'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'EnableScriptBlockLogging'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\PowerShell\\ScriptBlockLogging'\n                        : name equals 'EnableScriptBlockLogging'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","ccis":["CCI-000135"],"group_title":"SRG-OS-000042-GPOS-00020","severity":"medium","rule_version":"WN11-CC-000326","third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000042-GPOS-00020","id":"V-253414"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253414r958422","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE \nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\PowerShell\\ScriptBlockLogging\\\n\nValue Name: EnableScriptBlockLogging\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253414r958422_rule"},{"stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","discussion":"Maintaining an audit trail of system activity logs can help identify configuration errors, troubleshoot service disruptions, and analyze compromises that have occurred, as well as detect attacks. Audit logs are necessary to provide a trail of evidence in case the system or network is compromised. Collecting this data is essential for analyzing the security of information assets and detecting signs of suspicious and unexpected behavior.\n\nEnabling PowerShell Transcription will record detailed information from the processing of PowerShell commands and scripts. This can provide additional detail when malware has run on a system.","mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"PowerShell Transcription must be enabled on Windows 11.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (PowerShell Transcription is enabled on Windows 11)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25341500 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : PowerShell Transcription is enabled on Windows 11\nCheck Existence         : All collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25341500 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\PowerShell\\Transcription'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'EnableTranscripting'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\PowerShell\\Transcription'\n                        : name equals 'EnableTranscripting'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253415"},"uuid":"3673CAE0-6BF8-1014-874C-9B17CD0D5BCA","status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Windows PowerShell &gt;&gt; \"Turn on PowerShell Transcription\" to \"Enabled\".\n\nSpecify the Transcript output directory to point to a Central Log Server or another secure location to prevent user access.","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253415","group_id":"V-253415","potential_impacts":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253415","title":"SRG-OS-000041-GPOS-00019"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253415r958420","ia_controls":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\PowerShell\\Transcription\\\n\nValue Name: EnableTranscripting\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1","rule_id_src":"SV-253415r958420_rule","ccis":["CCI-000134"],"group_title":"SRG-OS-000041-GPOS-00019","severity":"medium","rule_version":"WN11-CC-000327"},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Allow Basic authentication' is set to 'Disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25341600 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Allow Basic authentication' is set to 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25341600 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\WinRM\\Client'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'AllowBasic'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\WinRM\\Client'\n                        : name equals 'AllowBasic'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","mitigations":"","discussion":"Basic authentication uses plain text passwords that could be used to compromise a system.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The Windows Remote Management (WinRM) client must not use Basic authentication.","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Windows Remote Management (WinRM) &gt;&gt; WinRM Client &gt;&gt; \"Allow Basic authentication\" to \"Disabled\".","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253416","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253416","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253416","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"uuid":"3673D1C7-6BF8-1014-8F65-DFF15F0B1CA0","status":"not_a_finding","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id":"SV-253416r958510","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253416r958510_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\WinRM\\Client\\\n\nValue Name: AllowBasic\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000125-GPOS-00065","id":"V-253416"},"responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN11-CC-000330","ccis":["CCI-000877"],"severity":"high","group_title":"SRG-OS-000125-GPOS-00065"},{"group_title":"SRG-OS-000393-GPOS-00173","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-002890"],"rule_version":"WN11-CC-000335","weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000393-GPOS-00173","id":"V-253417"},"check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\WinRM\\Client\\\n\nValue Name: AllowUnencryptedTraffic\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253417r958848_rule","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253417r958848","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"3673D850-6BF8-1014-A87E-8F08D9683BC3","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253417"},"potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253417","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253417","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Windows Remote Management (WinRM) &gt;&gt; WinRM Client &gt;&gt; \"Allow unencrypted traffic\" to \"Disabled\".","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The Windows Remote Management (WinRM) client must not allow unencrypted traffic.","discussion":"Unencrypted remote access to a system can allow sensitive information to be compromised. Windows remote management connections must be encrypted to prevent this.","mitigations":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Allow unencrypted traffic' is set to 'Disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25341700 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Allow unencrypted traffic' is set to 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25341700 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\WinRM\\Client'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'AllowUnencryptedTraffic'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\WinRM\\Client'\n                        : name equals 'AllowUnencryptedTraffic'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n"},{"stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","discussion":"Basic authentication uses plain text passwords that could be used to compromise a system.","mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The Windows Remote Management (WinRM) service must not use Basic authentication.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Allow Basic authentication' is set to 'Disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25341800 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Allow Basic authentication' is set to 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25341800 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\WinRM\\Service'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'AllowBasic'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\WinRM\\Service'\n                        : name equals 'AllowBasic'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253418","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"uuid":"3673DFA1-6BF8-1014-9535-9CD36FF4E8A0","status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Windows Remote Management (WinRM) &gt;&gt; WinRM Service &gt;&gt; \"Allow Basic authentication\" to \"Disabled\".\n\nSeverity Override Guidance: The AO can allow the severity override if they have reviewed the overall protection. This would only be allowed temporarily for implementation as documented and approved. \n....\nAllowing Basic authentication to be used for the sole creation of Office 365 DoD tenants.\n....\nA documented mechanism and or script that can disable Basic authentication once administration completes. \n....\nUse of a Privileged Access Workstation (PAW) and adherence to the Clean Source principle for administration.","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253418","group_id":"V-253418","potential_impacts":"","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000125-GPOS-00065","id":"V-253418"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253418r958510","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\WinRM\\Service\\\n\nValue Name: AllowBasic\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253418r958510_rule","ccis":["CCI-000877"],"group_title":"SRG-OS-000125-GPOS-00065","severity":"high","rule_version":"WN11-CC-000345"},{"comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id":"SV-253419r958850","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253419r958850_rule","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\WinRM\\Service\\\n\nValue Name: AllowUnencrypte