","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\WinRM\\Client\\\n\nValue Name: AllowDigest\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0","rule_id_src":"SV-253421r958510_rule","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253421r958510"},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nTest                    :     false ('Let Windows apps activate with voice' is set to 'Enabled' with 'Default for all Apps' set to 'Force Deny')\nTest                    :     true ('Let Windows apps activate with voice while the system is locked' is set to 'Enabled' with 'Default for all Apps' set to 'Force Deny')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25342200 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : 'Let Windows apps activate with voice' is set to 'Enabled' with 'Default for all Apps' set to 'Force Deny'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25342200 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\AppPrivacy'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'LetAppsActivateWithVoice'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000002 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '2'\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25342201 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Let Windows apps activate with voice while the system is locked' is set to 'Enabled' with 'Default for all Apps' set to 'Force Deny'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25342201 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\AppPrivacy'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'LetAppsActivateWithVoiceAboveLock'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000002 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\AppPrivacy'\n                        : name equals 'LetAppsActivateWithVoiceAboveLock'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '2'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","rule_title":"Windows 11 must be configured to prevent Windows apps from being activated by voice while the system is locked.","security_override_guidance":"","mitigations":"","discussion":"Allowing Windows apps to be activated by voice from the lock screen could allow for unauthorized use. Requiring logon will ensure the apps are only used by authorized personnel.","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; App Privacy &gt;&gt; \"Let Windows apps activate with voice while the system is locked\" to \"Enabled\" with Default for all Apps: set to Force Deny. \n\nThe requirement is NA if the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; App Privacy &gt;&gt; \"Let Windows apps activate with voice\" is configured to \"Enabled\" with Default for all Apps: set to Force Deny.","group_id":"V-253422","potential_impacts":"","group_id_src":"V-253422","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","uuid":"3673FED4-6BF8-1014-BE2D-FCC69ECE389C","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253422","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id":"SV-253422r958400","mitigation_control":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id_src":"SV-253422r958400_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"The setting is NA when the \"Allow voice activation\" policy is configured to disallow applications to be activated with voice for all users.\nIf the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\AppPrivacy\\\n\nValue Name: LetAppsActivateWithVoiceAboveLock\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000002 (2)\n\nIf the following registry value exists and is configured as specified, requirement is NA: \n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\AppPrivacy\\\n\nValue Name: LetAppsActivateWithVoice\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000002 (2)","group_tree":{"id":"V-253422","title":"SRG-OS-000028-GPOS-00009"},"reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN11-CC-000365","ccis":["CCI-000056"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000028-GPOS-00009"},{"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253423","title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049"},"check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\System\n\nValue Name: AllowDomainPINLogon\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue data: 0","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253423r958478_rule","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253423r958478","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"rule_version":"WN11-CC-000370","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The convenience PIN for Windows 11 must be disabled.","discussion":"This policy controls whether a domain user can sign in using a convenience PIN to prevent enabling (Password Stuffer).","mitigations":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Turn on convenience PIN sign-in' is 'Disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25342300 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Turn on convenience PIN sign-in' is 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : All collected items must exist.\nCheck           