one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\WindowsInkWorkspace'\n                        : name equals 'AllowWindowsInkWorkspace'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","mitigations":"","discussion":"This action secures Windows Ink, which contains applications and features oriented toward pen computing.","rule_title":"Windows Ink Workspace must be configured to disallow access above the lock.","security_override_guidance":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253424","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253424","fix_text":"Disable the convenience PIN sign-in. \n\nTo correct this, configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Windows Ink Workspace &gt;&gt; Set \"Allow Windows Ink Workspace\" to \"Enabled and set Options \"On, but disallow access above lock\".","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253424"},"uuid":"36740B43-6BF8-1014-B5B4-90EAAE5B65CB"},{"rule_id_src":"SV-253425r958478_rule","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_CURRENT_USER\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CloudContent\\\n\nValue Name: DisableThirdPartySuggestions\n\nType: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)","ia_controls":"","rule_id":"SV-253425r958478","mitigation_control":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","id":"V-253425"},"reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","rule_version":"WN11-CC-000390","severity":"low","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Do not suggest third-party content in Windows spotlight' is set to 'Enabled')\nTest                    :     false (For the current user, 'Do not suggest third-party content in Windows spotlight' is set to 'Enabled')\nResult Analysis         :          Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_CURRENT_USER\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CloudContent\\DisableThirdPartySuggestions'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25342500 (ntuser_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Do not suggest third-party content in Windows spotlight' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : All collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25342500 (ntuser_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CloudContent'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisableThirdPartySuggestions'\nExclude Items If        : enabled equals 'false'\nExclude Items If        : days_since_modified is greater than '35'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000022 (ntuser_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CloudContent'\n                        : name equals 'DisableThirdPartySuggestions'\n                        : sid equals 'S-1-5-21-1196677333-4084102320-1286229203-1001'\n                        : username equals 'WKS1-SOTERIA\\Degthat'\n                        : account_type equals 'local'\n                        : logged_on equals 'false'\n                        : days_since_last_logon equals '16'\n                        : enabled equals 'true'\n                        : date_modified equals '134331012980000000'\n                        : days_since_modified equals '1'\n                        : filepath equals 'C:\\Users\\Degthat\\ntuser.dat'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134317136990000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25342501 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : For the current user, 'Do not suggest third-party content in Windows spotlight' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25342501 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_CURRENT_USER'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CloudContent'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisableThirdPartySuggestions'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_CURRENT_USER\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CloudContent\\DisableThirdPartySuggestions'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows 11 must be configured to prevent users from receiving suggestions for third-party or additional applications.","mitigations":"","discussion":"Windows spotlight features may suggest apps and content from third-party software publishers in addition to Microsoft apps and content.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253425","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253425","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for User Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates. &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Cloud Content &gt;&gt; \"Do not suggest third-party content in Windows spotlight\" to \"Enabled\".","status":"open","uuid":"36741277-6BF8-1014-8F1E-E0B60F8EEEEB","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253425"}},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Enumeration policy for external devices incompatible with Kernel DMA Protection' is set to 'Enabled' with 'Enumeration Policy' set to 'Block All')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25342600 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Enumeration policy for external devices incompatible with Kernel DMA Protection' is set to 'Enabled' with 'Enumeration Policy' set to 'Block All'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25342600 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Kernel DMA Protection'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DeviceEnumerationPolicy'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Kernel DMA Protection'\n                        : name equals 'DeviceEnumerationPolicy'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","discussion":"Kernel DMA Protection to protect PCs against drive-by Direct Memory Access (DMA) attacks using PCI hot plug devices connected to Thunderbolt 3 ports. Drive-by DMA attacks can lead to disclosure of sensitive information residing on a PC, or even injection of malware that allows attackers to bypass the lock screen or control PCs remotely.","mitigations":"","rule_title":"Windows 11 Kernel (Direct Memory Access) DMA Protection must be enabled.","security_override_guidance":"","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; System &gt;&gt; Kernel DMA Protection &gt;&gt; \"Enumeration policy for external devices incompatible with Kernel DMA Protection\" to \"Enabled\" with \"Enumeration Policy\" set to \"Block All\".","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253426","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253426","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253426","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"uuid":"367419C6-6BF8-1014-8F2D-CAA8A60992AD","status":"not_a_finding","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253426r991580","ia_controls":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\Kernel DMA Protection\n\nValue Name: DeviceEnumerationPolicy\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0","rule_id_src":"SV-253426r991580_rule","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253426","title":"SRG-OS-000471-GPOS-00216"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","rule_version":"WN11-EP-000310","ccis":["CCI-000172"],"group_title":"SRG-OS-000471-GPOS-00216","severity":"medium"},{"check_content":"Verify the DoD Root CA certificates are installed as Trusted Root Certification Authorities.\n\nThe certificates and thumbprints referenced below apply to unclassified systems; refer to PKE documentation for other networks.\n\nRun \"PowerShell\" as an administrator.\n\nExecute the following command:\n\nGet-ChildItem -Path Cert:Localmachine\\root | Where Subject -Like \"*DoD*\" | FL Subject, Thumbprint, NotAfter\n\nIf the following certificate \"Subject\" and \"Thumbprint\" information is not displayed, this is a finding. \n\nSubject: CN=DoD Root CA 3, OU=PKI, OU=DoD, O=U.S. Government, C=US\nThumbprint: D73CA91102A2204A36459ED32213B467D7CE97FB\nNotAfter: 12/30/2029\n\nSubject: CN=DoD Root CA 4, OU=PKI, OU=DoD, O=U.S. Government, C=US\nThumbprint: B8269F25DBD937ECAFD4C35A9838571723F2D026\nNotAfter: 7/25/2032\n\nSubject: CN=DoD Root CA 5, OU=PKI, OU=DoD, O=U.S. Government, C=US\nThumbprint: 4ECB5CC3095670454DA1CBD410FC921F46B8564B\nNotAfter: 6/14/2041\n\nSubject: CN=DoD Root CA 6 OU=PKI, OU=DoD, O=U.S. Government, C=US\nThumbprint: D37ECF61C0B4ED88681EF3630C4E2FC787B37AEF\nNotAfter: 1/24/2053\n\nAlternately, use the Certificates MMC snap-in:\n\nRun \"MMC\".\n\nSelect \"File\", \"Add/Remove Snap-in\".\n\nSelect \"Certificates\", click \"Add\".\n\nSelect \"Computer account\", click \"Next\".\n\nSelect \"Local computer: (the computer this console is running on)\", click \"Finish\".\n\nClick \"OK\".\n\nExpand \"Certificates\" and navigate to Trusted Root Certification Authorities &gt;&gt; Certificates.\n\nFor each of the DoD Root CA certificates noted below:\n\nRight-click on the certificate and select \"Open\".\n\nSelect the \"Details\" tab.\n\nScroll to the bottom and select \"Thumbprint\".\n\nIf the DoD Root CA certificates below are not listed or the value for the \"Thumbprint\" field is not as noted, this is a finding.\n\nDoD Root CA 3\nThumbprint: D73CA91102A2204A36459ED32213B467D7CE97FB\nValid to: Sunday, December 30, 2029\n\nDoD Root CA 4\nThumbprint: B8269F25DBD937ECAFD4C35A9838571723F2D026\nValid to: Sunday, July 25, 2032\n\nDoD Root CA 5\nThumbprint: 4ECB5CC3095670454DA1CBD410FC921F46B8564B\nValid to: Friday, June 14, 2041\n\nDoD Root CA 6\nThumbprint : D37ECF61C0B4ED88681EF3630C4E2FC787B37AEF\nValid to: Friday, January 24, 2053\n","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253427r958448_rule","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253427r958448","weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253427","title":"SRG-OS-000066-GPOS-00034"},"rule_version":"WN11-PK-000005","group_title":"SRG-OS-000066-GPOS-00034","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-000185"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     false (The DoD Root CA 3 Certificate expiring 12/30/2029 is installed into the Trusted Root Store.)\nResult Analysis         :          Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nTest                    :     false (The DoD Root CA 4 Certificate expiring 7/25/2032 is installed into the Trusted Root Store.)\nResult Analysis         :          Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nTest                    :     false (The DoD Root CA 5 Certificate expiring 6/14/2041 is installed into the Trusted Root Store.)\nResult Analysis         :          Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nTest                    :     false (The DoD Root CA 6 Certificate expiring 1/24/2053 is installed into the Trusted Root Store.)\nResult Analysis         :          Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25342700 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : The DoD Root CA 3 Certificate expiring 12/30/2029 is installed into the Trusted Root Store.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25342700 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nResult Analysis         : Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25342701 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : The DoD Root CA 4 Certificate expiring 7/25/2032 is installed into the Trusted Root Store.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25342705 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nResult Analysis         : Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25342702 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : The DoD Root CA 5 Certificate expiring 6/14/2041 is installed into the Trusted Root Store.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25342710 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nResult Analysis         : Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25342703 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : The DoD Root CA 6 Certificate expiring 1/24/2053 is installed into the Trusted Root Store.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25342715 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nResult Analysis         : Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n","discussion":"To ensure secure DoD websites and DoD-signed code are properly validated, the system must trust the DoD Root Certificate Authorities (CAs). The DoD root certificates will ensure that the trust chain is established for server certificates issued from the DoD CAs.","mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The DoD Root CA certificates must be installed in the Trusted Root Store.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253427","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253427","fix_text":"Install the DoD Root CA certificates.\nDoD Root CA 3\nDoD Root CA 4\nDoD Root CA 5                                               \nDoD Root CA 6\n\nThe InstallRoot tool is available on Cyber Exchange at https://cyber.mil/pki-pke/tools-configuration-files. PKI can be found at https://crl.gds.disa.mil/.","status":"open","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253427"},"uuid":"36741F13-6BF8-1014-9B87-EA2EC66E8A77"},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     false (ECA Root CA 4 certificate expiring 12/30/2029 is installed in the Trusted Root Store)\nResult Analysis         :          Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25342800 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : ECA Root CA 4 certificate expiring 12/30/2029 is installed in the Trusted Root Store\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25342800 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nResult Analysis         : Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","mitigations":"","discussion":"To ensure secure websites protected with External Certificate Authority (ECA) server certificates are properly validated, the system must trust the ECA Root CAs. The ECA root certificates will ensure the trust chain is established for server certificates issued from the External CAs. This requirement only applies to unclassified systems.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The External Root CA certificates must be installed in the Trusted Root Store on unclassified systems.","fix_text":"Install the ECA Root CA certificates on unclassified systems.\n\nECA Root CA 4\n\nThe InstallRoot tool is available on Cyber Exchange at https://cyber.mil/pki-pke/tools-configuration-files. PKI can be found at https://crl.gds.disa.mil/.","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253428","group_id":"V-253428","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253428"},"uuid":"367424C0-6BF8-1014-BC95-B1D2BA03CDD3","status":"open","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id":"SV-253428r958448","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253428r958448_rule","check_content":"Verify the ECA Root CA certificates are installed on unclassified systems as Trusted Root Certification Authorities.\n\nRun \"PowerShell\" as an administrator.\n\nExecute the following command:\n\nGet-ChildItem -Path Cert:Localmachine\\root | Where Subject -Like \"*ECA*\" | FL Subject, Thumbprint, NotAfter\n\nIf the following certificate \"Subject\" and \"Thumbprint\" information is not displayed, this is a finding. \n\nSubject: CN=ECA Root CA 4, OU=ECA, O=U.S. Government, C=US\nThumbprint: 73E8BB08E337D6A5A6AEF90CFFDD97D9176CB582\nNotAfter: 12/30/2029\n\nAlternately use the Certificates MMC snap-in:\n\nRun \"MMC\".\n\nSelect \"File\", \"Add/Remove Snap-in\".\n\nSelect \"Certificates\", click \"Add\".\n\nSelect \"Computer account\", click \"Next\".\n\nSelect \"Local computer: (the computer this console is running on)\", click \"Finish\".\n\nClick \"OK\".\n\nExpand \"Certificates\" and navigate to Trusted Root Certification Authorities &gt;&gt; Certificates.\n\nFor each of the ECA Root CA certificates noted below:\n\nRight-click on the certificate and select \"Open\".\n\nSelect the \"Details\" tab.\n\nScroll to the bottom and select \"Thumbprint\".\n\nIf the ECA Root CA certificates below are not listed or the value for the \"Thumbprint\" field is not as noted, this is a finding.\n\nECA Root CA 4\nThumbprint: 73E8BB08E337D6A5A6AEF90CFFDD97D9176CB582\nValid to: Sunday, December 30, 2029","ia_controls":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253428","title":"SRG-OS-000066-GPOS-00034"},"reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN11-PK-000010","ccis":["CCI-000185"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000066-GPOS-00034"},{"stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","discussion":"To ensure users do not experience denial of service when performing certificate-based authentication to DoD websites due to the system chaining to a root other than DoD Root CAs, the DoD Interoperability Root CA cross-certificates must be installed in the Untrusted Certificate Store. This requirement only applies to unclassified systems.","mitigations":"","rule_title":"The DoD Interoperability Root CA cross-certificates must be installed in the Untrusted Certificates Store on unclassified systems.","security_override_guidance":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     false (DoD Interoperability Root CA 2 certificate expiring 11/16/2024 is installed in the Untrusted Certificates Store)\nResult Analysis         :          Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25342900 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : DoD Interoperability Root CA 2 certificate expiring 11/16/2024 is installed in the Untrusted Certificates Store\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25342900 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nResult Analysis         : Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253429","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"uuid":"367429C8-6BF8-1014-840B-A820FBEEC228","status":"open","fix_text":"Install the DoD Interoperability Root CA cross-certificates on unclassified systems.  \n                                           \nIssued To - Issued By - Thumbprint\nDoD Root CA 3 - DoD Interoperability Root CA 2 - 49CBE933151872E17C8EAE7F0ABA97FB610F6477\n\nThe certificates can be installed using the InstallRoot tool. The tool and user guide are available on Cyber Exchange at https://cyber.mil/pki-pke/tools-configuration-files. Certificate bundles published by the PKI can be found at https://crl.gds.disa.mil/.","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253429","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253429","responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000066-GPOS-00034","id":"V-253429"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253429r958448","check_content":"Verify the DoD Interoperability cross-certificates are installed on unclassified systems as Untrusted Certificates.\n\nRun \"PowerShell\" as an administrator.\n\nExecute the following command:\n\nGet-ChildItem -Path Cert:Localmachine\\disallowed | Where {$_.Issuer -Like \"*DoD Interoperability*\" -and $_.Subject -Like \"*DoD*\"} | FL Subject, Issuer, Thumbprint, NotAfter\n\nIf the following certificate \"Subject\", \"Issuer\", and \"Thumbprint\" information is not displayed, this is a finding.\n\nSubject: CN=DoD Root CA 3, OU=PKI, OU=DoD, O=U.S. Government, C=US\nIssuer: CN=DoD Interoperability Root CA 2, OU=PKI, OU=DoD, O=U.S. Government, C=US\nThumbprint: 49CBE933151872E17C8EAE7F0ABA97FB610F6477\nNotAfter: 11/16/2024 \n           \nSubject: CN=DoD Root CA 3, OU=PKI, OU=DoD, O=U.S. Government, C=US\nIssuer: CN=DoD Interoperability Root CA 2, OU=PKI, OU=DoD, O=U.S. Government, C=US\nThumbprint: AC06108CA348CC03B53795C64BF84403C1DBD341\nNotAfter: 1/22/2022 \n\nAlternately, use the Certificates MMC snap-in:\n\nRun \"MMC\".\n\nSelect \"File\", \"Add/Remove Snap-in\".\n\nSelect \"Certificates\", click \"Add\".\n\nSelect \"Computer account\", click \"Next\".\n\nSelect \"Local computer: (the computer this console is running on)\", click \"Finish\".\n\nClick \"OK\".\n\nExpand \"Certificates\" and navigate to Untrusted Certificates &gt;&gt; Certificates.\n\nFor each certificate with \"DoD Root CA....\" under \"Issued To\" and \"DoD Interoperability Root CA....\" under \"Issued By\":\n\nRight-click on the certificate and select \"Open\".\n\nSelect the \"Details\" tab.\n\nScroll to the bottom and select \"Thumbprint\".\n\nIf the certificates below are not listed or the value for the \"Thumbprint\" field is not as noted, this is a finding.\n\nIssued To: DoD Root CA 3\nIssued By: Interoperability Root CA 2\nThumbprint : 49CBE933151872E17C8EAE7F0ABA97FB610F6477\nValid to: Saturday, November 16, 2024","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253429r958448_rule","ccis":["CCI-002470"],"group_title":"SRG-OS-000066-GPOS-00034","severity":"medium","rule_version":"WN11-PK-000015"},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     false (US DoD CCEB Interoperability Root CA 2 cross-certificate expiring 7/18/2025 is installed in the Untrusted Certificates Store)\nResult Analysis         :          Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nTest                    :     false (US DoD CCEB Interoperability Root CA 2 cross-certificate expiring 7/18/2026 is installed in the Untrusted Certificates Store)\nResult Analysis         :          Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25343000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : US DoD CCEB Interoperability Root CA 2 cross-certificate expiring 7/18/2025 is installed in the Untrusted Certificates Store\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25343000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nResult Analysis         : Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25343001 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : US DoD CCEB Interoperability Root CA 2 cross-certificate expiring 7/18/2026 is installed in the Untrusted Certificates Store\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25343005 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nResult Analysis         : Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n","discussion":"To ensure users do not experience denial of service when performing certificate-based authentication to DOD websites due to the system chaining to a root other than DOD Root CAs, the US DOD CCEB Interoperability Root CA cross-certificates must be installed in the Untrusted Certificate Store. This requirement only applies to unclassified systems.","mitigations":"","rule_title":"The US DOD CCEB Interoperability Root CA cross-certificates must be installed in the Untrusted Certificates Store on unclassified systems.","security_override_guidance":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253430","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253430","fix_text":"Install the US DOD CCEB Interoperability Root CA cross-certificate on unclassified systems.\n\nIssued To - Issued By - Thumbprint\n9B74964506C7ED9138070D08D5F8B969866560C8\nNotAfter: 7/18/2025 9:56:22 AM                                         \nIssued To: DOD Root CA 6\nIssued By: US DOD CCEB Interoperability Root CA 2\nThumbprint: D471CA32F7A692CE6CBB6196BD3377FE4DBCD106\nNotAfter: 7/18/2026 \n\nThe certificates can be installed using the InstallRoot tool. The tool and user guide are available on Cyber Exchange at https://cyber.mil/pki-pke/tools-configuration-files. Certificate bundles published by the PKI can be found at https://crl.gds.disa.mil/.","status":"open","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253430"},"uuid":"36742E92-6BF8-1014-B6F8-B8AD07E59A20","check_content":"Verify the US DOD CCEB Interoperability Root CA cross-certificate is installed on unclassified systems as an Untrusted Certificate.\n\nRun \"PowerShell\" as an administrator.\n\nExecute the following command:\n\nGet-ChildItem -Path Cert:Localmachine\\disallowed | Where Issuer -Like \"*CCEB Interoperability*\" | FL Subject, Issuer, Thumbprint, NotAfter\n\nIf the following certificate \"Subject\", \"Issuer\", and \"Thumbprint\" information is not displayed, this is a finding. \n\nSubject: CN=DOD Root CA 3, OU=PKI, OU=DOD, O=U.S. Government, C=US\nIssuer: CN=US DOD CCEB Interoperability Root CA 2, OU=PKI, OU=DOD, O=U.S. Government, C=US\nThumbprint: 9B74964506C7ED9138070D08D5F8B969866560C8\nNotAfter: 7/18/2025 9:56:22 A\n\nAlternately, use the Certificates MMC snap-in:\n\nRun \"MMC\".\n\nSelect \"File\", then click \"Add/Remove Snap-in\".\n\nSelect \"Certificates\", then click \"Add\".\n\nSelect \"Computer account\", then click \"Next\".\n\nSelect \"Local computer: (the computer this console is running on)\", then click \"Finish\".\n\nClick \"OK\".\n\nExpand \"Certificates\" and navigate to Untrusted Certificates &gt;&gt; Certificates.\n\nFor each certificate with \"US DOD CCEB Interoperability Root CA...\" under \"Issued By\":\n\nRight-click on the certificate and select \"Open\".\n\nSelect the \"Details\" tab.\n\nScroll to the bottom and select \"Thumbprint\".\n\nIf the certificate below is not listed or the value for the \"Thumbprint\" field is not as noted, this is a finding.\n\nSubject: CN=DOD Root CA 3, OU=PKI, OU=DOD, O=U.S. Government, C=US\nIssuer: CN=US DOD CCEB Interoperability Root CA 2, OU=PKI, OU=DOD, O=U.S. Government, C=US\nThumbprint: Thumbprint: 9B74964506C7ED9138070D08D5F8B969866560C8\nNotAfter: 7/18/2025 9:56:22 AM                                       \nSubject: CN=DOD Root CA 6, OU=PKI, OU=DOD, O=U.S. Government, C=US\nIssuer: CN=US DOD CCEB Interoperability Root CA 2, OU=PKI, OU=DOD, O=U.S. Government, C=US\nThumbprint: D471CA32F7A692CE6CBB6196BD3377FE4DBCD106\nNotAfter: 7/18/2026 9:56:22 AM","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253430r1081058_rule","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253430r1081058","weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000403-GPOS-00182","id":"V-253430"},"rule_version":"WN11-PK-000020","group_title":"SRG-OS-000403-GPOS-00182","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-002470"]},{"ccis":["CCI-002235"],"group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","severity":"medium","rule_version":"WN11-RG-000005","responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","id":"V-253431"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253431r958726","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","ia_controls":"","check_content":"Verify the default registry permissions for the keys note below of the HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE hive.\n\nIf any non-privileged groups such as Everyone, Users or Authenticated Users have greater than Read permission, this is a finding.\n\nRun \"Regedit\".\nRight click on the registry areas noted below.\nSelect \"Permissions...\" and the \"Advanced\" button.\n\nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SECURITY\nType - \"Allow\" for all\nInherited from - \"None\" for all\nPrincipal - Access - Applies to\nSYSTEM - Full Control - This key and subkeys\nAdministrators - Special - This key and subkeys\n\nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\nType - \"Allow\" for all\nInherited from - \"None\" for all\nPrincipal - Access - Applies to\nUsers - Read - This key and subkeys\nAdministrators - Full Control - This key and subkeys\nSYSTEM - Full Control - This key and subkeys\nCREATOR OWNER - Full Control - This key and subkeys\nALL APPLICATION PACKAGES - Read - This key and subkeys\n\nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\nType - \"Allow\" for all\nInherited from - \"None\" for all\nPrincipal - Access - Applies to\nUsers - Read - This key and subkeys\nAdministrators - Full Control - This key and subkeys\nSYSTEM - Full Control - This key and subkeys\nCREATOR OWNER - Full Control - This key and subkeys\nALL APPLICATION PACKAGES - Read - This key and subkeys\n\nOther subkeys under the noted keys may also be sampled. There may be some instances where non-privileged groups have greater than read permission.\n\nMicrosoft has given Read permission to the SOFTWARE and SYSTEM registry keys in later versions of Windows 11 to the following SID, this is currently not a finding.\n\nS-1-15-3-1024-1065365936-1281604716-3511738428-1654721687-432734479-3232135806-4053264122-3456934681\n\nIf the defaults have not been changed, these are not a finding.","rule_id_src":"SV-253431r958726_rule","uuid":"367436EE-6BF8-1014-A6B7-AF4B3EE27277","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:253431"},"status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Maintain the default permissions for the HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE registry hive.\n\nThe default permissions of the higher level keys are noted below.\n\nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SECURITY\nType - \"Allow\" for all\nInherited from - \"None\" for all\nPrincipal - Access - Applies to\nSYSTEM - Full Control - This key and subkeys\nAdministrators - Special - This key and subkeys\n\nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\nType - \"Allow\" for all\nInherited from - \"None\" for all\nPrincipal - Access - Applies to\nUsers - Read - This key and subkeys\nAdministrators - Full Control - This key and subkeys\nSYSTEM - Full Control - This key and subkeys\nCREATOR OWNER - Full Control - This key and subkeys\nALL APPLICATION PACKAGES - Read - This key and subkeys\n\nHKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\nType - \"Allow\" for all\nInherited from - \"None\" for all\nPrincipal - Access - Applies to\nUsers - Read - This key and subkeys\nAdministrators - Full Control - This key and subkeys\nSYSTEM - Full Control - This key and subkeys\nCREATOR OWNER - Full Control - This key and subkeys\nALL APPLICATION PACKAGES - Read - This key and subkeys\n\nMicrosoft has also given read permission to the SOFTWARE and SYSTEM registry keys in later versions of Windows 11 to the following SID.\n\nS-1-15-3-1024-1065365936-1281604716-3511738428-1654721687-432734479-3232135806-4053264122-3456934681","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253431","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253431","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Default permissions for the HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE registry hive must be maintained.","discussion":"The registry is integral to the function, security, and stability of the Windows system. Changing the system's registry permissions allows the possibility of unauthorized and anonymous modification to the operating system.","mitigations":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Default permissions for the HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SECURITY registry key must be maintained.)\nTest                    :   true (Default permissions for the HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE registry key must be maintained.)\nTest                    :   true (Default permissions for the HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM registry key must be maintained.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25343101 (shellcommand_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Default permissions for the HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SECURITY registry key must be maintained.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25343101 (shellcommand_object)\nObject Comment          : Gather permissions for the HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SECURITY registry\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'shell' must be equal to 'powershell'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'command' must be equal to '([Microsoft.Win32.Registry]::LocalMachine.OpenSubKey(\"Security\", [System.Security.AccessControl.RegistryRights]::ReadPermissions)).GetAccessControl().Access |  Where-Object { $_.RegistryRights -notmatch '\\d+' } | ForEach-Object { \"Identity:$($_.IdentityReference), Rights: $($_.RegistryRights), Access: $($_.AccessControlType), IsInherited: $($_.IsInherited), InheritanceFlags: $($_.InheritanceFlags), PropagationFlags: $($_.PropagationFlags)\" }'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25343101 (shellcommand_state)\nState Comment           : System Full, Administrators ReadPermission and ChangePermissions \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'stdout_line' must match the pattern '^Identity:NT AUTHORITY\\\\SYSTEM, Rights: FullControl, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: ContainerInherit, PropagationFlags: None$|^Identity:BUILTIN\\\\Administrators, Rights: ReadPermissions, ChangePermissions, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: ContainerInherit, PropagationFlags: None$'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : shell equals 'powershell'\n                        : command equals '([Microsoft.Win32.Registry]::LocalMachine.OpenSubKey(\"Security\", [System.Security.AccessControl.RegistryRights]::ReadPermissions)).GetAccessControl().Access |  Where-Object { $_.RegistryRights -notmatch '\\d+' } | ForEach-Object { \"Identity:$($_.IdentityReference), Rights: $($_.RegistryRights), Access: $($_.AccessControlType), IsInherited: $($_.IsInherited), InheritanceFlags: $($_.InheritanceFlags), PropagationFlags: $($_.PropagationFlags)\" }'\n                        : pattern equals ''\n                        : exit_status equals ''\n                        : stdout_line equals 'Identity:NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM, Rights: FullControl, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: ContainerInherit, PropagationFlags: None'\n                        : stdout_line equals 'Identity:BUILTIN\\Administrators, Rights: ReadPermissions, ChangePermissions, Access: Allow, IsInherited: False, InheritanceFlags: ContainerInherit, PropagationFlags: None'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25343102 (shellcommand_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Default permissions for the HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE registry key must be maintained.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25343102 (shellcommand_object)\nObject Comment          : Gather permissions for the HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE registry\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'shell' must be equal to 'powershell'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'command' must be equal to '([Microsoft.Win32.Registry]::LocalMachine.OpenSubKey(\"Software\", [System.Security.AccessControl.RegistryRights]::ReadPermissions)).GetAccessControl().Access | Where-Object { $_.RegistryRights -notmatch '\