s &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options.\n\nIf the value for \"Accounts: Guest account status\" is not set to \"Disabled\", this is a finding.","ia_controls":"","rule_id":"SV-253433r958504","mitigation_control":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"36743C9A-6BF8-1014-909B-9BD9091E4695","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253433","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253433","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253433","false_positives":"","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; \"Accounts: Guest account status\" to \"Disabled\".","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The built-in guest account must be disabled.","mitigations":"","discussion":"A system faces an increased vulnerability threat if the built-in guest account is not disabled. This account is a known account that exists on all Windows systems and cannot be deleted. This account is initialized during the installation of the operating system with no password assigned.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (The built-in guest account is disabled.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25343300 (user_sid55_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The built-in guest account is disabled.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25343300 (user_sid55_object)\nObject Comment          : Built-in Guest account\nObject Requirement      : for user_sid, the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     user_sid must be equal to 'S-1-5-21-1196677333-4084102320-1286229203-501'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000017 (user_sid55_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'enabled' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : user_sid equals 'S-1-5-21-1196677333-4084102320-1286229203-501'\n                        : enabled equals 'false'\n                        : group_sid equals 'S-1-5-32-546'\n                        : last_logon equals '0'\n                        : user equals 'Visitor'\n                        : group equals 'Guests'\n                        : full_name equals ''\n                        : comment equals 'Built-in account for guest access to the computer/domain'\n                        : password_age_days equals '0'\n"},{"discussion":"An account without a password can allow unauthorized access to a system as only the username would be required. Password policies must prevent accounts with blank passwords from existing on a system. However, if a local account with a blank password did exist, enabling this setting will prevent network access, limiting the account to local console logon only.","mitigations":"","rule_title":"Local accounts with blank passwords must be restricted to prevent access from the network.","security_override_guidance":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Accounts: Limit local account use of blank passwords to console logon only' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25343400 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Accounts: Limit local account use of blank passwords to console logon only' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25343400 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'LimitBlankPasswordUse'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa'\n                        : name equals 'LimitBlankPasswordUse'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995350000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253434","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"uuid":"3674423F-6BF8-1014-AF7A-EE161924BF99","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253434","group_id":"V-253434","potential_impacts":"","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; \"Accounts: Limit local account use of blank passwords to console logon only\" to \"Enabled\".","weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-253434"},"check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa\\\n\nValue Name: LimitBlankPasswordUse\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253434r991589_rule","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253434r991589","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"rule_version":"WN11-SO-000015"},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Accounts: Rename administrator account' is not set to 'Administrator' or 'localdomain\\Administrator')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25343500 (sid_sid_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Accounts: Rename administrator account' is not set to 'Administrator' or 'localdomain\\Administrator'\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\nState Operator          : All item-state comparisons must be true.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25343500 (sid_sid_object)\nObject Comment          : Built-in Administrator SID\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'trustee_sid' must match the pattern '^S-1-5-[0-9-]+-500$'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25343500 (sid_sid_state)\nState Comment           : Not Administrator\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'trustee_name' must not be equal (case insensitive) to 'Administrator'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25343501 (sid_sid_state)\nState Comment           : Not localdomain\\Administrator\nState Requirement       : for alltrustee_name, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     trustee_name must not be equal (case insensitive) to 'WKS1-SOTERIA\\Administrator'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-21-1196677333-4084102320-1286229203-500'\n                        : trustee_name equals 'X_Admin'\n                        : trustee_domain equals 'WKS1-SOTERIA'\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","rule_title":"The built-in administrator account must be renamed.","security_override_guidance":"","mitigations":"","discussion":"The built-in administrator account is a well-known account subject to attack. Renaming this account to an unidentified name improves the protection of this account and the system.","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; \"Accounts: Rename administrator account\" to a name other than \"Administrator\".","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253435","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253435","uuid":"3674493E-6BF8-1014-A567-CE4A1B70D62A","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253435"},"status":"not_a_finding","rule_id":"SV-253435r991589","mitigation_control":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id_src":"SV-253435r991589_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options.\n\nIf the value for \"Accounts: Rename administrator account\" is set to \"Administrator\", this is a finding.","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-253435"},"third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN11-SO-000020","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},{"classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253436r991589","ia_controls":"","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options.\n\nIf the value for \"Accounts: Rename guest account\" is set to \"Guest\", this is a finding.","rule_id_src":"SV-253436r991589_rule","third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-253436"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","rule_version":"WN11-SO-000025","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","severity":"medium","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Accounts: Rename Guest account' is not set to 'Guest' or 'localdomain\\Guest')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25343600 (sid_sid_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Accounts: Rename Guest account' is not set to 'Guest' or 'localdomain\\Guest'\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\nState Operator          : All item-state comparisons must be true.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25343600 (sid_sid_object)\nObject Comment          : Built-in Guest SID\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'trustee_sid' must match the pattern '^S-1-5-[0-9-]+-501$'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25343600 (sid_sid_state)\nState Comment           : Not Guest\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'trustee_name' must not be equal (case insensitive) to 'Guest'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25343601 (sid_sid_state)\nState Comment           : Not localdomain\\Guest\nState Requirement       : for alltrustee_name, the following must be true:\nState Requirement       :     trustee_name must not be equal (case insensitive) to 'WKS1-SOTERIA\\Guest'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : trustee_sid equals 'S-1-5-21-1196677333-4084102320-1286229203-501'\n                        : trustee_name equals 'Visitor'\n                        : trustee_domain equals 'WKS1-SOTERIA'\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","discussion":"The built-in guest account is a well-known user account on all Windows systems and, as initially installed, does not require a password. This can allow access to system resources by unauthorized users. Renaming this account to an unidentified name improves the protection of this account and the system.","mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The built-in guest account must be renamed.","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; \"Accounts: Rename guest account\" to a name other than \"Guest\".","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253436","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253436","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253436"},"uuid":"36745080-6BF8-1014-9370-F35E7EFE17A9","status":"not_a_finding"},{"discussion":"Maintaining an audit trail of system activity logs can help identify configuration errors, troubleshoot service disruptions, and analyze compromises that have occurred, as well as detect attacks. Audit logs are necessary to provide a trail of evidence in case the system or network is compromised. Collecting this data is essential for analyzing the security of information assets and detecting signs of suspicious and unexpected behavior. This setting allows administrators to enable more precise auditing capabilities.","mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Audit policy using subcategories must be enabled.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Audit policy using subcategories is enabled.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25343700 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Audit policy using subcategories is enabled.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25343700 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \n