91589_rule","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Netlogon\\Parameters\\\n\nValue Name: DisablePasswordChange\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0","ia_controls":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id":"SV-253441r991589","mitigation_control":"","severity":"low","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"rule_version":"WN11-SO-000050","mitigations":"","discussion":"Computer account passwords are changed automatically on a regular basis. Disabling automatic password changes can make the system more vulnerable to malicious access. Frequent password changes can be a significant safeguard for the system. A new password for the computer account will be generated every 30 days.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The computer account password must not be prevented from being reset.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Domain member: Disable machine account password changes' is set to 'Disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25344100 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Domain member: Disable machine account password changes' is set to 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25344100 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Netlogon\\Parameters'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisablePasswordChange'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Netlogon\\Parameters'\n                        : name equals 'DisablePasswordChange'\n                        : last_write_time equals '133564299920000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253441","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"uuid":"3674978D-6BF8-1014-B36D-9E433BBF0E87","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253441","false_positives":"","group_id":"V-253441","potential_impacts":"","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; \"Domain member: Disable machine account password changes\" to \"Disabled\"."},{"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253442"},"uuid":"36749EFF-6BF8-1014-A618-CEA6C0FA00B1","status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"This is the default configuration for this setting (30 days).\n\nConfigure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; \"Domain member: Maximum machine account password age\" to \"30\" or less (excluding 0 which is unacceptable).","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253442","false_positives":"","group_id":"V-253442","potential_impacts":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","mitigations":"","discussion":"Computer account passwords are changed automatically on a regular basis. This setting controls the maximum password age that a machine account may have. This setting must be set to no more than 30 days, ensuring the machine changes its password monthly.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The maximum age for machine account passwords must be configured to 30 days or less.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Domain member: Maximum machine account password age' is set to 30 or less (but not 0).)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25344200 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Domain member: Maximum machine account password age' is set to 30 or less (but not 0).\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\nState Operator          : All item-state comparisons must be true.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25344200 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Netlogon\\Parameters'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'MaximumPasswordAge'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25344200 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be greater than '0'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25344201 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be less than or equal to '30'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Netlogon\\Parameters'\n                        : name equals 'MaximumPasswordAge'\n                        : last_write_time equals '133564299920000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '30'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"severity":"low","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","rule_version":"WN11-SO-000055","group_tree":{"id":"V-253442","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id":"SV-253442r991589","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253442r991589_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"(remove)This is the default configuration for this setting (30 days).\n\nIf the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Netlogon\\Parameters\\\n\nValue Name: MaximumPasswordAge\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x0000001e (30) (or less, excluding 0)"},{"fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; \"Domain member: Require strong (Windows 2000 or Later) session key\" to \"Enabled\".","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253443","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253443","uuid":"3674A68D-6BF8-1014-BED1-8A15B904D475","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253443"},"status":"not_a_finding","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Domain member: Require strong (Windows 2000 or Later) session key' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25344300 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Domain member: Require strong (Windows 2000 or Later) session key' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25344300 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Netlogon\\Parameters'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'RequireStrongKey'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Netlogon\\Parameters'\n                        : name equals 'RequireStrongKey'\n                        : last_write_time equals '133564299920000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The system must be configured to require a strong session key.","discussion":"A computer connecting to a domain controller will establish a secure channel. Requiring strong session keys enforces 128-bit encryption between systems.","mitigations":"","rule_version":"WN11-SO-000060","ccis":["CCI-002418"],"group_title":"SRG-OS-000423-GPOS-00187","severity":"medium","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253443r958908","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"ia_controls":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\Netlogon\\Parameters\\\n\nValue Name: RequireStrongKey\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1\n \nWarning: This setting may prevent a system from being joined to a domain if not configured consistently between systems.","rule_id_src":"SV-253443r958908_rule","third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253443","title":"SRG-OS-000423-GPOS-00187"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false"},{"status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253444","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"uuid":"3674ADE4-6BF8-1014-BFEA-D0C504BE9892","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253444","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253444","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; \"Interactive logon: Machine inactivity limit\" to \"900\" seconds\" or less, excluding \"0\" which is effectively disabled.","mitigations":"","discussion":"Unattended systems are susceptible to unauthorized use and must be locked when unattended. The screen saver must be set at a maximum of 15 minutes and be password protected. This protects critical and sensitive data from exposure to unauthorized personnel with physical access to the computer.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000279-GPOS-00109, SRG-OS-000163-GPOS-00072","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The machine inactivity limit must be set to 15 minutes, locking the system with the screensaver.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (The machine inactivity limit is set to 15 minutes or less)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.windows:tst:25344400 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The machine inactivity limit is set to 15 minutes or less\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\nState Operator          : All item-state comparisons must be true.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.windows:obj:25344400 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'InactivityTimeoutSecs'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.windows:ste:25344400 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be less than or equal to '900'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.windows:ste:25344401 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be greater than '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\n                        : name equals 'InactivityTimeoutSecs'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '900'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000279-GPOS-00109","ccis":["CCI-001133","CCI-002361"],"rule_version":"WN11-SO-000070","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"id":"V-253444","title":"SRG-OS-000279-GPOS-00109"},"responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253444r958636_rule","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System\\\n\nValue Name: InactivityTimeoutSecs\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000384 (900) (or less, excluding \"0\" which is effectively disabled)","ia_controls":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id":"SV-253444r958636","mitigation_control":""},{"ccis":["CCI-000044","CCI-000048","CCI-000050"],"group_title":"SRG-OS-000024-GPOS-00007","severity":"medium","rule_version":"WN11-SO-000075","third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253445","title":"SRG-OS-000024-GPOS-00007"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253445r958392","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"ia_controls":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System\\\n\nValue Name: LegalNoticeText\n\nValue Type: REG_SZ\nValue: \nYou are accessing a U.S. Government (USG) Information System (IS) that is provided for USG-authorized use only.\n\nBy using this IS (which includes any device attached to this IS), you consent to the following conditions:\n\n-The USG routinely intercepts and monitors communications on this IS for purposes including, but not limited to, penetration testing, COMSEC monitoring, network operations and defense, personnel misconduct (PM), law enforcement (LE), and counterintelligence (CI) investigations.\n\n-At any time, the USG may inspect and seize data stored on this IS.\n\n-Communications using, or data stored on, this IS are not private, are subject to routine monitoring, interception, and search, and may be disclosed or used for any USG-authorized purpose.\n\n-This IS includes security measures (e.g., authentication and access controls) to protect USG interests--not for your personal benefit or privacy.\n\n-Notwithstanding the above, using this IS does not constitute consent to PM, LE or CI investigative searching or monitoring of the content of privileged communications, or work product, related to personal representation or services by attorneys, psychotherapists, or clergy, and their assistants. Such communications and work product are private and confidential. See User Agreement for details.","rule_id_src":"SV-253445r958392_rule","uuid":"3674B56A-6BF8-1014-827E-AF360C807EA1","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:253445","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; \"Interactive logon: Message text for users attempting to log on\" to the following.\n\nYou are accessing a U.S. Government (USG) Information System (IS) that is provided for USG-authorized use only.\n\nBy using this IS (which includes any device attached to this IS), you consent to the following conditions:\n\n-The USG routinely intercepts and monitors communications on this IS for purposes including, but not limited to, penetration testing, COMSEC monitoring, network operations and defense, personnel misconduct (PM), law enforcement (LE), and counterintelligence (CI) investigations.\n\n-At any time, the USG may inspect and seize data stored on this IS.\n\n-Communications using, or data stored on, this IS are not private, are subject to routine monitoring, interception, and search, and may be disclosed or used for any USG-authorized purpose.\n\n-This IS includes security measures (e.g., authentication and access controls) to protect USG interests--not for your personal benefit or privacy.\n\n-Notwithstanding the above, using this IS does not constitute consent to PM, LE or CI investigative searching or monitoring of the content of privileged communications, or work product, related to personal representation or services by attorneys, psychotherapists, or clergy, and their assistants. Such communications and work product are private and confidential. See User Agreement for details.","group_id":"V-253445","potential_impacts":"","group_id_src":"V-253445","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The required legal notice must be configured to display before console logon.","discussion":"Failure to display the logon banner prior to a logon attempt will negate legal proceedings resulting from unauthorized access to system resources.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000024-GPOS-00007, SRG-OS-000228-GPOS-00088, SRG-OS-000024-GPOS-00007","mitigations":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (The required legal notice must be configured to display before console logon - Message Content 1)\nTest                    :   true (The required legal notice must be configured to display before console logon - Message Content 2)\nTest                    :   true (The required legal notice must be configured to display before console logon - Message Content 3)\nTest                    :   true (The required legal notice must be configured to display before console logon - Message Content 4)\nTest                    :   true (The required legal notice must be configured to display before console logon - Message Content 5)\nTest                    :   true (The required legal notice must be configured to display before console logon - Message Content 6)\nTest                    :   true (The required legal notice must be configured to display before console logon - Message Content 7)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25344501 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The required legal notice must be configured to display before console logon - Message Content 1\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : One and only one item may match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25344501 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Legal notice text\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'LegalNoticeText'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25344501 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Warning Banner - You are accessing a U.S. Government (USG) Information System (IS) that is provided for USG-authorized use only.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must match the pattern 'You are accessing a U.S. Government \\(USG\\) Information System \\(IS\\) that is provided for USG-authorized use only.'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\n                        : name equals 'LegalNoticeText'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals 'You are accessing a U.S. Government (USG) Information System (IS) that is provided for USG-authorized use only.\n                        : By using this IS (which includes any device attached to this IS), you consent to the following conditions:\n                        : -The USG routinely intercepts and monitors communications on this IS for purposes including, but not limited to, penetration testing, COMSEC monitoring, network operations and defense, personnel misconduct (PM), law enforcement (LE), and counterintelligence (CI) investigations.\n                        : -At any time, the USG may inspect and seize data stored on this IS.\n                        : -Communications using, or data stored on, this IS are not private, are subject to routine monitoring, interception, and search, and may be disclosed or used for any USG-authorized purpose.\n                        : -This IS includes security measures (e.g., authentication and access controls) to protect USG interests--not for your personal benefit or privacy.\n                        : -Notwithstanding the above, using this IS does not constitute consent to PM, LE or CI investigative searching or monitoring of the content of privileged communications, or work product, related to personal representation or services by attorneys, psychotherapists, or clergy, and their assistants. Such communications and work product are private and confidential. See User Agreement for details.'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25344502 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The required legal notice must be configured to display before console logon - Message Content 2\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : One and only one item may match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25344501 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Legal notice text\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\nObject Requirement      :  