se.\n                        : -This IS includes security measures (e.g., authentication and access controls) to protect USG interests--not for your personal benefit or privacy.\n                        : -Notwithstanding the above, using this IS does not constitute consent to PM, LE or CI investigative searching or monitoring of the content of privileged communications, or work product, related to personal representation or services by attorneys, psychotherapists, or clergy, and their assistants. Such communications and work product are private and confidential. See User Agreement for details.'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25344506 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The required legal notice must be configured to display before console logon - Message Content 6\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : One and only one item may match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25344501 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Legal notice text\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'LegalNoticeText'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25344506 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Warning Banner - -This IS includes security measures (e.g., authentication and access controls) to protect USG interests--not for your personal benefit or privacy.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must match the pattern '-This IS includes security measures \\(e.g., authentication and access controls\\) to protect USG interests--not for your personal benefit or privacy.'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\n                        : name equals 'LegalNoticeText'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals 'You are accessing a U.S. Government (USG) Information System (IS) that is provided for USG-authorized use only.\n                        : By using this IS (which includes any device attached to this IS), you consent to the following conditions:\n                        : -The USG routinely intercepts and monitors communications on this IS for purposes including, but not limited to, penetration testing, COMSEC monitoring, network operations and defense, personnel misconduct (PM), law enforcement (LE), and counterintelligence (CI) investigations.\n                        : -At any time, the USG may inspect and seize data stored on this IS.\n                        : -Communications using, or data stored on, this IS are not private, are subject to routine monitoring, interception, and search, and may be disclosed or used for any USG-authorized purpose.\n                        : -This IS includes security measures (e.g., authentication and access controls) to protect USG interests--not for your personal benefit or privacy.\n                        : -Notwithstanding the above, using this IS does not constitute consent to PM, LE or CI investigative searching or monitoring of the content of privileged communications, or work product, related to personal representation or services by attorneys, psychotherapists, or clergy, and their assistants. Such communications and work product are private and confidential. See User Agreement for details.'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25344507 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The required legal notice must be configured to display before console logon - Message Content 7\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : One and only one item may match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25344501 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Legal notice text\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'LegalNoticeText'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25344507 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Warning Banner - -Notwithstanding the above, using this IS does not constitute consent to PM, LE or CI investigative searching or monitoring of the content of privileged communications, or work product, related to personal representation or services by attorneys, psychotherapists, or clergy, and their assistants. Such communications and work product are private and confidential. See User Agreement for details.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must match the pattern '-Notwithstanding the above, using this IS does not constitute consent to PM, LE or CI investigative searching or monitoring of the content of privileged communications, or work product, related to personal representation or services by attorneys, psychotherapists, or clergy, and their assistants. Such communications and work product are private and confidential. See User Agreement for details.'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\n                        : name equals 'LegalNoticeText'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals 'You are accessing a U.S. Government (USG) Information System (IS) that is provided for USG-authorized use only.\n                        : By using this IS (which includes any device attached to this IS), you consent to the following conditions:\n                        : -The USG routinely intercepts and monitors communications on this IS for purposes including, but not limited to, penetration testing, COMSEC monitoring, network operations and defense, personnel misconduct (PM), law enforcement (LE), and counterintelligence (CI) investigations.\n                        : -At any time, the USG may inspect and seize data stored on this IS.\n                        : -Communications using, or data stored on, this IS are not private, are subject to routine monitoring, interception, and search, and may be disclosed or used for any USG-authorized purpose.\n                        : -This IS includes security measures (e.g., authentication and access controls) to protect USG interests--not for your personal benefit or privacy.\n                        : -Notwithstanding the above, using this IS does not constitute consent to PM, LE or CI investigative searching or monitoring of the content of privileged communications, or work product, related to personal representation or services by attorneys, psychotherapists, or clergy, and their assistants. Such communications and work product are private and confidential. See User Agreement for details.'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n"},{"severity":"low","group_title":"SRG-OS-000228-GPOS-00088","ccis":["CCI-000048","CCI-001384","CCI-001385","CCI-001386","CCI-001387","CCI-001388"],"rule_version":"WN11-SO-000080","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"id":"V-253446","title":"SRG-OS-000228-GPOS-00088"},"third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253446r958586_rule","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System\\\n\nValue Name: LegalNoticeCaption\n\nValue Type: REG_SZ\nValue: See message title above\n\n\"DoD Notice and Consent Banner\", \"US Department of Defense Warning Statement\" or a site-defined equivalent, this is a finding.\n\nIf a site-defined title is used, it can in no case contravene or modify the language of the banner text required in WN11-SO-000075.","ia_controls":"","rule_id":"SV-253446r958586","mitigation_control":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"3674BED3-6BF8-1014-B21A-CBBC76E5DC80","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:253446","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml"},"potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253446","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253446","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; \"Interactive logon: Message title for users attempting to log on\" to \"DoD Notice and Consent Banner\", \"US Department of Defense Warning Statement\", or a site-defined equivalent.\n\nIf a site-defined title is used, it can in no case contravene or modify the language of the banner text required in WN11-SO-000075.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The Windows message title for the legal notice must be configured.","mitigations":"","discussion":"Failure to display the logon banner prior to a logon attempt will negate legal proceedings resulting from unauthorized access to system resources.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nTest                    :   false (The Windows dialog box title for the legal banner must be configured. Title Option 1)\nTest                    :   true (The Windows dialog box title for the legal banner must be configured. Title Option 2)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25344601 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : The Windows dialog box title for the legal banner must be configured. Title Option 1\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : One and only one item may match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25344601 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : LegalNoticeCaption Setting\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'LegalNoticeCaption'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25344601 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Logon Banner - DoD Notice and Consent Banner.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must match the pattern 'DoD Notice and Consent Banner'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\n                        : name equals 'LegalNoticeCaption'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals 'US Department of Defense Warning Statement'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25344602 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The Windows dialog box title for the legal banner must be configured. Title Option 2\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : One and only one item may match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25344601 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : LegalNoticeCaption Setting\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'LegalNoticeCaption'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25344602 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Logon Banner - US Department of Defense Warning Statement.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must match the pattern 'US Department of Defense Warning Statement'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\n                        : name equals 'LegalNoticeCaption'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals 'US Department of Defense Warning Statement'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n"},{"severity":"low","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"rule_version":"WN11-SO-000085","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-253447"},"responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253447r991589_rule","check_content":"This is the default configuration for this setting (10 logons to cache).\n\nIf the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE \nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\Winlogon\\\n\nValue Name: CachedLogonsCount\n\nValue Type: REG_SZ\nValue: 10 (or less)\n\nThis setting only applies to domain-joined systems, however, it is configured by default on all systems.","ia_controls":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id":"SV-253447r991589","mitigation_control":"","status":"not_applicable","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253447","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"uuid":"3674C6EF-6BF8-1014-A270-90119E2F128E","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253447","false_positives":"","group_id":"V-253447","potential_impacts":"","fix_text":"This is the default configuration for this setting (10 logons to cache).\n\nConfigure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; \"Interactive logon: Number of previous logons to cache (in case domain controller is not available)\" to \"10\" logons or less.\n\nThis setting only applies to domain-joined systems, however, it is configured by default on all systems.","mitigations":"","discussion":"The default Windows configuration caches the last logon credentials for users who log on interactively to a system. This feature is provided for system availability reasons, such as the user's machine being disconnected from the network or domain controllers being unavailable. Even though the credential cache is well-protected, if a system is attacked, an unauthorized individual may isolate the password to a domain user account using a password-cracking program and gain access to the domain.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Caching of logon credentials must be limited.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n"},{"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-253448"},"reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id":"SV-253448r991589","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253448r991589_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\Winlogon\\\n\nValue Name: SCRemoveOption\n\nValue Type: REG_SZ\nValue: 1 (Lock Workstation) or 2 (Force Logoff)\n\nThis can be left not configured or set to \"No action\" on workstations with the following conditions. This must be documented with the ISSO.\n-The setting cannot be configured due to mission needs, or because it interferes with applications.\n-Policy must be in place that users manually lock workstations when leaving them unattended.\n-The screen saver is properly configured to lock as required.","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","rule_version":"WN11-SO-000095","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","mitigations":"","discussion":"Unattended systems are susceptible to unauthorized use and must be locked. Configuring a system to lock when a smart card is removed will ensure the system is inaccessible when unattended.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The Smart Card removal option must be configured to Force Logoff or Lock Workstation.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Interactive logon: Smart card removal behavior' is set to 'Lock Workstation' or 'Force Logoff')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25344800 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Interactive logon: Smart card removal behavior' is set to 'Lock Workstation' or 'Force Logoff'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\nState Operator          : One or more item-state comparisons may be true.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25344800 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\Winlogon'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'SCRemoveOption'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25445900 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_sz'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25445901 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_sz'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion\\Winlogon'\n                        : name equals 'SCRemoveOption'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995370000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253448","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"uuid":"3674CDD9-6BF8-1014-A461-A22D95717B65","status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; \"Interactive logon: Smart card removal behavior\" to \"Lock Workstation\" or \"Force Logoff\".","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253448","group_id":"V-253448","potential_impacts":""},{"comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id":"SV-253449r958908","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253449r958908_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\LanmanWorkstation\\Parameters\\\n\nValue Name: RequireSecuritySignature\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1","group_tree":{"id":"V-253449","title":"SRG-OS-000423-GPOS-00187"},"responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN11-SO-000100","ccis":["CCI-002418"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000423-GPOS-00187","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Microsoft Network Client: Digitally sign communications (always)' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25344900 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Microsoft Network Client: Digitally sign communications (always)' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25344900 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Check the registry value store at HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\LanmanWorkstation\\Parameters\\RequireSecuritySignature\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\LanmanWorkstation\\Parameters'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'RequireSecuritySignature'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\LanmanWorkstation\\Parameters'\n                        : name equals 'RequireSecuritySignature'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134054567970000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","mitigations":"","discussion":"The server message block (SMB) protocol provides the basis for many network operations. Digitally signed SMB packets aid in preventing man-in-the-middle attacks. If this policy is enabled, the SMB client will only communicate with an SMB server that performs SMB packet signing.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The Windows SMB client must be configured to always perform SMB packet signing.","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; \"Microsoft network client: Digitally sign communications (always)\" to \"Enabled\".","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253449","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253449","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253449"},"uuid":"3674D982-6BF8-1014-B463-89FFCF74BB09","status":"not_a_finding"},{"group_title":"SRG-OS-000074-GPOS-00042","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-000197"],"rule_version":"WN11-SO-000110","weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253450","title":"SRG-OS-000074-GPOS-00042"},"ia_controls":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\LanmanWorkstation\\Parameters\\\n\nValue Name: EnablePlainTextPassword\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0","rule_id_src":"SV-253450r987796_rule","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253450r987796","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"3674E0FC-6BF8-1014-96CF-CE765A9EDDF0","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253450","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253450","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253450","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; \"Microsoft network client: Send unencrypted password to third-party SMB servers\" to \"Disabled\".","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Unencrypted passwords must not be sent to third-party SMB Servers.","discussion":"Some non-Microsoft SMB servers only support unencrypted (plain text) password authentication. Sending plain text passwords across the network, when authenticating to an SMB server, reduces the overall security of the environment. Check with the vendor of the SMB server to see if there is a way to support encrypted password authentication.","mitigations":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Microsoft Network Client: Send unencrypted password to connect to third-party SMB servers' is set to 'Disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25345000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Microsoft Network Client: Send unencrypted password to connect to third-party SMB servers' is set to 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25345000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\LanmanWorkstation\\Parameters'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'EnablePlainTextPassword'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\LanmanWorkstation\\Parameters'\n                        : name equals 'EnablePlainTextPassword'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134054567970000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n"},{"rule_title":"The Windows SMB server must be configured to always perform SMB packet signing.","security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"The server message block (SMB) protocol provides the basis for many network operations. Digitally signed SMB packets aid in preventing man-in-the-middle attacks. If this policy is enabled, the SMB server will only communicate with an SMB client that performs SMB packet signing.","mitigations":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Microsoft network server: Digitally sign communications (always)' is set to