 Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; \"Microsoft network server: Digitally sign communications (always)\" to \"Enabled\".","weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253451","title":"SRG-OS-000423-GPOS-00187"},"check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\LanManServer\\Parameters\\\n\nValue Name: RequireSecuritySignature\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253451r958908_rule","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253451r958908","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"group_title":"SRG-OS-000423-GPOS-00187","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-002418"],"rule_version":"WN11-SO-000120"},{"documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-253452"},"third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253452r991589_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options.\n\nIf the value for \"Network access: Allow anonymous SID/Name translation\" is not set to \"Disabled\", this is a finding.","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id":"SV-253452r991589","mitigation_control":"","severity":"high","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"rule_version":"WN11-SO-000140","mitigations":"","discussion":"Allowing anonymous SID/Name translation can provide sensitive information for accessing a system. Only authorized users must be able to perform such translations.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Anonymous SID/Name translation must not be allowed.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Network access: Allow anonymous SID/Name translation is set to 'Disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25345201 (passwordpolicy_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Network access: Allow anonymous SID/Name translation is set to 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25345201 (passwordpolicy_object)\nObject Comment          : Retrieves a passwordpolicy_object.\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25345201 (passwordpolicy_state)\nState Comment           : This passwordpolicy_state represents a password policy that has a anonymous_name_lookup equal to '0'.\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'anonymous_name_lookup' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : max_passwd_age equals '5184000'\n                        : min_passwd_age equals '86400'\n                        : min_passwd_len equals '14'\n                        : password_hist_len equals '24'\n                        : password_complexity equals '1'\n                        : reversible_encryption equals '0'\n                        : anonymous_name_lookup equals '0'\n","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:253452"},"uuid":"3674EF26-6BF8-1014-9896-B94F724470E1","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253452","group_id":"V-253452","potential_impacts":"","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; \"Network access: Allow anonymous SID/Name translation\" to \"Disabled\"."},{"severity":"high","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"rule_version":"WN11-SO-000145","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-253453"},"responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253453r991589_rule","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa\\\n\nValue Name: RestrictAnonymousSAM\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1","ia_controls":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id":"SV-253453r991589","mitigation_control":"","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253453","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"uuid":"3674F616-6BF8-1014-82E1-8AE73EF625EB","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253453","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253453","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; \"Network access: Do not allow anonymous enumeration of SAM accounts\" to \"Enabled\".","mitigations":"","discussion":"Anonymous enumeration of SAM accounts allows anonymous log on users (null session connections) to list all accounts names, thus providing a list of potential points to attack the system.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Anonymous enumeration of SAM accounts must not be allowed.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Network access: Do not allow anonymous enumeration of SAM accounts' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25345300 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Network access: Do not allow anonymous enumeration of SAM accounts' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25345300 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Check for HKLM\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa\\RestrictAnonymousSAM\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'System\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'RestrictAnonymousSAM'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'System\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa'\n                        : name equals 'RestrictAnonymousSAM'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995350000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n"},{"stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","discussion":"Allowing anonymous logon users (null session connections) to list all account names and enumerate all shared resources can provide a map of potential points to attack the system.","mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Anonymous enumeration of shares must be restricted.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Network access: Do not allow anonymous enumeration of SAM accounts and shares' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25345400 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Network access: Do not allow anonymous enumeration of SAM accounts and shares' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25345400 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'restrictanonymous'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa'\n                        : name equals 'restrictanonymous'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995350000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253454"},"uuid":"3674FDFF-6BF8-1014-963D-E0D751D1A212","status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; \"Network access: Do not allow anonymous enumeration of SAM accounts and shares\" to \"Enabled\".","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253454","false_positives":"","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253454","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000138-GPOS-00069","id":"V-253454"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253454r1137695","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa\\\n\nValue Name: RestrictAnonymous\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253454r1137695_rule","ccis":["CCI-001090"],"group_title":"SRG-OS-000138-GPOS-00069","severity":"high","rule_version":"WN11-SO-000150"},{"discussion":"Access by anonymous users must be restricted. If this setting is enabled, then anonymous users have the same rights and permissions as the built-in Everyone group. Anonymous users must not have these permissions or rights.","mitigations":"","rule_title":"The system must be configured to prevent anonymous users from having the same rights as the Everyone group.","security_override_guidance":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Network access: Let Everyone permissions apply to anonymous users' is set to 'Disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25345500 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Network access: Let Everyone permissions apply to anonymous users' is set to 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25345500 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'EveryoneIncludesAnonymous'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa'\n                        : name equals 'EveryoneIncludesAnonymous'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995350000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253455","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"uuid":"36750559-6BF8-1014-B8A7-93673BA08435","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253455","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253455","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; \"Network access: Let Everyone permissions apply to anonymous users\" to \"Disabled\".","weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-253455"},"check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa\\\n\nValue Name: EveryoneIncludesAnonymous\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253455r991589_rule","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253455r991589","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"rule_version":"WN11-SO-000160"},{"reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000138-GPOS-00069","id":"V-253456"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253456r1137695","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\LanManServer\\Parameters\\\n\nValue Name: RestrictNullSessAccess\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253456r1137695_rule","ccis":["CCI-001090"],"group_title":"SRG-OS-000138-GPOS-00069","severity":"high","rule_version":"WN11-SO-000165","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","discussion":"Allowing anonymous access to named pipes or shares provides the potential for unauthorized system access. This setting restricts access to those defined in \"Network access: Named Pipes that can be accessed anonymously\" and \"Network access: Shares that can be accessed anonymously\", both of which must be blank under other requirements.","mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Anonymous access to Named Pipes and Shares must be restricted.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Network access: Restrict anonymous access to Named Pipes and Shares' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25345600 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Network access: Restrict anonymous access to Named Pipes and Shares' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25345600 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\LanmanServer\\Parameters'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'restrictnullsessaccess'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\LanmanServer\\Parameters'\n                        : name equals 'restrictnullsessaccess'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995390000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253456","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"uuid":"36750CAC-6BF8-1014-825A-89B347B4F7C6","status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; \"Network access: Restrict anonymous access to Named Pipes and Shares\" to \"Enabled\".","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253456","group_id":"V-253456","potential_impacts":""},{"rule_version":"WN11-SO-000167","ccis":["CCI-002235"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id":"SV-253457r1081060","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253457r1081060_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa\\\n\nValue Name: RestrictRemoteSAM\n\nValue Type: REG_SZ\nValue: O:BAG:BAD:(A;;RC;;;BA)\n\nIf a domain application account such as for a management tool requires this user right, this would not be a finding.\nVendor documentation must support the requirement for having the user right.\nThe requirement must be documented with the ISSO.","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","id":"V-253457"},"reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","fix_text":"Navigate to the policy Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; \"Network access: Restrict clients allowed to make remote calls to SAM\".\n\nSelect \"Edit Security\" to configure the \"Security descriptor:\".\n\nAdd \"Administrators\" in \"Group or user names:\" if it is not already listed (this is the default).\n\nSelect \"Administrators\" in \"Group or user names:\".\n\nSelect \"Allow\" for \"Remote Access\" in \"Permissions for \"Administrators\".\n\nClick \"OK\".\n\nThe \"Security descriptor:\" must be populated with \"O:BAG:BAD:(A;;RC;;;BA) for the policy to be enforced.","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253457","group_id":"V-253457","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253457","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"uuid":"367513A1-6BF8-1014-BF18-D8D42CF68996","status":"not_a_finding","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Allow Administrators group to make remote calls to SAM)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.windows:tst:25345700 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Allow Administrators group to make remote calls to SAM\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.windows:obj:25345700 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'RestrictRemoteSAM'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.windows:ste:25345700 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Reg_Sz type and value equals O:BAG:BAD:(A;;RC;;;BA)\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_sz'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to 'O:BAG:BAD:(A;;RC;;;BA)'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa'\n                        : name equals 'RestrictRemoteSAM'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995350000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals 'O:BAG:BAD:(A;;RC;;;BA)'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","mitigations":"","discussion":"The Windows SAM stores users' passwords. Restricting remote rpc connections to the SAM to Administrators helps protect those credentials.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Remote calls to the Security Account Manager (SAM) must be restricted to Administrators."},{"legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253458","false_positives":"","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253458","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; \"Network security: Allow LocalSystem NULL session fallback\" to \"Disabled\".","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253458","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"uuid":"36751BA5-6BF8-1014-B54D-AE03545096C9","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Network security: Allow LocalSystem NULL session fallback' is set to 'Disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25345800 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Network security: Allow LocalSystem NULL session fallback' is set to 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25345800 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\LSA\\MSV1_0'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'allownullsessionfallback'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\LSA\\MSV1_0'\n                        : name equals 'allownullsessionfallback'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134054566350000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","discussion":"NTLM sessions that are allowed to fall back to Null (unauthenticated) sessions may gain unauthorized access.","mitigations":"","rule_title":"NTLM must be prevented from falling back to a Null session.","security_override_guidance":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","rule_version":"WN11-SO-000180","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\LSA\\MSV1_0\\\n\nValue Name: allownullsessionfallback\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253458r991589_rule","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253458r991589","weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-253458"}},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Network Security: Allow PKU2U authentication requests to this computer to use online identities' is set to 'Disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25345900 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Network Security: Allow PKU2U authentication requests to this computer to use online identities' is set to 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25345900 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Check the registry value at HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\LSA\\pku2u\\AllowOnlineID\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\LSA\\pku2u'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'AllowOnlineID'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\LSA\\pku2u'\n                        : name equals 'AllowOnlineID'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134054566350000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","mitigations":"","discussion":"PKU2U is a peer-to-peer authentication protocol.  This setting prevents online identities from authenticating to domain-joined systems. Authentication will be centrally managed with Windows user accounts.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"PKU2U authentication using online identities must be prevented.","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; \"Network security: Allow PKU2U authentication requests to this computer to use online identities\" to \"Disabled\".","group_id_src":"V-253459","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253459","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253459","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"uuid":"36752AAD-6BF8-1014-9F91-D903EB1D523C","status":"not_a_finding","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id":"SV-253459r991589","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253459r991589_rule","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\LSA\\pku2u\\\n\nValue Name: AllowOnlineID\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0","ia_controls":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253459","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","rule_version":"WN11-SO-000185","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},{"rule_version":"WN11-SO-000190","ccis":["CCI-000803"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000120-GPOS-00061","rule_id":"SV-253460r971535","mitigation_control":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id_src":"SV-253460r971535_rule","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System\\Kerberos\\Parameters\\\n\nValue Name: SupportedEncryptionTypes\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x7ffffff8 (2147483640)","ia_controls":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000120-GPOS-00061","id":"V-253460"},"responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; \"Network security: Configure encryption types allowed for Kerberos\" to \"Enabled\" with only the following selected:\n\nAES128_HMAC_SHA1\nAES256_HMAC_SHA1\nFuture encryption types","group_id":"V-253460","potential_impacts":"","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253460","uuid":"367532CA-6BF8-1014-838B-990954244134","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253460"},"status":"not_a_finding","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Network Security: Configure encryption types allowed for Kerberos' is set to 'Enabled' with 'AES128_HMAC_SHA1', 'AES256_HMAC_SHA1', 'Future encryption types')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25346000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Network Security: Configure encryption types allowed for Kerberos' is set to 'Enabled' with 'AES128_HMAC_SHA1', 'AES256_HMAC_SHA1', 'Future encryption types'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25346000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System\\Kerberos\\Parameters'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'SupportedEncryptionTypes'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25346000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Reg_Dword type and value equals 2147483640 for AES128_HMAC_SHA1, AES256_HMAC_SHA1, and Future_Encryption_Types\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '2147483640'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System\\Kerberos\\Parameters'\n                        : name equals 'SupportedEncryptionTypes'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134054567570000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '2147483640'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","rule_title":"Kerberos encryption types must be configured to prevent the use of DES and RC4 encryption suites.","security_override_guidance":"","mitigations":"","discussion":"Certain encryption types are no longer considered secure. This setting configures a minimum encryption type for Kerberos, preventing the use of the DES and RC4 encryption suites."},{"rule_version":"WN11-SO-000195","group_title":"SRG-OS-000073-GPOS-00041","severity":"high","ccis":["CCI-004062","CCI-000196"],"check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa\\\n\nValue Name: NoLMHash\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253461r1051056_rule","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253461r1051056","weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000073-GPOS-00041","id":"V-253461"},"legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253461","false_positives":"","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253461","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; \"Network security: Do not store LAN Manager hash value on next password change\" to \"Enabled\".","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253461"},"uuid":"367539EC-6BF8-1014-92FD-939882BC440A","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Network security: Do not store LAN Manager hash value on next password change' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25346100 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Network security: Do not store LAN Manager hash value on next password change' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25346100 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Check the contents of HKLM\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa\\NoLMHash\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'System\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'NoLMHash'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'System\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa'\n                        : name equals 'NoLMHash'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995350000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","discussion":"The LAN Manager hash uses a weak encryption algorithm and there are several tools available that use this hash to retrieve account passwords. This setting controls whether or not a LAN Manager hash of the password is stored in the SAM the next time the password is changed.","mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The system must be configured to prevent the storage of the LAN Manager hash of passwords.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4"},{"fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; \"Network security: LAN Manager authentication level\" to \"Send NTLMv2 response only. Refuse LM &amp; NTLM\".","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253462","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253462","uuid":"36754272-6BF8-1014-8775-DA77308CBB0C","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253462"},"status":"not_a_finding","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Network security: LAN Manager authentication level' is set to 'Send NTLMv2 response only. Refuse LM &amp; NTLM' (Level 5))\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25346200 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Network security: LAN Manager authentication level' is set to 'Send NTLMv2 response only. Refuse LM &amp; NTLM' (Level 5)\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25346200 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'LmCompatibilityLevel'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25346200 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Reg_Dword type and value equals 5\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '5'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa'\n                        : name equals 'LmCompatibilityLevel'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995350000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '5'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The LanMan authentication level must be set to send NTLMv2 response only, and to refuse LM and NTLM.","discussion":"The Kerberos v5 authentication protocol is the default for authentication of users who are logging on to domain accounts. NTLM, which is less secure, is retained in later Windows versions for compatibility with clients and servers that are running earlier versions of Windows or applications that still use it. It is also used to authenticate logons to stand-alone computers that are running later versions.","mitigations":"","rule_version":"WN11-SO-000205","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","severity":"high","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253462r991589","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","ia_controls":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa\\\n\nValue Name: LmCompatibilityLevel\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 5","rule_id_src":"SV-253462r991589_rule","responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253462","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false"},{"group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"rule_version":"WN11-SO-000210","weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-253463"},"check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\LDAP\\\n\nValue Name: LDAPClientIntegrity\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253463r991589_rule","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253463r991589","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253463","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"uuid":"367549AF-6BF8-1014-82D3-D9F9465F49AA","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253463","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253463","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; \"Network security: LDAP client signing requirements\" to \"Negotiate signing\" at a minimum.","discussion":"This setting controls the signing requirements for LDAP clients. This setting must be set to Negotiate signing or Require signing, depending on the environment and type of LDAP server in use.","mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The system must be configured to the required LDAP client signing level.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Network security: LDAP client signing requirements' is set to 'Negotiate signing' or 'Require signing')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25346300 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Network security: LDAP client signing requirements' is set to 'Negotiate signing' or 'Require signing'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\nState Operator          : One or more item-state comparisons may be true.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25346300 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\LDAP'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'LDAPClientIntegrity'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000002 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\LDAP'\n                        : name equals 'LDAPClientIntegrity'\n                        : last_write_time equals '133564299920000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n"},{"documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"id":"V-253464","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253464r991589_rule","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa\\MSV1_0\\\n\nValue Name: NTLMMinClientSec\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x20080000 (537395200)","ia_controls":"","rule_id":"SV-253464r991589","mitigation_control":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"rule_version":"WN11-SO-000215","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The system must be configured to meet the minimum session security requirement for NTLM SSP based clients.","mitigations":"","discussion":"Microsoft has implemented a variety of security support providers for use with RPC sessions. All of the options must be enabled to ensure the maximum security level.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (The system is configured to meet the minimum session security requirement for NTLM SSP based clients.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25346400 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The system is configured to meet the minimum session security requirement for NTLM SSP based clients.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25346400 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa\\MSV1_0'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'NTLMMinClientSec'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25346500 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Value bitwise and 537395200\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '537395200'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa\\MSV1_0'\n                        : name equals 'NTLMMinClientSec'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134054566350000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '537395200'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"36755190-6BF8-1014-82DB-974E46E45C7C","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253464"},"group_id":"V-253464","potential_impacts":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253464","false_positives":"","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; \"Network security: Minimum session security for NTLM SSP based (including secure RPC) clients\" to \"Require NTLMv2 session security\" and \"Require 128-bit encryption\" (all options selected)."},{"ia_controls":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa\\MSV1_0\\\n\nValue Name: NTLMMinServerSec\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x20080000 (537395200)","rule_id_src":"SV-253465r991589_rule","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253465r991589","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-253465"},"rule_version":"WN11-SO-000220","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Network security: Minimum session security for NTLM SSP based (including secure RPC) servers' is set to 'Require NTLMv2 session security' and 'Require 128-bit encryption')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25346500 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Network security: Minimum session security for NTLM SSP based (including secure RPC) servers' is set to 'Require NTLMv2 session security' and 'Require 128-bit encryption'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25346500 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa\\MSV1_0'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'NTLMMinServerSec'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25346500 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Value bitwise and 537395200\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '537395200'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa\\MSV1_0'\n                        : name equals 'NTLMMinServerSec'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134054566350000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '537395200'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","rule_title":"The system must be configured to meet the minimum session security requirement for NTLM SSP based servers.","security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"Microsoft has implemented a variety of security support providers for use with RPC sessions. All of the options must be enabled to ensure the maximum security level.","mitigations":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","group_id":"V-253465","potential_impacts":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253465","false_positives":"","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; \"Network security: Minimum session security for NTLM SSP based (including secure RPC) servers\" to \"Require NTLMv2 session security\" and \"Require 128-bit encryption\" (all options selected).","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"36755B02-6BF8-1014-B70B-82204C825B86","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253465"}},{"stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The system must be configured to use FIPS-compliant algorithms for encryption, hashing, and signing.","mitigations":"","discussion":"This setting ensures that the system uses algorithms that are FIPS-compliant for encryption, hashing, and signing. FIPS-compliant algorithms meet specific standards established by the U.S. Government and must be the algorithms used for all OS encryption functions.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     false ('System cryptography: Use FIPS compliant algorithms for encryption, hashing, and signing' is set to 'Enabled')\nResult Analysis         :          HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa\\FIPSAlgorithmPolicy\\Enabled\\value = '0' failed test of 'equals' compared to '1' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25346600 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : 'System cryptography: Use FIPS compliant algorithms for encryption, hashing, and signing' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25346600 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa\\FIPSAlgorithmPolicy'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'Enabled'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa\\FIPSAlgorithmPolicy'\n                        : name equals 'Enabled'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134054532270000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\nResult Analysis         : HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa\\FIPSAlgorithmPolicy\\Enabled\\value = '0' failed test of 'equals' compared to '1' \n","uuid":"36756400-6BF8-1014-9D94-AF8FADF096B2","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253466"},"status":"open","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; \"System cryptography: Use FIPS compliant algorithms for encryption, hashing, and signing\" to \"Enabled\".","group_id":"V-253466","potential_impacts":"","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253466","group_tree":{"id":"V-253466","title":"SRG-OS-000478-GPOS-00223"},"third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","rule_id":"SV-253466r1137699","mitigation_control":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id_src":"SV-253466r1137699_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Lsa\\FIPSAlgorithmPolicy\\\n\nValue Name: Enabled\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1\n \nWarning: Clients with this setting enabled will not be able to communicate via digitally encrypted or signed protocols with servers that do not support these algorithms.","ccis":["CCI-002450"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000478-GPOS-00223","rule_version":"WN11-SO-000230"},{"rule_version":"WN11-SO-000240","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","severity":"low","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253467r991589","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Session Manager\\\n\nValue Name: ProtectionMode\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253467r991589_rule","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","id":"V-253467"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; \"System objects: Strengthen default permissions of internal system objects (e.g. Symbolic links)\" to \"Enabled\".","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253467","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253467","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253467"},"uuid":"36756DE1-6BF8-1014-80DB-F5039CC61248","status":"not_a_finding","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('System objects: Strengthen default permissions of internal system objects (e.g. Symbolic links)' is set to 'Enabled'.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25346700 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'System objects: Strengthen default permissions of internal system objects (e.g. Symbolic links)' is set to 'Enabled'.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25346700 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Session Manager'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'ProtectionMode'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Control\\Session Manager'\n                        : name equals 'ProtectionMode'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330997150000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","discussion":"Windows systems maintain a global list of shared system resources such as DOS device names, mutexes, and semaphores. Each type of object is created with a default DACL that specifies who can access the objects with what permissions. If this policy is enabled, the default DACL is stronger, allowing non-admin users to read shared objects, but not modify shared objects that they did not create.","mitigations":"","rule_title":"The default permissions of global system objects must be increased.","security_override_guidance":""},{"security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"User Account Control approval mode for the built-in Administrator must be enabled.","discussion":"User Account Control (UAC) is a security mechanism for limiting the elevation of privileges, including administrative accounts, unless authorized. This setting configures the built-in Administrator account so that it runs in Admin Approval Mode.","mitigations":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Verifies 'User Account Control: Admin Approval Mode for the Built-in Administrator account' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25346800 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Verifies 'User Account Control: Admin Approval Mode for the Built-in Administrator account' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25346800 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'FilterAdministratorToken'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\n                        : name equals 'FilterAdministratorToken'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"367574F7-6BF8-1014-B1D2-B138E43C2728","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253468"},"potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253468","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253468","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; \"User Account Control: Admin Approval Mode for the Built-in Administrator account\" to \"Enabled\".","weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000373-GPOS-00157","id":"V-253468"},"ia_controls":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System\\\n\nValue Name: FilterAdministratorToken\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1","rule_id_src":"SV-253468r1051057_rule","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253468r1051057","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"group_title":"SRG-OS-000373-GPOS-00157","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-002038"],"rule_version":"WN11-SO-000245"},{"uuid":"36757FB5-6BF8-1014-B036-95E4890B5385","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253469"},"status":"open","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; \"User Account Control: Behavior of the elevation prompt for administrators in Admin Approval Mode\" to \"Prompt for consent on the secure desktop\".","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253469","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253469","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"User Account Control must prompt administrators for consent on the secure desktop.","mitigations":"","discussion":"User Account Control (UAC) is a security mechanism for limiting the elevation of privileges, including administrative accounts, unless authorized. This setting configures the elevation requirements for logged on administrators to complete a task that requires raised privileges.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     false ('User Account Control: Behavior of the elevation prompt for administrators in Admin Approval Mode' is set to 'Prompt for consent on the secure desktop')\nResult Analysis         :          HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System\\ConsentPromptBehaviorAdmin\\value = '0' failed test of 'equals' compared to '2' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25346900 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : 'User Account Control: Behavior of the elevation prompt for administrators in Admin Approval Mode' is set to 'Prompt for consent on the secure desktop'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25346900 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'ConsentPromptBehaviorAdmin'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000002 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\n                        : name equals 'ConsentPromptBehaviorAdmin'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\nResult Analysis         : HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System\\ConsentPromptBehaviorAdmin\\value = '0' failed test of 'equals' compared to '2' \n","ccis":["CCI-001084"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000134-GPOS-00068","rule_version":"WN11-SO-000250","group_tree":{"id":"V-253469","title":"SRG-OS-000134-GPOS-00068"},"responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","rule_id":"SV-253469r958518","mitigation_control":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id_src":"SV-253469r958518_rule","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System\\\n\nValue Name: ConsentPromptBehaviorAdmin\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 2 (Prompt for consent on the secure desktop)","ia_controls":""},{"security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows 11 must use multifactor authentication for local and network access to privileged and nonprivileged accounts.","mitigations":"","discussion":"Without the use of multifactor authentication, the ease of access to privileged and nonprivileged functions is greatly increased. \n\nAll domain accounts must be enabled for multifactor authentication with the exception of local emergency accounts. \n\nMultifactor authentication requires using two or more factors to achieve authentication.\n\nFactors include: \n\n1) Something a user knows (e.g., password/PIN);\n\n2) Something a user has (e.g., cryptographic identification device, token); and\n\n3) Something a user is (e.g., biometric).\n\nA privileged account is defined as an information system account with authorizations of a privileged user.\n\nNetwork access is defined as access to an information system by a user (or a process acting on behalf of a user) communicating through a network (e.g., local area network, wide area network, or the internet).\n\nLocal access is defined as access to an organizational information system by a user (or process acting on behalf of a user) communicating through a direct connection without the use of a network.\n\nThe DoD CAC with DoD-approved PKI is an example of multifactor authentication.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000106-GPOS-00053, SRG-OS-000107-GPOS-00054, SRG-OS-000108-GPOS-00055","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","status":"not_applicable","uuid":"36758554-6BF8-1014-9C1D-F0C73696C1C6","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253470"},"group_id":"V-253470","potential_impacts":"","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253470","fix_text":"For nondomain joined systems, configuring Windows Hello for sign-on options would be suggested based on the organization's needs and capabilities.","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"id":"V-253470","title":"SRG-OS-000105-GPOS-00052"},"third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253470r1106510_rule","check_content":"If the system is not a member of a domain, this is Not Applicable.\n\nIf all of the following settings exist and are populated, this is not a finding.\n\n\\HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Cryptography\\Calais\\Readers\n\\HKLM\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Cryptography\\Calais\\SmartCards","ia_controls":"","rule_id":"SV-253470r1106510","mitigation_control":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000105-GPOS-00052","ccis":["CCI-000765"],"rule_version":"WN11-SO-000251"},{"legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253471","false_positives":"","group_id":"V-253471","potential_impacts":"","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; \"User Account Control: Behavior of the elevation prompt for standard users\" to \"Automatically deny elevation requests\".","status":"open","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253471","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"uuid":"36758A32-6BF8-1014-9262-B294330344AE","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     false (Verifies 'User Account Control: Behavior of the elevation prompt for standard users' is set to 'Automatically deny elevation requests')\nResult Analysis         :          HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System\\ConsentPromptBehaviorUser\\value = '3' failed test of 'equals' compared to '0' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25347100 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Verifies 'User Account Control: Behavior of the elevation prompt for standard users' is set to 'Automatically deny elevation requests'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25347100 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'ConsentPromptBehaviorUser'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\n                        : name equals 'ConsentPromptBehaviorUser'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '3'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\nResult Analysis         : HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System\\ConsentPromptBehaviorUser\\value = '3' failed test of 'equals' compared to '0' \n","mitigations":"","discussion":"User Account Control (UAC) is a security mechanism for limiting the elevation of privileges, including administrative accounts, unless authorized. Denying elevation requests from standard user accounts requires tasks that need elevation to be initiated by accounts with administrative privileges. This ensures correct accounts are used on the system for privileged tasks to help mitigate credential theft.","rule_title":"User Account Control must automatically deny elevation requests for standard users.","security_override_guidance":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","rule_version":"WN11-SO-000255","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000373-GPOS-00157","ccis":["CCI-002038"],"rule_id_src":"SV-253471r1051058_rule","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System\\\n\nValue Name: ConsentPromptBehaviorUser\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0","ia_controls":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id":"SV-253471r1051058","mitigation_control":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"id":"V-253471","title":"SRG-OS-000373-GPOS-00157"},"reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":""},{"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000134-GPOS-00068","ccis":["CCI-001084"],"rule_version":"WN11-SO-000260","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000134-GPOS-00068","id":"V-253472"},"reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253472r958518_rule","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System\\\n\nValue Name: EnableInstallerDetection\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1","ia_controls":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id":"SV-253472r958518","mitigation_control":"","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253472","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"uuid":"367593F8-6BF8-1014-B417-945D16A5174A","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253472","group_id":"V-253472","potential_impacts":"","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; \"User Account Control: Detect application installations and prompt for elevation\" to \"Enabled\".","mitigations":"","discussion":"User Account Control (UAC) is a security mechanism for limiting the elevation of privileges, including administrative accounts, unless authorized. This setting requires Windows to respond to application installation requests by prompting for credentials.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"User Account Control must be configured to detect application installations and prompt for elevation.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('User Account Control: Detect application installations and prompt for elevation' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25347200 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'User Account Control: Detect application installations and prompt for elevation' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25347200 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'EnableInstallerDetection'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\n                        : name equals 'EnableInstallerDetection'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n"},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('User Account Control: Only elevate UIAccess applications that are installed in secure locations' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25347300 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'User Account Control: Only elevate UIAccess applications that are installed in secure locations' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25347300 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'EnableSecureUIAPaths'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\n                        : name equals 'EnableSecureUIAPaths'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"User Account Control must only elevate UIAccess applications that are installed in secure locations.","mitigations":"","discussion":"User Account Control (UAC) is a security mechanism for limiting the elevation of privileges, including administrative accounts, unless authorized. This setting configures Windows to only allow applications installed in a secure location on the file system, such as the Program Files or the Windows\\System32 folders, to run with elevated privileges.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253473","group_id_src":"V-253473","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; \"User Account Control: Only elevate UIAccess applications that are installed in secure locations\" to \"Enabled\".","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"36759C30-6BF8-1014-AA21-D126BCC8B235","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253473","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"rule_id_src":"SV-253473r958518_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System\\\n\nValue Name: EnableSecureUIAPaths\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1","rule_id":"SV-253473r958518","mitigation_control":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000134-GPOS-00068","id":"V-253473"},"reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","rule_version":"WN11-SO-000265","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000134-GPOS-00068","ccis":["CCI-001084"]},{"rule_version":"WN11-SO-000270","ccis":["CCI-002038"],"group_title":"SRG-OS-000373-GPOS-00157","severity":"medium","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253474r1051059","ia_controls":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System\\\n\nValue Name: EnableLUA\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1","rule_id_src":"SV-253474r1051059_rule","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253474","title":"SRG-OS-000373-GPOS-00157"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; \"User Account Control: Run all administrators in Admin Approval Mode\" to \"Enabled\".","group_id_src":"V-253474","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id":"V-253474","potential_impacts":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253474","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"uuid":"3675A482-6BF8-1014-BC78-F4287A38DE8F","status":"not_a_finding","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Verifies 'User Account Control: Run all administrators in Admin Approval Mode' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25347400 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Verifies 'User Account Control: Run all administrators in Admin Approval Mode' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25347400 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'EnableLUA'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\n                        : name equals 'EnableLUA'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","discussion":"User Account Control (UAC) is a security mechanism for limiting the elevation of privileges, including administrative accounts, unless authorized. This setting enables UAC.","mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"User Account Control must run all administrators in Admin Approval Mode, enabling UAC."},{"rule_version":"WN11-SO-000275","ccis":["CCI-001084"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000134-GPOS-00068","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id":"SV-253475r958518","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253475r958518_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System\\\n\nValue Name: EnableVirtualization\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1","group_tree":{"id":"V-253475","title":"SRG-OS-000134-GPOS-00068"},"reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; Security Options &gt;&gt; \"User Account Control: Virtualize file and registry write failures to per-user locations\" to \"Enabled\".","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253475","false_positives":"","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253475","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253475"},"uuid":"3675ABEE-6BF8-1014-9641-EC9F0629A0D6","status":"not_a_finding","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('User Account Control: Virtualize file and registry write failures to per-user locations' is set to 'Enabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25347500 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'User Account Control: Virtualize file and registry write failures to per-user locations' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25347500 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'EnableVirtualization'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\System'\n                        : name equals 'EnableVirtualization'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995380000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","mitigations":"","discussion":"User Account Control (UAC) is a security mechanism for limiting the elevation of privileges, including administrative accounts, unless authorized. This setting configures non-UAC compliant applications to run in virtualized file and registry entries in per-user locations, allowing them to run.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"User Account Control must virtualize file and registry write failures to per-user locations."},{"documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"id":"V-253476","title":"SRG-OS-000076-GPOS-00044"},"third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253476r1051060_rule","check_content":"If there are no enabled local Administrator accounts, this is Not Applicable.\n\nReview the password last set date for the enabled local Administrator account.\n\nOn the standalone or domain-joined workstation:\n\nOpen \"PowerShell\".\n\nEnter \"Get-LocalUser -Name * | Select-Object *\".\n\nIf the \"PasswordLastSet\" date is greater than \"60\" days old for the local Administrator account for administering the computer/domain, this is a finding.\n\nVerify LAPS is configured and operational. \n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; System &gt;&gt; LAPS &gt;&gt; Password Settings &gt;&gt; Set to enabled. Password Complexity, large letters + small letters + numbers + special, Password Length 14, Password Age 60. If not configured as shown, this is a finding. \n\nVerify LAPS Operational logs &gt;&gt; Event Viewer &gt;&gt; Applications and Services Logs &gt;&gt; Microsoft &gt;&gt; Windows &gt;&gt; LAPS &gt;&gt; Operational. Verify LAPS policy process is completing. If it is not, this is a finding.","ia_controls":"","rule_id":"SV-253476r1051060","mitigation_control":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000076-GPOS-00044","ccis":["CCI-004066","CCI-000199"],"rule_version":"WN11-SO-000280","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Passwords for enabled local Administrator accounts must be changed at least every 60 days.","mitigations":"","discussion":"The longer a password is in use, the greater the opportunity for someone to gain unauthorized knowledge of the password. A local Administrator account is not generally used and its password may not be changed as frequently as necessary. Changing the password for enabled Administrator accounts on a regular basis will limit its exposure.\n\nWindows LAPS must be used to change the built-in Administrator account password.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Password Age Check: Verify all enabled local Administrator accounts passwords are less than 60 days old)\nResult Analysis         :        WKS1-SOTERIA\\Degthat = '324' failed test of 'less than or equal' compared to '60' \nTest                    :   false (LAPS Compliance: Password Age - 60)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\LAPS\\PasswordAgeDays'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nTest                    :   false (LAPS Compliance: Password Length - 14)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\LAPS\\PasswordLength'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nTest                    :   false (LAPS Compliance: Password Complexity - large letters + small letters + numbers + specials)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\LAPS\\PasswordComplexity'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nTest                    :   false (Verify LAPS policy process is completing)\nResult Analysis         :        Failed state entity existence check.  ,  Element: 'subexpression' does not exist.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25347601 (user_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Password Age Check: Verify all enabled local Administrator accounts passwords are less than 60 days old\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25347601 (user_object)\nObject Comment          : Enabled Local Administrators\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'user' must match the pattern '.*'\nInclude Items If        : group equals 'Administrators'\nInclude Items If        : enabled equals 'true'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25347601 (user_state)\nState Comment           : Confirm that all enabled local Administrators have a password age less than or equal to 60 days\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'password_age_days' must be less than or equal to '60'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : user equals 'WKS1-SOTERIA\\Degthat'\n                        : enabled equals 'true'\n                        : group equals 'Administrators'\n                        : last_logon equals '1788627762'\n                        : full_name equals ''\n                        : comment equals ''\n                        : password_age_days equals '324'\n\nResult Analysis         : WKS1-SOTERIA\\Degthat = '324' failed test of 'less than or equal' compared to '60' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25347602 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : LAPS Compliance: Password Age - 60\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25347602 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Windows LAPS PasswordAgeDays\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\LAPS'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'PasswordAgeDays'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25347602 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Registry value must be of type reg_dword and value less than or equals 60\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be less than or equal to '60'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\LAPS\\PasswordAgeDays'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25347603 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : LAPS Compliance: Password Length - 14\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25347603 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Windows LAPS PasswordLength\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\LAPS'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'PasswordLength'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25347603 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Registry value must be of type reg_dword and value greater than or equals 14\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be greater than or equal to '14'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\LAPS\\PasswordLength'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25347604 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : LAPS Compliance: Password Complexity - large letters + small letters + numbers + specials\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25347604 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Windows LAPS PasswordComplexity\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\LAPS'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'PasswordComplexity'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25347604 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Registry value must be of type reg_dword and value equals 4\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '4'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\LAPS\\PasswordComplexity'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25347605 (shellcommand_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Verify LAPS policy process is completing\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : At least one collected item must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25347605 (shellcommand_object)\nObject Comment          : Operational logs - Event Viewer - Applications and Services Logs - Microsoft - Windows - LAPS - Operational\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'shell' must be equal to 'powershell'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'command' must be equal to 'get-winevent -logname Microsoft-Windows-LAPS/Operational -MaxEvents 50'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'pattern' must be equal to 'LAPS policy processing (\\w+)\\.'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:25347605 (shellcommand_state)\nState Comment           : LAPS Operational\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'shell' must be equal to 'powershell'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'command' must be equal to 'get-winevent -logname Microsoft-Windows-LAPS/Operational -MaxEvents 50'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'subexpression' must match the pattern 'succeeded'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : shell equals 'powershell'\n                        : command equals 'get-winevent -logname Microsoft-Windows-LAPS/Operational -MaxEvents 50'\n                        : pattern equals 'LAPS policy processing (\\w+)\\.'\n                        : exit_status equals ''\n                        : stderr_line equals 'get-winevent : No events were found that match the specified selection criteria.'\n                        : stderr_line equals 'At line:1 char:1'\n                        : stderr_line equals '+ get-winevent -logname Microsoft-Windows-LAPS/Operational -MaxEvents 5 ...'\n                        : stderr_line equals '+ ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~'\n                        : stderr_line equals '    + CategoryInfo          : ObjectNotFound: (:) [Get-WinEvent], Exception'\n                        : stderr_line equals '    + FullyQualifiedErrorId : NoMatchingEventsFound,Microsoft.PowerShell.Commands.GetWinEventCommand'\n                        : stderr_line equals ' '\n\nResult Analysis         : Failed state entity existence check.  ,  Element: 'subexpression' does not exist.\n","status":"open","uuid":"3675B375-6BF8-1014-8BEB-EA8557D6E2B1","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:253476","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml"},"group_id":"V-253476","potential_impacts":"","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253476","fix_text":"Change the enabled local Administrator account password at least every 60 days. \n\nWindows LAPS must be used to change the built-in Administrator account password. Domain-joined and nondomain-joined systems can configure this to occur more frequently. LAPS will change the password every 30 days by default. \n\nMore information is available at:\nhttps://techcommunity.microsoft.com/t5/windows-it-pro-blog/by-popular-demand-windows-laps-available-now/ba-p/3788747\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows-server/identity/laps/laps-overview#windows-laps-supported-platforms-and-azure-ad-laps-preview-status"},{"status":"open","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253477"},"uuid":"3675C479-6BF8-1014-8190-F72761FD8EE5","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253477","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253477","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for User Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Start Menu and Taskbar &gt;&gt; Notifications &gt;&gt; \"Turn off toast notifications on the lock screen\" to \"Enabled\".","discussion":"Toast notifications that are displayed on the lock screen could display sensitive information to unauthorized personnel. Turning off this feature will limit access to the information to a logged on user.","mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Toast notifications to the lock screen must be turned off.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Turn off toast notifications on the lock screen' is set to 'Enabled')\nTest                    :     false (For the current user, 'Turn off toast notifications on the lock screen' is set to 'Enabled')\nResult Analysis         :          Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_CURRENT_USER\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\PushNotifications\\NoToastApplicationNotificationOnLockScreen'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25347700 (ntuser_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Turn off toast notifications on the lock screen' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : All collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25347700 (ntuser_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\PushNotifications'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'NoToastApplicationNotificationOnLockScreen'\nExclude Items If        : enabled equals 'false'\nExclude Items If        : days_since_modified is greater than '35'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000022 (ntuser_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : key equals 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\PushNotifications'\n                        : name equals 'NoToastApplicationNotificationOnLockScreen'\n                        : sid equals 'S-1-5-21-1196677333-4084102320-1286229203-1001'\n                        : username equals 'WKS1-SOTERIA\\Degthat'\n                        : account_type equals 'local'\n                        : logged_on equals 'false'\n                        : days_since_last_logon equals '16'\n                        : enabled equals 'true'\n                        : date_modified equals '134331012980000000'\n                        : days_since_modified equals '1'\n                        : filepath equals 'C:\\Users\\Degthat\\ntuser.dat'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134317136990000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25347701 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : For the current user, 'Turn off toast notifications on the lock screen' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25347701 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_CURRENT_USER'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\PushNotifications'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'NoToastApplicationNotificationOnLockScreen'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_CURRENT_USER\\Software\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\PushNotifications\\NoToastApplicationNotificationOnLockScreen'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","severity":"low","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"rule_version":"WN11-UC-000015","weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253477","title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049"},"ia_controls":"","check_content":"If the following registry value does not exist or is not configured as specified, this is a finding:\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_CURRENT_USER\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\PushNotifications\\\n\nValue Name: NoToastApplicationNotificationOnLockScreen\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 1","rule_id_src":"SV-253477r958478_rule","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253477r958478"},{"ccis":["CCI-000366"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","rule_version":"WN11-UC-000020","group_tree":{"id":"V-253478","title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227"},"reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","rule_id":"SV-253478r991589","mitigation_control":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id_src":"SV-253478r991589_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"The default behavior is for Windows to mark file attachments with their zone information.\n\nIf it exists and is configured with a value of \"1\", this is a finding.\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_CURRENT_USER\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\Attachments\\\n\nValue Name: SaveZoneInformation\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000002 (2) (or if the Value Name does not exist)","uuid":"3675D06C-6BF8-1014-BDA5-CAC3F8F10B9E","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253478","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"The default behavior is for Windows to mark file attachments with their zone information.\n\nTo correct this, configure the policy value for User Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Attachment Manager &gt;&gt; \"Do not preserve zone information in file attachments\" to \"Not Configured\" or \"Disabled\".","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253478","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253478","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","rule_title":"Zone information must be preserved when saving attachments.","security_override_guidance":"","mitigations":"","discussion":"Preserving zone of origin (internet, intranet, local, restricted) information on file attachments allows Windows to determine risk.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true ('Do not preserve zone information in file attachments' is set to 'Not Configured' or 'Disabled')\nTest                    :     true (For the current user, 'Do not preserve zone information in file attachments' is set to 'Not Configured' or 'Disabled')\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25347800 (ntuser_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 'Do not preserve zone information in file attachments' is set to 'Not Configured' or 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25347800 (ntuser_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\Attachments'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'SaveZoneInformation'\nExclude Items If        : enabled equals 'false'\nExclude Items If        : days_since_modified is greater than '35'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000023 (ntuser_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : does not exist\n                        : key does not exist\n                        : sid equals 'S-1-5-21-1196677333-4084102320-1286229203-1001'\n                        : username equals 'WKS1-SOTERIA\\Degthat'\n                        : account_type equals 'local'\n                        : logged_on equals 'false'\n                        : days_since_last_logon equals '16'\n                        : enabled equals 'true'\n                        : date_modified equals '134331012980000000'\n                        : days_since_modified equals '1'\n                        : filepath equals 'C:\\Users\\Degthat\\ntuser.dat'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25347801 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : For the current user, 'Do not preserve zone information in file attachments' is set to 'Not Configured' or 'Disabled'\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25347801 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_CURRENT_USER'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Policies\\Attachments'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'SaveZoneInformation'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000002 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '2'\n"},{"ccis":["CCI-002235"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","rule_version":"WN11-UR-000005","group_tree":{"id":"V-253479","title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125"},"reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id":"SV-253479r958726","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253479r958726_rule","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any groups or accounts are granted the \"Access Credential Manager as a trusted caller\" user right, this is a finding.","ia_controls":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253479"},"uuid":"3675D97E-6BF8-1014-8F86-F83972CC4D42","status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; \"Access Credential Manager as a trusted caller\" to be defined but containing no entries (blank).","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253479","group_id":"V-253479","potential_impacts":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","mitigations":"","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nAccounts with the \"Access Credential Manager as a trusted caller\" user right may be able to retrieve the credentials of other accounts from Credential Manager.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The \"Access Credential Manager as a trusted caller\" user right must not be assigned to any groups or accounts.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Access Credential Manager as a trusted caller - None)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25347900 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Access Credential Manager as a trusted caller - None\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000008 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : All security principles\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'security_principle' must match the pattern '.+'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25347900 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Access Credential Manager as a trusted caller\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'setrustedcredmanaccessnameright' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : setrustedcredmanaccessnameright equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : setrustedcredmanaccessnameright equals '0' for: Access Control Assistance Operators, Administrators, Backup Operators, Cryptographic Operators, Device Owners, Distributed COM Users, Event Log Readers, Guests, Hyper-V Administrators, IIS_IUSRS, Network Configuration Operators, OpenSSH Users, Performance Log Users, Performance Monitor Users, Power Users, Remote Desktop Users, Remote Management Users, Replicator, System Managed Accounts Group, User Mode Hardware Operators, Users, DefaultAccount, WKS1-SOTERIA\\Degthat, Visitor, WDAGUtilityAccount, X_Admin, NETWORK SERVICE, LOCAL SERVICE, SYSTEM, IUSR, TERMINAL SERVER USER, Authenticated Users, ENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS, PROXY, ANONYMOUS LOGON, SERVICE, INTERACTIVE, BATCH, NETWORK, DIALUP, CREATOR GROUP SERVER, CREATOR OWNER SERVER, CREATOR GROUP, CREATOR OWNER, Everyone, Window Manager\\Window Manager Group, RESTRICTED SERVICES\\ALL RESTRICTED SERVICES, NT SERVICE\\autotimesvc, NT SERVICE\\ALL SERVICES, RESTRICTED SERVICES\\PrintSpoolerService, NT SERVICE\\WdiServiceHost\n"},{"rule_version":"WN11-UR-000010","ccis":["CCI-000213"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id":"SV-253480r1137691","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253480r1137691_rule","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any groups or accounts other than the following are granted the \"Access this computer from the network\" user right, this is a finding:\n\nAdministrators\nRemote Desktop Users\n\nIf a domain application account such as for a management tool requires this user right, this would not be a finding.\n\nVendor documentation must support the requirement for having the user right.\n\nThe requirement must be documented with the ISSO.\n\nThe application account, managed at the domain level, must meet requirements for application account passwords, such as length and frequency of changes as defined in the Windows Server STIGs.","ia_controls":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253480","title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048"},"reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; \"Access this computer from the network\" to only include the following groups or accounts:\n\nAdministrators  \nRemote Desktop Users","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253480","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253480","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253480","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"uuid":"3675E224-6BF8-1014-AFF6-9880E67F8EEC","status":"not_a_finding","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (The 'Access this computer from the network' user right is only assigned to the Administrators and Remote Desktop Users groups.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25348000 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The 'Access this computer from the network' user right is only assigned to the Administrators and Remote Desktop Users groups.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000010 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : Administrators, Remote Desktop Users\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'Administrators'\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'Remote Desktop Users'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25348000 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'senetworklogonright' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : senetworklogonright equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : senetworklogonright equals '0' for: ENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS, WKS1-SOTERIA\\Degthat, Window Manager\\Window Manager Group, NT SERVICE\\ALL SERVICES, Power Users, CREATOR GROUP SERVER, SERVICE, Guests, Access Control Assistance Operators, NT SERVICE\\WdiServiceHost, NETWORK, DIALUP, CREATOR OWNER SERVER, ANONYMOUS LOGON, WDAGUtilityAccount, RESTRICTED SERVICES\\ALL RESTRICTED SERVICES, CREATOR OWNER, Performance Log Users, RESTRICTED SERVICES\\PrintSpoolerService, Cryptographic Operators, INTERACTIVE, Replicator, LOCAL SERVICE, NT SERVICE\\autotimesvc, Everyone, Network Configuration Operators, Visitor, PROXY, IUSR, User Mode Hardware Operators, Authenticated Users, DefaultAccount, BATCH, Distributed COM Users, NETWORK SERVICE, Remote Management Users, Hyper-V Administrators, Device Owners, Users, TERMINAL SERVER USER, Performance Monitor Users, IIS_IUSRS, OpenSSH Users, CREATOR GROUP, Event Log Readers, System Managed Accounts Group, SYSTEM, Backup Operators, X_Admin\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","mitigations":"","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nAccounts with the \"Access this computer from the network\" user right may access resources on the system, and must be limited to those that require it.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The \"Access this computer from the network\" user right must only be assigned to the Administrators and Remote Desktop Users groups."},{"group_tree":{"id":"V-253481","title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125"},"third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","rule_id":"SV-253481r958726","mitigation_control":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id_src":"SV-253481r958726_rule","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any groups or accounts (to include administrators), are granted the \"Act as part of the operating system\" user right, this is a finding.","ia_controls":"","ccis":["CCI-002235"],"severity":"high","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","rule_version":"WN11-UR-000015","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The \"Act as part of the operating system\" user right must not be assigned to any groups or accounts.","mitigations":"","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nAccounts with the \"Act as part of the operating system\" user right can assume the identity of any user and gain access to resources that user is authorized to access. Any accounts with this right can take complete control of a system.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     tru