\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : secreateglobalprivilege equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : secreateglobalprivilege equals '0' for: Window Manager\\Window Manager Group, ENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS, WKS1-SOTERIA\\Degthat, CREATOR GROUP SERVER, Power Users, NT SERVICE\\ALL SERVICES, Guests, Access Control Assistance Operators, NETWORK, NT SERVICE\\WdiServiceHost, DIALUP, CREATOR OWNER SERVER, CREATOR OWNER, RESTRICTED SERVICES\\ALL RESTRICTED SERVICES, ANONYMOUS LOGON, WDAGUtilityAccount, Performance Log Users, RESTRICTED SERVICES\\PrintSpoolerService, Cryptographic Operators, INTERACTIVE, Replicator, NT SERVICE\\autotimesvc, PROXY, Visitor, Network Configuration Operators, Everyone, User Mode Hardware Operators, IUSR, DefaultAccount, Authenticated Users, BATCH, Distributed COM Users, Remote Management Users, Hyper-V Administrators, Device Owners, Users, Performance Monitor Users, TERMINAL SERVER USER, IIS_IUSRS, OpenSSH Users, CREATOR GROUP, Event Log Readers, SYSTEM, System Managed Accounts Group, Backup Operators, Remote Desktop Users, X_Admin\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nAccounts with the \"Create global objects\" user right can create objects that are available to all sessions, which could affect processes in other users' sessions.","mitigations":"","rule_title":"The \"Create global objects\" user right must only be assigned to Administrators, Service, Local Service, and Network Service.","security_override_guidance":""},{"uuid":"36763C30-6BF8-1014-8095-8174AB758569","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253488"},"status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; \"Create permanent shared objects\" to be defined but containing no entries (blank).","group_id":"V-253488","potential_impacts":"","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253488","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The \"Create permanent shared objects\" user right must not be assigned to any groups or accounts.","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nAccounts with the \"Create permanent shared objects\" user right could expose sensitive data by creating shared objects.","mitigations":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (No groups or accounts are granted the 'Create permanent shared objects' user right.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25348800 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : No groups or accounts are granted the 'Create permanent shared objects' user right.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000008 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : All security principles\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'security_principle' must match the pattern '.+'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25348800 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'secreatepermanentprivilege' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : secreatepermanentprivilege equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : secreatepermanentprivilege equals '0' for: Access Control Assistance Operators, Administrators, Backup Operators, Cryptographic Operators, Device Owners, Distributed COM Users, Event Log Readers, Guests, Hyper-V Administrators, IIS_IUSRS, Network Configuration Operators, OpenSSH Users, Performance Log Users, Performance Monitor Users, Power Users, Remote Desktop Users, Remote Management Users, Replicator, System Managed Accounts Group, User Mode Hardware Operators, Users, DefaultAccount, WKS1-SOTERIA\\Degthat, Visitor, WDAGUtilityAccount, X_Admin, NETWORK SERVICE, LOCAL SERVICE, SYSTEM, IUSR, TERMINAL SERVER USER, Authenticated Users, ENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS, PROXY, ANONYMOUS LOGON, SERVICE, INTERACTIVE, BATCH, NETWORK, DIALUP, CREATOR GROUP SERVER, CREATOR OWNER SERVER, CREATOR GROUP, CREATOR OWNER, Everyone, Window Manager\\Window Manager Group, RESTRICTED SERVICES\\ALL RESTRICTED SERVICES, NT SERVICE\\autotimesvc, NT SERVICE\\ALL SERVICES, RESTRICTED SERVICES\\PrintSpoolerService, NT SERVICE\\WdiServiceHost\n","ccis":["CCI-002235"],"group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","severity":"medium","rule_version":"WN11-UR-000055","responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","id":"V-253488"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253488r958726","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"ia_controls":"","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any groups or accounts are granted the \"Create permanent shared objects\" user right, this is a finding.","rule_id_src":"SV-253488r958726_rule"},{"rule_id_src":"SV-253489r958726_rule","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any groups or accounts other than the following are granted the \"Create symbolic links\" user right, this is a finding:\n\nAdministrators\n\nIf the workstation has an approved use of Hyper-V, such as being used as a dedicated admin workstation using Hyper-V to separate administration and standard user functions, \"NT VIRTUAL MACHINES\\VIRTUAL MACHINE\" may be assigned this user right and is not a finding.","ia_controls":"","rule_id":"SV-253489r958726","mitigation_control":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"id":"V-253489","title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125"},"reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","rule_version":"WN11-UR-000060","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","ccis":["CCI-002235"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Create symbolic links - Administrators)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25348900 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Create symbolic links - Administrators\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000009 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : Administrators\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'Administrators'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25348900 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Create symbolic links\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'secreatesymboliclinkprivilege' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : secreatesymboliclinkprivilege equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : secreatesymboliclinkprivilege equals '0' for: BATCH, Distributed COM Users, Remote Management Users, NETWORK SERVICE, Hyper-V Administrators, Device Owners, NT SERVICE\\autotimesvc, Everyone, Visitor, Network Configuration Operators, PROXY, Authenticated Users, DefaultAccount, IUSR, User Mode Hardware Operators, SYSTEM, Event Log Readers, System Managed Accounts Group, Backup Operators, Remote Desktop Users, X_Admin, TERMINAL SERVER USER, Users, Performance Monitor Users, OpenSSH Users, IIS_IUSRS, CREATOR GROUP, SERVICE, Guests, Access Control Assistance Operators, NT SERVICE\\WdiServiceHost, NETWORK, WKS1-SOTERIA\\Degthat, ENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS, Window Manager\\Window Manager Group, Power Users, NT SERVICE\\ALL SERVICES, CREATOR GROUP SERVER, Cryptographic Operators, RESTRICTED SERVICES\\PrintSpoolerService, INTERACTIVE, Replicator, LOCAL SERVICE, CREATOR OWNER SERVER, DIALUP, WDAGUtilityAccount, RESTRICTED SERVICES\\ALL RESTRICTED SERVICES, ANONYMOUS LOGON, CREATOR OWNER, Performance Log Users\n","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The \"Create symbolic links\" user right must only be assigned to the Administrators group.","mitigations":"","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nAccounts with the \"Create symbolic links\" user right can create pointers to other objects, which could potentially expose the system to attack.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","group_id":"V-253489","potential_impacts":"","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253489","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; \"Create symbolic links\" to only include the following groups or accounts:\n\nAdministrators","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"367643A0-6BF8-1014-AC35-BEF556F99495","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253489","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"}},{"rule_id_src":"SV-253490r958726_rule","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any groups or accounts other than the following are granted the \"Debug Programs\" user right, this is a finding:\n\nAdministrators","ia_controls":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id":"SV-253490r958726","mitigation_control":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","id":"V-253490"},"third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","rule_version":"WN11-UR-000065","severity":"high","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","ccis":["CCI-002235"],"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Debug Programs - Administrators)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25349000 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Debug Programs - Administrators\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000009 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : Administrators\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'Administrators'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25349000 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Debug programs\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'sedebugprivilege' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : sedebugprivilege equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : sedebugprivilege equals '0' for: BATCH, Distributed COM Users, Remote Management Users, NETWORK SERVICE, Hyper-V Administrators, Device Owners, NT SERVICE\\autotimesvc, Everyone, Visitor, Network Configuration Operators, PROXY, Authenticated Users, DefaultAccount, IUSR, User Mode Hardware Operators, SYSTEM, Event Log Readers, System Managed Accounts Group, Backup Operators, Remote Desktop Users, X_Admin, TERMINAL SERVER USER, Users, Performance Monitor Users, OpenSSH Users, IIS_IUSRS, CREATOR GROUP, SERVICE, Guests, Access Control Assistance Operators, NT SERVICE\\WdiServiceHost, NETWORK, WKS1-SOTERIA\\Degthat, ENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS, Window Manager\\Window Manager Group, Power Users, NT SERVICE\\ALL SERVICES, CREATOR GROUP SERVER, Cryptographic Operators, RESTRICTED SERVICES\\PrintSpoolerService, INTERACTIVE, Replicator, LOCAL SERVICE, CREATOR OWNER SERVER, DIALUP, WDAGUtilityAccount, RESTRICTED SERVICES\\ALL RESTRICTED SERVICES, ANONYMOUS LOGON, CREATOR OWNER, Performance Log Users\n","mitigations":"","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nAccounts with the \"Debug Programs\" user right can attach a debugger to any process or to the kernel, providing complete access to sensitive and critical operating system components. This right is given to Administrators in the default configuration.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The \"Debug programs\" user right must only be assigned to the Administrators group.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","group_id_src":"V-253490","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253490","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; \"Debug programs\" to only include the following groups or accounts:\n\nAdministrators","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253490"},"uuid":"3676707A-6BF8-1014-8891-DA43DFCE1F60"},{"group_id_src":"V-253491","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id":"V-253491","potential_impacts":"","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; \"Deny access to this computer from the network\" to include the following:\n\nDomain Systems Only:\nEnterprise Admins group\nDomain Admins group\nLocal account (see Note below)\n\nAll Systems:\nGuests group\n\nPrivileged Access Workstations (PAWs) dedicated to the management of Active Directory are exempt from denying the Enterprise Admins and Domain Admins groups. (See the Windows Privileged Access Workstation STIG for PAW requirements.)\n\nNote: \"Local account\" is a built-in security group used to assign user rights and permissions to all local accounts.","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253491"},"uuid":"36767A32-6BF8-1014-9FF6-F31E7F5C5A53","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :     true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nCriteria                :       false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :         false (Deny access to this computer from the network - Domain Admins)\nTest                    :         false (Deny access to this computer from the network - Enterprise Admins)\nTest                    :         false (Deny access to this computer from the network - Local account)\nCriteria                :         false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :           false (The system is a Windows Domain Member Workstation)\nCriteria                :       true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :         true (The system is a Windows Standalone Workstation)\nTest                    :     true (Deny access to this computer from the network - Guests)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25349101 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Deny access to this computer from the network - Domain Admins\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : At least one collected item must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000003 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'security_principle' must match the pattern '^(?i)(.+\\\\)?Domain Admins$'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25349100 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Deny access to this computer from the network\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'sedenynetworklogonright' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\nCollected Item Property : sedenynetworklogonright equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : sedenynetworklogonright equals '0' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25349102 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Deny access to this computer from the network - Enterprise Admins\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : At least one collected item must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000004 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'security_principle' must match the pattern '^(?i)(.+\\\\)?Enterprise Admins$'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25349100 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Deny access to this computer from the network\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'sedenynetworklogonright' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\nCollected Item Property : sedenynetworklogonright equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : sedenynetworklogonright equals '0' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25349103 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Deny access to this computer from the network - Local account\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000007 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'security_principle' must match the pattern '^(?i)(NT AUTHORITY\\\\)?Local account$'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25349100 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Deny access to this computer from the network\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'sedenynetworklogonright' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\nCollected Item Property : sedenynetworklogonright equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : sedenynetworklogonright equals '0' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:10000200 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : The system is a Windows Domain Member Workstation\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:10000100 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT DomainRole FROM win32_computersystem'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:10000200 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : Domain Member Workstation\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all domainrole must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT DomainRole FROM win32_computersystem'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : domainrole = '0'\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:10000100 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The system is a Windows Standalone Workstation\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:10000100 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT DomainRole FROM win32_computersystem'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:10000100 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : Standalone Workstation\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all domainrole must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT DomainRole FROM win32_computersystem'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : domainrole = '0'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25349100 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Deny access to this computer from the network - Guests\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000006 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'security_principle' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'Guests'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25349100 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Deny access to this computer from the network\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'sedenynetworklogonright' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : sedenynetworklogonright equals '1' for: Guests\nCollected Item Property : sedenynetworklogonright equals '0' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\n","mitigations":"","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nThe \"Deny access to this computer from the network\" right defines the accounts that are prevented from logging on from the network.\n\nIn an Active Directory Domain, denying logons to the Enterprise Admins and Domain Admins groups on lower trust systems helps mitigate the risk of privilege escalation from credential theft attacks, which could lead to the compromise of an entire domain.\n\nLocal accounts on domain-joined systems must also be assigned this right to decrease the risk of lateral movement resulting from credential theft attacks.\n\nThe Guests group must be assigned this right to prevent unauthenticated access.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The \"Deny access to this computer from the network\" user right on workstations must be configured to prevent access from highly privileged domain accounts and local accounts on domain systems and unauthenticated access on all systems.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","rule_version":"WN11-UR-000070","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048","ccis":["CCI-000213"],"rule_id_src":"SV-253491r1137691_rule","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf the following groups or accounts are not defined for the \"Deny access to this computer from the network\" right, this is a finding:\n\nDomain Systems Only:\nEnterprise Admins group\nDomain Admins group\nLocal account (see Note below)\n\nAll Systems:\nGuests group\n\nPrivileged Access Workstations (PAWs) dedicated to the management of Active Directory are exempt from denying the Enterprise Admins and Domain Admins groups. (See the Windows Privileged Access Workstation STIG for PAW requirements.)\n\nNote: \"Local account\" is a built-in security group used to assign user rights and permissions to all local accounts.","ia_controls":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id":"SV-253491r1137691","mitigation_control":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048","id":"V-253491"},"reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":""},{"mitigations":"","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nThe \"Deny log on as a batch job\" right defines accounts that are prevented from logging on to the system as a batch job, such as Task Scheduler.\n\nIn an Active Directory Domain, denying logons to the Enterprise Admins and Domain Admins groups on lower trust systems helps mitigate the risk of privilege escalation from credential theft attacks which could lead to the compromise of an entire domain.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The \"Deny log on as a batch job\" user right on domain-joined workstations must be configured to prevent access from highly privileged domain accounts.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","status":"not_applicable","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253492"},"uuid":"367681E3-6BF8-1014-B5CA-AFB654D036B1","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253492","group_id":"V-253492","potential_impacts":"","fix_text":"This requirement is applicable to domain-joined systems, for standalone systems this is NA.\n\nConfigure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; \"Deny log on as a batch job\" to include the following:\n\nDomain Systems Only:\nEnterprise Admin Group\nDomain Admin Group","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"id":"V-253492","title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048"},"reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253492r1137691_rule","check_content":"This requirement is applicable to domain-joined systems, for standalone systems this is NA.\n\nVerify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf the following groups or accounts are not defined for the \"Deny log on as a batch job\" right, this is a finding:\n\nDomain Systems Only:\nEnterprise Admin Group\nDomain Admin Group","ia_controls":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id":"SV-253492r1137691","mitigation_control":"","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048","ccis":["CCI-000213"],"rule_version":"WN11-UR-000075"},{"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253493"},"uuid":"367688ED-6BF8-1014-BBF4-88224403AB92","status":"not_applicable","fix_text":"This requirement is applicable to domain-joined systems, for standalone systems this is NA.\n\nConfigure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; \"Deny log on as a service\" to include the following:\n\nDomain Systems Only:\nEnterprise Admins Group\nDomain Admins Group","group_id_src":"V-253493","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id":"V-253493","potential_impacts":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nThe \"Deny log on as a service\" right defines accounts that are denied log on as a service.\n\nIn an Active Directory Domain, denying logons to the Enterprise Admins and Domain Admins groups on lower trust systems helps mitigate the risk of privilege escalation from credential theft attacks which could lead to the compromise of an entire domain.\n\nIncorrect configurations could prevent services from starting and result in a DoS.","mitigations":"","rule_title":"The \"Deny log on as a service\" user right on Windows 11 domain-joined workstations must be configured to prevent access from highly privileged domain accounts.","security_override_guidance":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","ccis":["CCI-000213"],"group_title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048","severity":"medium","rule_version":"WN11-UR-000080","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253493","title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253493r1137691","check_content":"This requirement is applicable to domain-joined systems, for standalone systems this is NA.\n\nVerify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf the following groups or accounts are not defined for the \"Deny log on as a service\" right , this is a finding:\n\nDomain Systems Only:\nEnterprise Admins Group\nDomain Admins Group","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253493r1137691_rule"},{"group_id":"V-253494","potential_impacts":"","group_id_src":"V-253494","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; \"Deny log on locally\" to include the following:\n\nDomain Systems Only:\nEnterprise Admins Group\nDomain Admins Group\n\nPrivileged Access Workstations (PAWs) dedicated to the management of Active Directory are exempt from denying the Enterprise Admins and Domain Admins groups. (See the Windows Privileged Access Workstation STIG for PAW requirements.)\n\nAll Systems:\nGuests Group","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"3676909A-6BF8-1014-BF74-B83569B8AACD","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253494","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :     true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nCriteria                :       false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :         false (Deny log on locally - Domain Admins)\nTest                    :         false (Deny log on as a locally - Enterprise Admins)\nTest                    :       true (System is not a member of a domain)\nTest                    :     true (Deny log on locally - Guests)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25349402 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Deny log on locally - Domain Admins\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : At least one collected item must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000003 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'security_principle' must match the pattern '^(?i)(.+\\\\)?Domain Admins$'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25349400 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Deny log on locally\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'sedenyinteractivelogonright' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\nCollected Item Property : sedenyinteractivelogonright equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : sedenyinteractivelogonright equals '0' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25349403 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Deny log on as a locally - Enterprise Admins\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : At least one collected item must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000004 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'security_principle' must match the pattern '^(?i)(.+\\\\)?Enterprise Admins$'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25349400 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Deny log on locally\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'sedenyinteractivelogonright' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\nCollected Item Property : sedenyinteractivelogonright equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : sedenyinteractivelogonright equals '0' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25349401 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : System is not a member of a domain\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\nState Operator          : One or more item-state comparisons may be true.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:10000100 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT DomainRole FROM win32_computersystem'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:10000100 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : Standalone Workstation\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all domainrole must be equal to '0'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:10000300 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : Standalone Server\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all domainrole must be equal to '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT DomainRole FROM win32_computersystem'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : domainrole = '0'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25349400 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Deny log on locally - Guests\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000006 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'security_principle' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'Guests'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25349400 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Deny log on locally\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'sedenyinteractivelogonright' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : sedenyinteractivelogonright equals '1' for: Guests\nCollected Item Property : sedenyinteractivelogonright equals '0' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\n","rule_title":"The \"Deny log on locally\" user right on workstations must be configured to prevent access from highly privileged domain accounts on domain systems and unauthenticated access on all systems.","security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nThe \"Deny log on locally\" right defines accounts that are prevented from logging on interactively.\n\nIn an Active Directory Domain, denying logons to the Enterprise Admins and Domain Admins groups on lower trust systems helps mitigate the risk of privilege escalation from credential theft attacks, which could lead to the compromise of an entire domain.\n\nThe Guests group must be assigned this right to prevent unauthenticated access.","mitigations":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","rule_version":"WN11-UR-000085","group_title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-000213"],"ia_controls":"","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf the following groups or accounts are not defined for the \"Deny log on locally\" right, this is a finding.\n\nDomain Systems Only:\nEnterprise Admins Group\nDomain Admins Group\n\nPrivileged Access Workstations (PAWs) dedicated to the management of Active Directory are exempt from denying the Enterprise Admins and Domain Admins groups. (See the Windows Privileged Access Workstation STIG for PAW requirements.)\n\nAll Systems:\nGuests Group","rule_id_src":"SV-253494r1137691_rule","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253494r1137691","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253494","title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048"}},{"stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The \"Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services\" user right on Windows 11 workstations must be configured to prevent access from highly privileged domain accounts and local accounts on domain systems and unauthenticated access on all systems.","mitigations":"","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nThe \"Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services\" right defines the accounts that are prevented from logging on using Remote Desktop Services.\n\nIf Remote Desktop Services is not used by the organization, the Everyone group must be assigned this right to prevent all access.\n\nIn an Active Directory Domain, denying logons to the Enterprise Admins and Domain Admins groups on lower trust systems helps mitigate the risk of privilege escalation from credential theft attacks, which could lead to the compromise of an entire domain.\n\nLocal accounts on domain-joined systems must also be assigned this right to decrease the risk of lateral movement resulting from credential theft attacks.\n\nThe Guests group must be assigned this right to prevent unauthenticated access.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nCriteria                :     true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :       true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nCriteria                :         false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :           false (Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services - Domain Admins)\nTest                    :           false (Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services - Enterprise Admins)\nTest                    :           false (Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services - Local account)\nTest                    :           false (System is a Windows non-DC domain-joined system)\nTest                    :         true (The system is a Windows Standalone Workstation or Server)\nTest                    :       true (Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services - Guests)\nTest                    :     false (Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services - Everyone)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25349501 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services - Domain Admins\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : At least one collected item must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000003 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'security_principle' must match the pattern '^(?i)(.+\\\\)?Domain Admins$'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25349500 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'sedenyremoteInteractivelogonright' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\nCollected Item Property : sedenyremoteInteractivelogonright equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : sedenyremoteInteractivelogonright equals '0' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25349502 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services - Enterprise Admins\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : At least one collected item must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000004 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'security_principle' must match the pattern '^(?i)(.+\\\\)?Enterprise Admins$'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25349500 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'sedenyremoteInteractivelogonright' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\nCollected Item Property : sedenyremoteInteractivelogonright equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : sedenyremoteInteractivelogonright equals '0' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25349503 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services - Local account\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000007 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'security_principle' must match the pattern '^(?i)(NT AUTHORITY\\\\)?Local account$'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25349500 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'sedenyremoteInteractivelogonright' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\nCollected Item Property : sedenyremoteInteractivelogonright equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : sedenyremoteInteractivelogonright equals '0' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25349504 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : System is a Windows non-DC domain-joined system\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\nState Operator          : One or more item-state comparisons may be true.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:10000100 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT DomainRole FROM win32_computersystem'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:10000200 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : Domain Member Workstation\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all domainrole must be equal to '1'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:10000400 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : Domain Member Server\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all domainrole must be equal to '3'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT DomainRole FROM win32_computersystem'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : domainrole = '0'\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25339402 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The system is a Windows Standalone Workstation or Server\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\nState Operator          : One or more item-state comparisons may be true.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:10000100 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT DomainRole FROM win32_computersystem'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:10000100 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : Standalone Workstation\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all domainrole must be equal to '0'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:10000300 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : Standalone Server\nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : all domainrole must be equal to '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT DomainRole FROM win32_computersystem'\n                        : collected 'result' result: \n                        : domainrole = '0'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25349500 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services - Guests\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000006 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'security_principle' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'Guests'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25349500 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'sedenyremoteInteractivelogonright' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : sedenyremoteInteractivelogonright equals '1' for: Guests\nCollected Item Property : sedenyremoteInteractivelogonright equals '0' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25349505 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services - Everyone\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000005 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'security_principle' must be equal (case insensitive) to 'Everyone'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25349500 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'sedenyremoteInteractivelogonright' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\nCollected Item Property : sedenyremoteInteractivelogonright equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : sedenyremoteInteractivelogonright equals '0' for: Everyone\n\n","uuid":"36769981-6BF8-1014-AC2D-9698918DD638","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253495","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; \"Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services\" to include the following:\n\nIf Remote Desktop Services is not used by the organization, assign the Everyone group this right to prevent all access.\n\nDomain Systems Only:\nEnterprise Admins group\nDomain Admins group\nLocal account (see Note below)\n\nAll Systems:\nGuests group\n\nPrivileged Access Workstations (PAWs) dedicated to the management of Active Directory are exempt from denying the Enterprise Admins and Domain Admins groups. (See the Windows Privileged Access Workstation STIG for PAW requirements.)\n\nNote: \"Local account\" is a built-in security group used to assign user rights and permissions to all local accounts.","group_id":"V-253495","potential_impacts":"","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253495","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048","id":"V-253495"},"third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","rule_id":"SV-253495r1137691","mitigation_control":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id_src":"SV-253495r1137691_rule","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf the following groups or accounts are not defined for the \"Deny log on through Remote Desktop Services\" right, this is a finding:\n\nIf Remote Desktop Services is not used by the organization, the \"Everyone\" group can replace all of the groups listed below.\n\nDomain Systems Only:\nEnterprise Admins group\nDomain Admins group\nLocal account (see Note below)\n\nAll Systems:\nGuests group\n\nPrivileged Access Workstations (PAWs) dedicated to the management of Active Directory are exempt from denying the Enterprise Admins and Domain Admins groups. (See the Windows Privileged Access Workstation STIG for PAW requirements.)\n\nNote: \"Local account\" is a built-in security group used to assign user rights and permissions to all local accounts.","ia_controls":"","ccis":["CCI-000213","CCI-002314"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000080-GPOS-00048","rule_version":"WN11-UR-000090"},{"rule_version":"WN11-UR-000095","ccis":["CCI-002235"],"group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","severity":"medium","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253496r958726","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any groups or accounts are granted the \"Enable computer and user accounts to be trusted for delegation\" user right, this is a finding.","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253496r958726_rule","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253496","title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; \"Enable computer and user accounts to be trusted for delegation\" to be defined but containing no entries (blank).","group_id":"V-253496","potential_impacts":"","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253496","uuid":"3676A166-6BF8-1014-94C3-C6EE3D489829","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253496","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"status":"not_a_finding","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Enable computer and user accounts to be trusted for delegation - None)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25349600 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Enable computer and user accounts to be trusted for delegation - None\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000008 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : All security principles\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'security_principle' must match the pattern '.+'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25349600 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Enable computer and user accounts to be trusted for delegation\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'seenabledelegationprivilege' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : seenabledelegationprivilege equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : seenabledelegationprivilege equals '0' for: Access Control Assistance Operators, Administrators, Backup Operators, Cryptographic Operators, Device Owners, Distributed COM Users, Event Log Readers, Guests, Hyper-V Administrators, IIS_IUSRS, Network Configuration Operators, OpenSSH Users, Performance Log Users, Performance Monitor Users, Power Users, Remote Desktop Users, Remote Management Users, Replicator, System Managed Accounts Group, User Mode Hardware Operators, Users, DefaultAccount, WKS1-SOTERIA\\Degthat, Visitor, WDAGUtilityAccount, X_Admin, NETWORK SERVICE, LOCAL SERVICE, SYSTEM, IUSR, TERMINAL SERVER USER, Authenticated Users, ENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS, PROXY, ANONYMOUS LOGON, SERVICE, INTERACTIVE, BATCH, NETWORK, DIALUP, CREATOR GROUP SERVER, CREATOR OWNER SERVER, CREATOR GROUP, CREATOR OWNER, Everyone, Window Manager\\Window Manager Group, RESTRICTED SERVICES\\ALL RESTRICTED SERVICES, NT SERVICE\\autotimesvc, NT SERVICE\\ALL SERVICES, RESTRICTED SERVICES\\PrintSpoolerService, NT SERVICE\\WdiServiceHost\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The \"Enable computer and user accounts to be trusted for delegation\" user right must not be assigned to any groups or accounts.","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nThe \"Enable computer and user accounts to be trusted for delegation\" user right allows the \"Trusted for Delegation\" setting to be changed. This could potentially allow unauthorized users to impersonate other users.","mitigations":""},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Force shutdown from a remote system - Administrators)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25349700 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Force shutdown from a remote system - Administrators\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000009 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : Administrators\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'Administrators'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25349700 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Force shutdown from a remote system\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'seremoteshutdownprivilege' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : seremoteshutdownprivilege equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : seremoteshutdownprivilege equals '0' for: BATCH, Distributed COM Users, Remote Management Users, NETWORK SERVICE, Hyper-V Administrators, Device Owners, NT SERVICE\\autotimesvc, Everyone, Visitor, Network Configuration Operators, PROXY, Authenticated Users, DefaultAccount, IUSR, User Mode Hardware Operators, SYSTEM, Event Log Readers, System Managed Accounts Group, Backup Operators, Remote Desktop Users, X_Admin, TERMINAL SERVER USER, Users, Performance Monitor Users, OpenSSH Users, IIS_IUSRS, CREATOR GROUP, SERVICE, Guests, Access Control Assistance Operators, NT SERVICE\\WdiServiceHost, NETWORK, WKS1-SOTERIA\\Degthat, ENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS, Window Manager\\Window Manager Group, Power Users, NT SERVICE\\ALL SERVICES, CREATOR GROUP SERVER, Cryptographic Operators, RESTRICTED SERVICES\\PrintSpoolerService, INTERACTIVE, Replicator, LOCAL SERVICE, CREATOR OWNER SERVER, DIALUP, WDAGUtilityAccount, RESTRICTED SERVICES\\ALL RESTRICTED SERVICES, ANONYMOUS LOGON, CREATOR OWNER, Performance Log Users\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The \"Force shutdown from a remote system\" user right must only be assigned to the Administrators group.","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nAccounts with the \"Force shutdown from a remote system\" user right can remotely shut down a system which could result in a DoS.","mitigations":"","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; \"Force shutdown from a remote system\" to only include the following groups or accounts:\n\nAdministrators","group_id":"V-253497","potential_impacts":"","group_id_src":"V-253497","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","uuid":"3676A8DB-6BF8-1014-916F-A26BF3A09DC6","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253497"},"status":"not_a_finding","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253497r958726","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any groups or accounts other than the following are granted the \"Force shutdown from a remote system\" user right, this is a finding:\n\nAdministrators","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253497r958726_rule","third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253497","title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","rule_version":"WN11-UR-000100","ccis":["CCI-002235"],"group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","severity":"medium"},{"false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253498","group_id":"V-253498","potential_impacts":"","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; \"Impersonate a client after authentication\" to only include the following groups or accounts:\n\nAdministrators\nLOCAL SERVICE\nNETWORK SERVICE\nRESTRICTED SERVICES\\PrintSpoolerService\nSERVICE","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253498","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"uuid":"3676AFF2-6BF8-1014-B014-D65AF5F0B8C9","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (No groups or accounts are granted the 'Impersonate a client after authentication' user right.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25349800 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : No groups or accounts are granted the 'Impersonate a client after authentication' user right.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25349800 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : Administrators, Local Service, Network Service, Service,Restricted Services/PrintSpoolerService\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'Administrators'\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'LOCAL SERVICE'\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'NETWORK SERVICE'\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'SERVICE'\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'Restricted Services\\PrintSpoolerService'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25349800 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'seimpersonateprivilege' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : seimpersonateprivilege equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : seimpersonateprivilege equals '0' for: Remote Management Users, Hyper-V Administrators, Device Owners, BATCH, Distributed COM Users, Everyone, Visitor, PROXY, Network Configuration Operators, User Mode Hardware Operators, IUSR, DefaultAccount, Authenticated Users, NT SERVICE\\autotimesvc, Backup Operators, Remote Desktop Users, X_Admin, System Managed Accounts Group, Event Log Readers, SYSTEM, CREATOR GROUP, Users, Performance Monitor Users, TERMINAL SERVER USER, IIS_IUSRS, OpenSSH Users, Access Control Assistance Operators, NT SERVICE\\WdiServiceHost, NETWORK, Guests, NT SERVICE\\ALL SERVICES, Power Users, CREATOR GROUP SERVER, ENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS, WKS1-SOTERIA\\Degthat, Window Manager\\Window Manager Group, Replicator, Cryptographic Operators, INTERACTIVE, Performance Log Users, DIALUP, CREATOR OWNER SERVER, WDAGUtilityAccount, ANONYMOUS LOGON, RESTRICTED SERVICES\\ALL RESTRICTED SERVICES, CREATOR OWNER\n","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nThe \"Impersonate a client after authentication\" user right allows a program to impersonate another user or account to run on their behalf. An attacker could potentially use this to elevate privileges.","mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The \"Impersonate a client after authentication\" user right must only be assigned to Administrators, Service, Local Service, and Network Service.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","rule_version":"WN11-UR-000110","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-002235"],"check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\n\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any groups or accounts other than the following are granted the \"Impersonate a client after authentication\" user right, this is a finding:\n\nAdministrators\nLOCAL SERVICE\nNETWORK SERVICE\nRESTRICTED SERVICES\\PrintSpoolerService\nSERVICE","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253498r1138526_rule","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253498r1138526","weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-253498","title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125"}},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Load and unload device drivers - Administrators)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25349900 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Load and unload device drivers - Administrators\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000009 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : Administrators\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'Administrators'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25349900 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Load and unload device drivers\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'seloaddriverprivilege' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : seloaddriverprivilege equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : seloaddriverprivilege equals '0' for: BATCH, Distributed COM Users, Remote Management Users, NETWORK SERVICE, Hyper-V Administrators, Device Owners, NT SERVICE\\autotimesvc, Everyone, Visitor, Network Configuration Operators, PROXY, Authenticated Users, DefaultAccount, IUSR, User Mode Hardware Operators, SYSTEM, Event Log Readers, System Managed Accounts Group, Backup Operators, Remote Desktop Users, X_Admin, TERMINAL SERVER USER, Users, Performance Monitor Users, OpenSSH Users, IIS_IUSRS, CREATOR GROUP, SERVICE, Guests, Access Control Assistance Operators, NT SERVICE\\WdiServiceHost, NETWORK, WKS1-SOTERIA\\Degthat, ENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS, Window Manager\\Window Manager Group, Power Users, NT SERVICE\\ALL SERVICES, CREATOR GROUP SERVER, Cryptographic Operators, RESTRICTED SERVICES\\PrintSpoolerService, INTERACTIVE, Replicator, LOCAL SERVICE, CREATOR OWNER SERVER, DIALUP, WDAGUtilityAccount, RESTRICTED SERVICES\\ALL RESTRICTED SERVICES, ANONYMOUS LOGON, CREATOR OWNER, Performance Log Users\n","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nThe \"Load and unload device drivers\" user right allows device drivers to dynamically be loaded on a system by a user. This could potentially be used to install malicious code by an attacker.","mitigations":"","rule_title":"The \"Load and unload device drivers\" user right must only be assigned to the Administrators group.","security_override_guidance":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-253499","group_id":"V-253499","potential_impacts":"","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; \"Load and unload device drivers\" to only include the following groups or accounts:\n\nAdministrators","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253499"},"uuid":"3676BA5E-6BF8-1014-AE5B-D4C92D40ED0C","ia_controls":"","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any groups or accounts other than the following are granted the \"Load and unload device drivers\" user right, this is a finding:\n\nAdministrators","rule_id_src":"SV-253499r958726_rule","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253499r958726","weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","id":"V-253499"},"rule_version":"WN11-UR-000120","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-002235"]},{"rule_version":"WN11-UR-000125","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","ccis":["CCI-002235"],"rule_id_src":"SV-253500r958726_rule","ia_controls":"","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any groups or accounts are granted the \"Lock pages in memory\" user right, this is a finding.","rule_id":"SV-253500r958726","mitigation_control":"","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"id":"V-253500","title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125"},"responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253500","group_id_src":"V-253500","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; \"Lock pages in memory\" to be defined but containing no entries (blank).","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"3676C054-6BF8-1014-9C52-B2E42CDE85BC","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253500","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8