N CONTROLLERS, PROXY, ANONYMOUS LOGON, SERVICE, INTERACTIVE, BATCH, NETWORK, DIALUP, CREATOR GROUP SERVER, CREATOR OWNER SERVER, CREATOR GROUP, CREATOR OWNER, Everyone, Window Manager\\Window Manager Group, RESTRICTED SERVICES\\ALL RESTRICTED SERVICES, NT SERVICE\\autotimesvc, NT SERVICE\\ALL SERVICES, RESTRICTED SERVICES\\PrintSpoolerService, NT SERVICE\\WdiServiceHost\n","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The \"Lock pages in memory\" user right must not be assigned to any groups or accounts.","mitigations":"","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nThe \"Lock pages in memory\" user right allows physical memory to be assigned to processes, which could cause performance issues or a DoS.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4"},{"fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; \"Manage auditing and security log\" to only include the following groups or accounts:\n\nAdministrators","group_id_src":"V-253501","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253501","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253501"},"uuid":"3676C557-6BF8-1014-B1BC-B7E4FAC6B830","status":"not_a_finding","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (The 'Manage auditing and security log' user right is only assigned to the Administrators group.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25350100 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : The 'Manage auditing and security log' user right is only assigned to the Administrators group.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000009 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : Administrators\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'Administrators'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25350100 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'sesecurityprivilege' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : sesecurityprivilege equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : sesecurityprivilege equals '0' for: BATCH, Distributed COM Users, Remote Management Users, NETWORK SERVICE, Hyper-V Administrators, Device Owners, NT SERVICE\\autotimesvc, Everyone, Visitor, Network Configuration Operators, PROXY, Authenticated Users, DefaultAccount, IUSR, User Mode Hardware Operators, SYSTEM, Event Log Readers, System Managed Accounts Group, Backup Operators, Remote Desktop Users, X_Admin, TERMINAL SERVER USER, Users, Performance Monitor Users, OpenSSH Users, IIS_IUSRS, CREATOR GROUP, SERVICE, Guests, Access Control Assistance Operators, NT SERVICE\\WdiServiceHost, NETWORK, WKS1-SOTERIA\\Degthat, ENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS, Window Manager\\Window Manager Group, Power Users, NT SERVICE\\ALL SERVICES, CREATOR GROUP SERVER, Cryptographic Operators, RESTRICTED SERVICES\\PrintSpoolerService, INTERACTIVE, Replicator, LOCAL SERVICE, CREATOR OWNER SERVER, DIALUP, WDAGUtilityAccount, RESTRICTED SERVICES\\ALL RESTRICTED SERVICES, ANONYMOUS LOGON, CREATOR OWNER, Performance Log Users\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","mitigations":"","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nAccounts with the \"Manage auditing and security log\" user right can manage the security log and change auditing configurations. This could be used to clear evidence of tampering.\n\nSatisfies: SRG-OS-000057-GPOS-00027, SRG-OS-000063-GPOS-00032","rule_title":"The \"Manage auditing and security log\" user right must only be assigned to the Administrators group.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_version":"WN11-UR-000130","ccis":["CCI-000162","CCI-000171"],"severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000057-GPOS-00027","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id":"SV-253501r958434","mitigation_control":"","rule_id_src":"SV-253501r958434_rule","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any groups or accounts other than the following are granted the \"Manage auditing and security log\" user right, this is a finding:\n\nAdministrators\n\nIf the organization has an \"Auditors\" group the assignment of this group to the user right would not be a finding.","ia_controls":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000057-GPOS-00027","id":"V-253501"},"reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0"},{"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","id":"V-253502"},"ia_controls":"","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any groups or accounts other than the following are granted the \"Modify firmware environment values\" user right, this is a finding:\n\nAdministrators","rule_id_src":"SV-253502r958726_rule","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-253502r958726","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-002235"],"rule_version":"WN11-UR-000140","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nAccounts with the \"Modify firmware environment values\" user right can change hardware configuration environment variables. This could result in hardware failures or a DoS.","mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"The \"Modify firmware environment values\" user right must only be assigned to the Administrators group.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Modify firmware environment values - Administrators)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25350200 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Modify firmware environment values - Administrators\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000009 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : Administrators\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'Administrators'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25350200 (accesst