priate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nAccounts with the \"Restore files and directories\" user right can circumvent file and directory permissions and could allow access to sensitive data. It could also be used to over-write more current data.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Restore files and directories - Administrators)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25350500 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Restore files and directories - Administrators\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000009 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : Administrators\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'Administrators'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25350500 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Restore files and directories\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'serestoreprivilege' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : serestoreprivilege equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : serestoreprivilege equals '0' for: BATCH, Distributed COM Users, Remote Management Users, NETWORK SERVICE, Hyper-V Administrators, Device Owners, NT SERVICE\\autotimesvc, Everyone, Visitor, Network Configuration Operators, PROXY, Authenticated Users, DefaultAccount, IUSR, User Mode Hardware Operators, SYSTEM, Event Log Readers, System Managed Accounts Group, Backup Operators, Remote Desktop Users, X_Admin, TERMINAL SERVER USER, Users, Performance Monitor Users, OpenSSH Users, IIS_IUSRS, CREATOR GROUP, SERVICE, Guests, Access Control Assistance Operators, NT SERVICE\\WdiServiceHost, NETWORK, WKS1-SOTERIA\\Degthat, ENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS, Window Manager\\Window Manager Group, Power Users, NT SERVICE\\ALL SERVICES, CREATOR GROUP SERVER, Cryptographic Operators, RESTRICTED SERVICES\\PrintSpoolerService, INTERACTIVE, Replicator, LOCAL SERVICE, CREATOR OWNER SERVER, DIALUP, WDAGUtilityAccount, RESTRICTED SERVICES\\ALL RESTRICTED SERVICES, ANONYMOUS LOGON, CREATOR OWNER, Performance Log Users\n","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"3676E27B-6BF8-1014-B341-ED52A7629A8B","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253505"},"group_id":"V-253505","potential_impacts":"","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253505","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; \"Restore files and directories\" to only include the following groups or accounts:\n\nAdministrators"},{"rule_version":"WN11-UR-000165","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125","ccis":["CCI-002235"],"rule_id_src":"SV-253506r958726_rule","check_content":"Verify the effective setting in Local Group Policy Editor.\nRun \"gpedit.msc\".\n\nNavigate to Local Computer Policy &gt;&gt; Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment.\n\nIf any groups or accounts other than the following are granted the \"Take ownership of files or other objects\" user right, this is a finding:\n\nAdministrators","ia_controls":"","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"rule_id":"SV-253506r958726","mitigation_control":"","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","group_tree":{"id":"V-253506","title":"SRG-OS-000324-GPOS-00125"},"reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","third_party_tools":"","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-253506","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-253506","fix_text":"Configure the policy value for Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Local Policies &gt;&gt; User Rights Assignment &gt;&gt; \"Take ownership of files or other objects\" to only include the following groups or accounts:\n\nAdministrators","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:253506"},"uuid":"3676EB19-6BF8-1014-83D1-9BB93E5990B5","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Take ownership of files or other objects - Administrators)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25350600 (accesstoken_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Take ownership of files or other objects - Administrators\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000009 (accesstoken_object)\nObject Comment          : Administrators\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\nExclude Items If        : security_principle equals (case insensitive) 'Administrators'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:25350600 (accesstoken_state)\nState Comment           : Take ownership of files or other objects\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'setakeownershipprivilege' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\nCollected Item Property : setakeownershipprivilege equals '1' for: &lt;no users or groups&gt;\nCollected Item Property : setakeownershipprivilege equals '0' for: BATCH, Distributed COM Users, Remote Management Users, NETWORK SERVICE, Hyper-V Administrators, Device Owners, NT SERVICE\\autotimesvc, Everyone, Visitor, Network Configuration Operators, PROXY, Authenticated Users, DefaultAccount, IUSR, User Mode Hardware Operators, SYSTEM, Event Log Readers, System Managed Accounts Group, Backup Operators, Remote Desktop Users, X_Admin, TERMINAL SERVER USER, Users, Performance Monitor Users, OpenSSH Users, IIS_IUSRS, CREATOR GROUP, SERVICE, Guests, Access Control Assistance Operators, NT SERVICE\\WdiServiceHost, NETWORK, WKS1-SOTERIA\\Degthat, ENTERPRISE DOMAIN CONTROLLERS, Window Manager\\Window Manager Group, Power Users, NT SERVICE\\ALL SERVICES, CREATOR GROUP SERVER, Cryptographic Operators, RESTRICTED SERVICES\\PrintSpoolerService, INTERACTIVE, Replicator, LOCAL SERVICE, CREATOR OWNER SERVER, DIALUP, WDAGUtilityAccount, RESTRICTED SERVICES\\ALL RESTRICTED SERVICES, ANONYMOUS LOGON, CREATOR OWNER, Performance Log Users\n","mitigations":"","discussion":"Inappropriate granting of user rights can provide system, administrative, and other high-level capabilities.\n\nAccounts with the \"Take ownership of files or other objects\" user right can take ownership of objects and make changes.","rule_title":"The \"Take ownership of files or other objects\" user right must only be assigned to the Administrators group.","security_override_guidance":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4"},{"rule_version":"WN11-CC-000391","group_title":"SRG-OS-000185-GPOS-00079","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"ia_controls":"","check_content":"Determine if IE11 is installed or enabled on Windows 11 semi-annual channel.\n\nIf IE11 is installed or not disabled on Windows 11 semi-annual channel, this is a finding.\n\nIf IE11 is installed on an unsupported operating system and is enabled or installed, this is a finding.\n\nFor more information, visit: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/lifecycle/faq/internet-explorer-microsoft-edge#what-is-the-lifecycle-policy-for-internet-explorer-","rule_id_src":"SV-256893r958552_rule","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-256893r958552","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","responsibility":"","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000185-GPOS-00079","id":"V-256893"},"group_id":"V-256893","potential_impacts":"","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-256893","fix_text":"For Windows 11 semi-annual channel, remove or disable the IE11 application. \n\nTo disable IE11 as a standalone browser:\n\nSet the policy value for \"Computer Configuration/Administrative Templates/Windows Components/Internet Explorer/Disable Internet Explorer 11 as a standalone browser\" to \"Enabled\" with the option value set to \"Never\".","status":"not_a_finding","uuid":"3676F280-6BF8-1014-A206-A1D18CA100CE","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:256893"},"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nCriteria                :     false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :       true (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nTest                    :         true (64-bit Microsoft Edge is installed) (negated)\nTest                    :         false (32-bit Microsoft Edge is installed) (negated)\nTest                    :       false (Internet Explorer 11 is disabled as a standalone browser)\nTest                    :     true (Internet Explorer 11 optional feature disabled or not installed)\nTest                    :     false (The OS is Windows Enterprise LTSC)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.edge:tst:100 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : 64-bit Microsoft Edge is installed\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.edge:obj:102 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : 64-bit DisplayName equals Microsoft Edge\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\nInclude Items If        : value equals 'Microsoft Edge'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : exists\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Wow6432Node\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Uninstall\\Microsoft Edge'\n                        : name equals 'DisplayName'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134331001020000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals 'Microsoft Edge'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.edge:tst:101 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : 32-bit Microsoft Edge is installed\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.edge:obj:103 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : 32-bit DisplayName equals Microsoft Edge\nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\nInclude Items If        : value equals 'Microsoft Edge'\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25689301 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Internet Explorer 11 is disabled as a standalone browser\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\nState Operator          : One or more item-state comparisons may be true.\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25689301 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\Internet Explorer\\Main'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'NotifyDisableIEOptions'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000002 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '2'\n\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:25689300 (wmi57_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Internet Explorer 11 optional feature disabled or not installed\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:25689300 (wmi57_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'namespace' must be equal to 'root\\cimv2'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'wql' must be equal to 'SELECT installstate FROM win32_optionalfeature WHERE name = 'Internet-Explorer-Optional-amd64''\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000020 (wmi57_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : for all 'result' the following must be true:\n                        : at least one installstate must be equal to '2'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : does not exist\n                        : namespace equals 'root\\cimv2'\n                        : wql equals 'SELECT installstate FROM win32_optionalfeature WHERE name = 'Internet-Explorer-Optional-amd64''\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:22070601 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : The OS is Windows Enterprise LTSC\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000017 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : EditionID\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'EditionId'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000018 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : EditionID = EnterpriseS (reg_sz)\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_sz'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to 'EnterpriseS'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Microsoft\\Windows NT\\CurrentVersion'\n                        : name equals 'EditionId'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330995370000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals 'Professional'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\n","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Internet Explorer must be disabled for Windows 11.","discussion":"Internet Explorer 11 (IE11) is not supported on Windows 11 semi-annual channel.","mitigations":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4"},{"false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-257592","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-257592","fix_text":"Contact the Administrator to run \"netsh interface portproxy delete\" with elevation. Remove any enabled portproxies that may be configured.","status":"not_a_finding","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:257592"},"uuid":"3676FA39-6BF8-1014-A52B-F7212AED8818","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     true (Windows 11 must not have portproxy enabled or in use.)\nTest                    :   true (Windows 11 must not have portproxy enabled or in use.)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25759202 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Windows 11 must not have portproxy enabled or in use.\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25759202 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Check registry for existence of v4tov4\\tcp\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\PortProxy\\v4tov4\\tcp'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:25759201 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Windows 11 must not have portproxy enabled or in use.\nCheck Existence         : No collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : Result is based on check existence only.\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:25759201 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Ensure no portproxies are configured.\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must match the pattern 'SYSTEM\\\\CurrentControlSet\\\\Services\\\\PortProxy\\\\v.tov.\\\\.*'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must match the pattern '.*'\n","discussion":"Having portproxy enabled or configured in Windows 10 could allow a man-in-the-middle attack.","mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows 11 must not have portproxy enabled or in use.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","rule_version":"WN11-00-000395","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"ia_controls":"","check_content":"Check the registry key for existence of proxied ports:\nHKLM\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\PortProxy\\.\n\nIf the key contains v4tov4\\tcp\\ or is populated v4tov4\\tcp\\, this is a finding.\n\nRun \"netsh interface portproxy show all\".\n\nIf the command displays any results, this is a finding.","rule_id_