fails to start and the name of the program or user that created it.\n\nThese audit events can assist in understanding how a computer is being used and tracking user activity.","mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows 11 must have command line process auditing events enabled for failures.","fix_text":"Go to Computer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt;Security Settings&gt;&gt; Advanced Audit Policy Configuration &gt;&gt; System Audit Policies &gt;&gt; Detailed Tracking &gt;&gt; Set \"Audit Process Creation\" to \"Failure\".","group_id_src":"V-257770","legacy_ids":[],"false_positives":"","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-257770","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:257770"},"uuid":"36770136-6BF8-1014-9A25-EF3F86EA3267","status":"open","classification":"Unclassified","comments":null,"mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-257770r958412","check_content":"Ensure Audit Process Creation auditing has been enabled: \n\nComputer Configuration &gt;&gt; Windows Settings &gt;&gt; Security Settings &gt;&gt; Advanced Audit Policy Configuration &gt;&gt; System Audit Policy &gt;&gt; Detailed Tracking &gt;&gt; Audit Process Creation. \n\nIf \"Audit Process Creation\" is not set to \"Failure\", this is a finding.","ia_controls":"","rule_id_src":"SV-257770r958412_rule","reference_identifier":"5471","third_party_tools":"","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-257770","title":"SRG-OS-000037-GPOS-00015"},"weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","rule_version":"WN11-AU-000585","ccis":["CCI-002234"],"group_title":"SRG-OS-000037-GPOS-00015","severity":"medium"},{"stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","mitigations":"","discussion":"Some features may communicate with the vendor, sending system information or downloading data or components for the feature. Turning off this capability will prevent potentially sensitive information from being sent outside the enterprise and uncontrolled updates to the system.","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Copilot must be disabled for Windows 11.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Run a PowerShell command to determine if copilot is in use. If Microsoft.Copilot displays, this is a finding.)\nResult Analysis         :        Collected Item did not meet the state requirement.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:tst:26831701 (shellcommand_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Run a PowerShell command to determine if copilot is in use. If Microsoft.Copilot displays, this is a finding.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:obj:26831701 (shellcommand_object)\nObject Comment          : Get-AppxPackage\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'shell' must be equal to 'powershell'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'command' must be equal to 'Get-AppxPackage -AllUsers | Where-Object { $_.Name -like '*Copilot*' }'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:ste:26831701 (shellcommand_state)\nState Comment           : stdout_line does not exist\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : shell equals 'powershell'\n                        : command equals 'Get-AppxPackage -AllUsers | Where-Object { $_.Name -like '*Copilot*' }'\n                        : pattern equals ''\n                        : exit_status equals ''\n                        : stdout_line equals ''\n                        : stdout_line equals ''\n                        : stdout_line equals 'Name              :