ystem is not being managed by GPO, ask the administrator to indicate which MDM is managing the device.\n\nFrom PowerShell: Get-Service -Name \"IntuneManagementExtension\"\n\nIf the Windows 11 system is not receiving policy from either group Policy or an MDM, this is a finding.\n\nThis is NA for standalone, nondomain-joined systems.","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","rule_id":"SV-268318r1135322","mitigation_control":"","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-OS-000480-GPOS-00227","ccis":["CCI-000366"],"rule_version":"WN11-CC-000063","mitigations":"","discussion":"Without Windows 11 systems being managed, devices could be rogue and become targets of an attacker.","rule_title":"Windows 11 systems must use either Group Policy or an approved Mobile Device Management (MDM) product to enforce STIG compliance.","security_override_guidance":"","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: notapplicableRule Result             : Not Applicable\n","status":"not_applicable","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.windows:def:268318"},"uuid":"367715C9-6BF8-1014-B8AE-A7872A21530C","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-268318","group_id":"V-268318","potential_impacts":"","fix_text":"Configure the Windows 11 system to use either Group Policy or an approved MDM product to enforce STIG compliance."},{"stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","rule_title":"Windows 11 must be configured to audit file system failures.","security_override_guidance":"","discussion":"Maintaining an audit trail of system activity logs can help identify configuration errors, troubleshoot service disruptions, and analyze compromises that have occurred, as well as detect attacks. Audit logs are necessary to provide a trail of evidence in case the system or network is compromised. Collecting this data is essential for analyzing the security of information assets and detecting signs of suspicious and unexpected behavior. Credential validation records events related to validation tests on credentials for a user account logon.","mitigations":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   false (One or more child tests must be true. (OR))\nTest                    :     false ('Audit File System' is set to 'Failure')\nResult Analysis         :          file_system = 'AUDIT_NONE' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'AUDIT_FAILURE' \nTest                    :     false ('Audit File System' is set to 'Success' and 'Failure')\nResult Analysis         :          file_system = 'AUDIT_NONE' failed test of 'equals' compared to 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:27894200 (auditeventpolicysubcategories_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : 'Audit File System' is set to 'Failure'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:20000000 (auditeventpolicysubcategories_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      : Collect any available items.\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:27894200 (auditeventpolicysubcategories_state)\nState Comment           : 'File System' is set to 'Failure'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'file_system' must be equal to 'AUDIT_FAILURE'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : credential_validation equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n                        : kerberos_authentication_service equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n        