         : central_access_policy_staging equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : audit_policy_change equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : authentication_policy_change equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : authorization_policy_change equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : filtering_platform_policy_change equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : mpssvc_rule_level_policy_change equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n                        : other_policy_change_events equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n                        : non_sensitive_privilege_use equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : other_privilege_use_events equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : sensitive_privilege_use equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n                        : ipsec_driver equals 'AUDIT_FAILURE'\n                        : other_system_events equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n                        : security_state_change equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : security_system_extension equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : system_integrity equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS_FAILURE'\n                        : group_membership equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : pnp_activity equals 'AUDIT_SUCCESS'\n                        : user_device_claims equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n                        : audit_detailedtracking_tokenrightadjusted equals 'AUDIT_NONE'\n","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","discussion":"Maintaining an audit trail of system activity logs can help identify configuration errors, troubleshoot service disruptions, and analyze compromises that have occurred, as well as detect attacks. Audit logs are necessary to provide a trail of evidence in case the system or network is compromised. Collecting this data is essential for analyzing the security of information assets and detecting signs of suspicious and unexpected behavior. Credential validation records events related to validation tests on credentials for a user account logon.","mitigations":"","rule_title":"Windows 11 must be configured to audit sensitive privilege use failures.","security_override_guidance":""},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T13:03:20\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nCriteria                :   false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :     false ('Prevent enabling lock screen camera' is set to 'Enabled')\nResult Analysis         :          Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\MicrosoftAccount\\DisableUserAuth'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:tst:27968800 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : 'Prevent enabling lock screen camera' is set to 'Enabled'\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:obj:27968800 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\MicrosoftAccount'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisableUserAuth'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.win:ste:20000001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\MicrosoftAccount\\DisableUserAuth'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n","discussion":"It is detrimental for operating systems to provide, or install by default, functionality exceeding requirements or mission objectives. These unnecessary capabilities or services are often overlooked and therefore, may remain unsecured. They increase the risk to the platform by providing additional attack vectors.\n\nOperating systems are capable of providing a wide variety of functions and services. Some of the functions and services, provided by default, may not be necessary to support essential organizational operations (e.g., key missions, functions).\n\nThe Copilot Rewrite functionality within Notepad and Image Generation within Paint is dependent upon the use of AI credits from a Microsoft 365 Personal or Family subscription. Organizational users must not use personal accounts to login to applications on enterprise machines.","mitigations":"","security_override_guidance":"","rule_title":"Windows 11 systems must block consumer account user authentication.","stig_uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","false_positives":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_id_src":"V-279688","potential_impacts":"","group_id":"V-279688","fix_text":"Configure the following Group Policy:\nComputer Configuration &gt;&gt; Administrative Templates &gt;&gt; Windows Components &gt;&gt; Microsoft Account \"block all consumer Microsoft account user authentication\" to \"Enabled\".\n\nFor systems managed by Intune, apply the DOD Windows 11 STIG Settings Catalog (or equivalent Intune policy) found in the Intune policy package available on cyber.mil.\nSteps to create an Intune policy:\n1. Sign in to the Intune admin center &gt;&gt; Devices &gt;&gt; Configuration &gt;&gt; Create &gt;&gt; New Policy.\n2. Platform: Windows 10 and later. Profile type: Settings Catalog, then click \"Create\".\n3. Basics: Provide a Name and Description of the profile, then click \"Next\".\n4. Configuration settings: Click \"+ Add settings\" and search for consumer under the Settings picker. Under the Administrative Templates\\Windows Components\\Microsoft account category, check the box next to \"Block all consumer Microsoft account user authentication\". Click the Enabled radio button, then click \"Next\".\n5. Scope tags: (optional), then click \"Next\".\n6. Assignments: Assign the policy to Entra security groups that contain the target users or devices, then click \"Next\".\n7. Review + create: Review the deployment summary, then click \"Create\".","status":"open","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.windows11:def:279688","href":"U_MS_Windows_11_V2R8_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV17-oval.xml"},"uuid":"36775D68-6BF8-1014-AFD9-89BB4CF5308B","ia_controls":"","check_content":"Verify the \"block all consumer Microsoft account user authentication\" is enabled.\n\nRegistry Hive: HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\nRegistry Path: \\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Microsoft\\MicrosoftAccount\n\nValue Name: DisableUserAuth\n\nValue Type: REG_DWORD\nValue: 0x00000001 (1)\n\nIf the registry value is not \"1\", this is a finding.","rule_id_src":"SV-279688r1153564_rule","comments":null,"classification":"Unclassified","mitigation_control":"","rule_id":"SV-279688r1153564","weight":"10.0","documentable":"false","third_party_tools":"","reference_identifier":"5471","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","id":"V-279688"},"rule_version":"WN11-00-000126","group_title":"SRG-OS-000095-GPOS-00049","severity":"medium","ccis":["CCI-000381"]}],"version":"2","stig_id":"Microsoft_Windows_11_STIG","release_info":"Release: 7 Benchmark Date: 01 Apr 2026","display_name":"Microsoft Windows 11","stig_name":"Microsoft Windows 11 Security Technical Implementation Guide","uuid":"3637ABFC-6BF8-1014-A5BB-C980152CC4B4","size":262,"reference_identifier":"5471"}],"cklb_version":"1.0","target_data":{"mac_address":"00:0C:29:03:21:20","host_name":"WKS1-SOTERIA","fqdn":"WKS1-SOTERIA.","target_type":"Computing","ip_address":"192.168.40.91","role":"Workstation"}}